<usx version="3.1">
  <book code="PSA" style="id">EN_UST en_English_ltr Mon Oct 09 2023 16:41:17 GMT-0500 (Central Daylight Time) tc</book>
  <para style="ide">UTF-8
</para>
  <para style="h">Psalms
</para>
  <para style="toc1">The Book of Psalms
</para>
  <para style="toc2">Psalms
</para>
  <para style="toc3">Psa
</para>
  <para style="mt1">Psalms
</para>
  <para style="cl">Psalm

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="PSA 1"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book One
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 1:1"/>The person who will have a truly good life
</para>
  <para style="q2">is the person who does not do what evil people tell him to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who does not imitate sinful people’s behavior,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who does not become like people who enjoy mocking.
<verse eid="PSA 1:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 1:2"/>Instead, he delights in what Yahweh teaches,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he thoughtfully reads it aloud every day and every night.
<verse eid="PSA 1:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 1:3"/>Like having plenty of water causes a well-cultivated tree
</para>
  <para style="q2">to produce fruit at the right time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and keeps it from dying,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so {his faithfulness to Yahweh} causes everything this person does to prosper.

<verse eid="PSA 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 1:4"/>That is not what wicked people are like!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Instead, they are like chaff that the wind blows away.
<verse eid="PSA 1:4"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 1:5"/>Just so, wicked people will not be able to endure {when Yahweh} judges {the world}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Neither will sinful people {be present when Yahweh} gathers all the righteous people together.

<verse eid="PSA 1:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 1:6"/>{All of this is} because Yahweh cares for righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but wicked people keep sinning until {Yahweh} destroys them {forever}.


<verse eid="PSA 1:6"/><verse eid="PSA 1:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 1"/>
  <chapter number="2" style="c" sid="PSA 2"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 2:1"/>Foreign kingdoms are scheming,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people groups are planning, but it is useless.
<verse eid="PSA 2:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 2:2"/>Earthly kings prepare to revolt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the rulers plot together to fight
</para>
  <para style="q2">against Yahweh and against his chosen king.
<verse eid="PSA 2:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 2:3"/>{They shout,} “We should break free from the shackles {that they control us with}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We should throw aside the ropes {that they rule over us with}!”

<verse eid="PSA 2:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 2:4"/>But the heavenly ruler sneers at them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Lord ridicules those rulers.
<verse eid="PSA 2:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 2:5"/>Then he speaks to them angrily.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He terrifies them by {showing them how} furious he is.
<verse eid="PSA 2:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 2:6"/>{Yahweh says,} “It is I who has made my king rule in Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{which is} my sacred hill.”

<verse eid="PSA 2:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 2:7"/>{Yahweh’s king says,} “I will proclaim what Yahweh has decreed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh said to me, ‘You are my son;
</para>
  <para style="q2">today I have become your father.
<verse eid="PSA 2:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 2:8"/>Request {this from} me:
</para>
  <para style="q2">{ask to} inherit the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{ask to} own the {whole} earth {even the} farthest parts.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will give them to you.
<verse eid="PSA 2:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 2:9"/>You will strike them with an iron rod
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will shatter into small pieces as if they were a clay pot.’”

<verse eid="PSA 2:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 2:10"/>So then, you kings should act wisely!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All rulers on the earth should allow Yahweh and his king to correct them!
<verse eid="PSA 2:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 2:11"/>Worship Yahweh respectfully.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be joyful and afraid {while you are worshiping him}!
<verse eid="PSA 2:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 2:12"/>Swear to be truly loyal to his son
</para>
  <para style="q2">otherwise, he may become angry
</para>
  <para style="q2">and suddenly kill you
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he can become angry quickly.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But all those who ask him to protect them will have a life that is truly good.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 2:12"/><verse eid="PSA 2:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 2"/>
  <chapter number="3" style="c" sid="PSA 3"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">David wrote this psalm when he was fleeing from his son Absalom.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 3:1"/>Yahweh, I have so many enemies!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Many people are deciding to oppose me.
<verse eid="PSA 3:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 3:2"/>Many people are saying about me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“God will not rescue him.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 3:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 3:3"/>But Yahweh, you are like a shield that protects me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You greatly honor me, and you encourage me.
<verse eid="PSA 3:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 3:4"/>Whenever I cry loudly to Yahweh {for help},
</para>
  <para style="q2">he {comes} from {Zion,} his sacred hill, to help me.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 3:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 3:5"/>I {can} lie down and sleep, {knowing that} I {will} wake up
</para>
  <para style="q2">because Yahweh guards me {all night}.
<verse eid="PSA 3:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 3:6"/>There may be thousands {of enemy soldiers} who surround me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I am not afraid.

<verse eid="PSA 3:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 3:7"/>Yahweh, get up!
</para>
  <para style="q2">My God, rescue me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You can {insultingly} slap my enemies on their cheeks,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and destroy those wicked people’s {power like breaking animals’} teeth,
<verse eid="PSA 3:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 3:8"/>Yahweh rescues!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Bless your people!
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 3:8"/><verse eid="PSA 3:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 3"/>
  <chapter number="4" style="c" sid="PSA 4"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this psalm to be accompanied by people playing stringed instruments.

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 4:1"/>Righteous God, respond to me when I pray to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You who have {always} rescued me when I was distressed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">act mercifully toward me and pay attention to what I pray.

<verse eid="PSA 4:1"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 4:2"/>How long will you mortal people dishonor me instead of honoring me?
</para>
  <para style="q2">How long will you love what is useless, and chase lies?
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 4:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 4:3"/>You all should know that Yahweh treats people who are faithful to him as special to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh will pay attention when I pray to him.
<verse eid="PSA 4:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 4:4"/>You should be afraid of Yahweh, and {because of that} stop sinning!
</para>
  <para style="q1">While you lie on your bed, examine what you are thinking and stop accusing {me}.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 4:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 4:5"/>Instead, offer to Yahweh the proper sacrifices
</para>
  <para style="q2">and continually trust him.

<verse eid="PSA 4:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 4:6"/>Many people are wishing for something good to happen.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, please do good things for us!
<verse eid="PSA 4:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 4:7"/>You have made me very joyful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">even more than {these complainers are} when they have plenty of food and drink.
<verse eid="PSA 4:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 4:8"/>I can lie down at night and sleep without worrying
</para>
  <para style="q2">because {I know that} it is only you, Yahweh, who keeps me safe.


<verse eid="PSA 4:8"/><verse eid="PSA 4:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 4"/>
  <chapter number="5" style="c" sid="PSA 5"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this psalm to be accompanied by people playing flutes.

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 5:1"/>Yahweh, listen to what I say!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Comprehend my distressed sigh.
<verse eid="PSA 5:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 5:2"/>{Since} you are my king and my God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">hear and respond when I plead aloud for rescuing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am praying to you {only}.

<verse eid="PSA 5:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 5:3"/>Yahweh, you will hear me pleading each morning.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Every morning I will request that you save me, and I will wait for you to do it.
<verse eid="PSA 5:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 5:4"/>You are a God who certainly does not approve of wicked people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">evil-doers never stay as your guests.
<verse eid="PSA 5:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 5:5"/>Boasters are not allowed to come worship you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You hate everyone who does evil things.
<verse eid="PSA 5:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 5:6"/>You kill liars.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh despises murderers and people who deceive others.
<verse eid="PSA 5:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 5:7"/>As for me, I will come {worship you} where you live, because you faithfully love us so abundantly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will reverently kneel to worship you at your sacred temple.

<verse eid="PSA 5:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 5:8"/>Yahweh, my enemies are watching me {to try to catch me doing something wrong}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please show me how to do what is right, just as you always do what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make it easy for me to live obediently to you.
<verse eid="PSA 5:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 5:9"/>Please do this because my enemies are untrustworthy;
</para>
  <para style="q2">one of their strongest desires is to destroy people.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They speak things that are vile like the smell of an open grave.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They flatter people {to trap and destroy them}.
<verse eid="PSA 5:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 5:10"/>O God, declare that they are guilty and punish them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Cause to happen to them the harmful events that they plan to cause to happen to others.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Get rid of them because they have sinned often,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and rebelled against you.
<verse eid="PSA 5:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 5:11"/>But enable all the people who ask you to protect them to be glad;
</para>
  <para style="q2">enable them to sing gladly always.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Please protect them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Enable everyone who loves it when you are famous to praise you.

<verse eid="PSA 5:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 5:12"/>{I ask this} because Yahweh, you always bless those who act righteously;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you protect them as if your good acts are like a shield around them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 5:12"/><verse eid="PSA 5:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 5"/>
  <chapter number="6" style="c" sid="PSA 6"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Musicians playing stringed instruments should accompany this song. Perform it in a low range. David wrote this psalm.

</para>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 6:1"/>Yahweh, do not correct me angrily,
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not punish me wrathfully.
<verse eid="PSA 6:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 6:2"/>Yahweh, act kindly toward me because I have become weak.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, heal me because my body shakes fearfully.
<verse eid="PSA 6:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 6:3"/>Yahweh, I am greatly troubled in my inner being.
</para>
  <para style="q2">How long must I endure this?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 6:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 6:4"/>Yahweh, relent from your anger and deliver me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Help me because you always do what you promise!
<verse eid="PSA 6:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 6:5"/>{Do this} because {I and} no one {else} who is dead can honor you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I and} no one {else} can praise you {if we are} in the place where the dead are.

<verse eid="PSA 6:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 6:6"/>I am exhausted because of my pain.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I cry all night long, so that my tears soak
</para>
  <para style="q2">and seem as if they will wash away my bed and my cushions.
<verse eid="PSA 6:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 6:7"/>I am very sad and {I cry so much that} I cannot see well.
</para>
  <para style="q2">My vision has become weak from {crying because of} all my enemies.

<verse eid="PSA 6:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 6:8"/>{I advise} all you people who do evil things to get away from me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because Yahweh heard me when I was crying;
<verse eid="PSA 6:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 6:9"/>he heard me when I called out for him to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will answer my prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 6:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 6:10"/>{When that happens,} all my enemies will be ashamed and very troubled.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will relent {from attacking me because they will} suddenly {be} ashamed.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 6:10"/><verse eid="PSA 6:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 6"/>
  <chapter number="7" style="c" sid="PSA 7"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm that David sang to Yahweh because of a Benjamite named Cush.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 7:1"/>Yahweh my God, I have come to you so that you can protect me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save me from everyone who is chasing me {in order to harm me}. Rescue me!
<verse eid="PSA 7:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 7:2"/>If you do not do that, they will maul me like a lion {does when it attacks the animals it wants to kill};
</para>
  <para style="q2">they shred me and there is not a rescuer.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 7:3"/>My God Yahweh, suppose that I have done these things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I am really guilty.
<verse eid="PSA 7:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 7:4"/>Suppose that I have harmed my ally,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{maybe} I {was unfaithful to my ally and instead} rescued an enemy for no reason.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 7:5"/>Then allow my enemies to chase and capture me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Allow them to stomp me into the ground
</para>
  <para style="q2">and leave me lying {dead} in the dirt.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 7:6"/>Get up Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you are angry, show that you are greater than what my furious enemies can do!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be alert so you can rescue me by doing what you have said is just!
<verse eid="PSA 7:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 7:7"/>The people of all nations gather around you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">return to ruling over them all!
<verse eid="PSA 7:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 7:8"/>Yahweh, judge the people of all nations!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Decide favorably for me, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am righteous and honorable {before you the} highest judge.
<verse eid="PSA 7:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 7:9"/>God, you are righteous and look closely at what people think and want.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Please stop evil people from doing wicked things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make {all of us} who are righteous secure!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 7:10"/>God, you protect me as a shield protects soldiers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you rescue all those who are righteous in their inner being.
<verse eid="PSA 7:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 7:11"/>God judges everyone correctly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God condemns {the wicked} constantly.
<verse eid="PSA 7:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 7:12"/>Whenever the wicked do not repent, it is as though God sharpens his sword
</para>
  <para style="q2">and puts a string on his bow {to get ready to kill them}.
<verse eid="PSA 7:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 7:13"/>He prepares his deadly weapons to kill {the wicked},
</para>
  <para style="q2">he makes his arrows have flaming tips.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 7:14"/>Look at the wicked person who is filled with evil intentions, as though pregnant with them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who plans to trouble people like conceiving a child,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who lies as naturally as giving birth.
<verse eid="PSA 7:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 7:15"/>If he digs a deep pit to trap others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will fall into his own trap.
<verse eid="PSA 7:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 7:16"/>He experiences the bad things that he wants to cause to others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he hurts himself by the violent things that he wants to do to others.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 7:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 7:17"/>I thank Yahweh because he always acts justly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I sing to praise Yahweh, who is the highest judge, and to make him famous.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 7:17"/><verse eid="PSA 7:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 7"/>
  <chapter number="8" style="c" sid="PSA 8"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Accompany the song with a stringed instrument. David wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 8:1"/>Our Lord Yahweh, people all over the world know how impressive you are!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have made the sky show {everyone} how grand you are {every time anyone looks at it}!
<verse eid="PSA 8:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 8:2"/>When {anyone who is weak cries for help like} nursing little children cry {for help},
</para>
  <para style="q2">you {listen and} protect them from your enemies, {the ones that want to hurt your people}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In order to protect them, you destroy enemies who want to harm them in return {for what you have justly done to them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 8:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 8:3"/>I look up at the sky {at night}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and see the things that you have made—
</para>
  <para style="q2">the moon and the stars that you have set in place.
<verse eid="PSA 8:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 8:4"/>It is amazing to me that you think about people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that you are concerned about humans!
<verse eid="PSA 8:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 8:5"/>In fact though, you made humans to be just slightly lower than heavenly beings.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You made humans to be glorious and majestic {like you}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 8:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 8:6"/>You put humans in charge of everything that you made,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you made them rule over all things—
<verse eid="PSA 8:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 8:7"/>{over} all {the domestic animals like} sheep, goats, and cattle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the wild animals too,
<verse eid="PSA 8:7"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 8:8"/>the birds in the sky,
</para>
  <para style="q3">the fish in the sea,
</para>
  <para style="q3">and everything else that swims in the ocean.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 8:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 8:9"/>Our Lord Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">people all over the world know how impressive you are!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 8:9"/><verse eid="PSA 8:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 8"/>
  <chapter number="9" style="c" sid="PSA 9"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: David wrote this song to the tune of “The Death of the Son.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 9:1"/>Yahweh, I will praise you with all of my inner being.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will tell others about all the wonderful things that you have done.
<verse eid="PSA 9:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 9:2"/>You make me extremely happy, so I will sing to celebrate what you, who are much greater than all other spirit beings, have done.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 9:3"/>When my foes flee {from your righteous anger},
</para>
  <para style="q2">they trip and fall. You kill them just by being near them.
<verse eid="PSA 9:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 9:4"/>{You are angry because} you have found my legal case to be righteous {and my enemies’ to be wicked}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You sit on a throne {like a king} judging {everything} rightly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 9:5"/>You reprimanded the people from other nations, and killed the wicked people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you eradicate them so thoroughly no one will ever remember their names.
<verse eid="PSA 9:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 9:6"/>Nothing remains of our enemies except the ruins
</para>
  <para style="q2">of their cities which you permanently destroyed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one even remembers those enemies anymore.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 9:7"/>But Yahweh rules forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is prepared to judge from his throne.
<verse eid="PSA 9:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 9:8"/>He will judge all the people in the world justly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will be fair when he judges the people of every nation.
<verse eid="PSA 9:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 9:9"/>Let Yahweh be like a fortress for those whom oppressors oppress;
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a strong fort for them when they have trouble.
<verse eid="PSA 9:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 9:10"/>Those who know your reputation should trust you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you, Yahweh, never abandon those who come to you {for help}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 9:11"/>Yahweh rules on Mount Zion;
</para>
  <para style="q2">praise him by singing to him!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Tell people from every nation the marvelous things that he has done.
<verse eid="PSA 9:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 9:12"/>Do this because Yahweh always remembers to repay any person who murders another person.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When someone’s enemy has oppressed him, and when that person calls to Yahweh to help him, Yahweh does not forget to avenge him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 9:13"/>Yahweh, act mercifully toward me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You who rescue me when I am almost dead, look at the ways that my enemies have oppressed me.
<verse eid="PSA 9:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 9:14"/>{I want to live} in order to tell all your people at the entrance to Jerusalem all the reasons to praise you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to rejoice because you rescued me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 9:15"/>{When you rescue me} it is like wicked people of many nations had dug a pit for me to fall into,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but have fallen into that same pit,
</para>
  <para style="q1">or like they hid a net to catch me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but their feet have been caught in that same net.
<verse eid="PSA 9:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 9:16"/>So you allow the traps that wicked people make to trap them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because of that, people can discover that you, Yahweh, are just.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Higgaion Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 9:17"/>Wicked people will flee {from you} back to the place where dead people stay.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{There are people there} from every nation, people who have forgotten {to worship the true} God.
<verse eid="PSA 9:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 9:18"/>This all happens because there is a certain time when God will remember {to take care of} poor people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is good for oppressed people to expect him to rescue them because he will do it one day.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 9:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 9:19"/>Yahweh, do something! Do not let {evil} people win!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Bring them} to your court and judge them!
<verse eid="PSA 9:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 9:20"/>Yahweh, teach them that they must be afraid of you and honor you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Cause {the rulers of} nations to know that they are mortal.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 9:20"/><verse eid="PSA 9:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 9"/>
  <chapter number="10" style="c" sid="PSA 10"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 10:1"/>Yahweh, please do not stay far away from us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please let us find you when enemies threaten us.
<verse eid="PSA 10:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 10:2"/>Wicked people proudly chase people until they can oppress them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, please make the bad things they plan to do to others happen to them instead.
<verse eid="PSA 10:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 10:3"/>A wicked person even brags about what he strongly wants to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He praises people who unjustly take things from other people. He curses Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 10:4"/>The wicked person is so proud that he does not care {about God}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He plans {to do evil things} as if there was no God.
<verse eid="PSA 10:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 10:5"/>What he does always prospers.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He ignores doing what you say is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He makes a mocking noise at all his enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 10:6"/>He thinks, “Nothing bad can happen to me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">As long as I live, nothing will trouble me.”
<verse eid="PSA 10:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 10:7"/>He constantly curses, lies, and threatens others.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is always talking about harming others and doing wrong.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 10:8"/>He hides outside villages to surprise attack people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From his secret spot he kills people who have done nothing wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From there he sneakily watches for some unlucky person.
<verse eid="PSA 10:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 10:9"/>He hides in a secret spot like a lion, {crouching} in the bushes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">waiting for people to catch and oppress.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He catches people and drags them away in a net to oppress them.
<verse eid="PSA 10:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 10:10"/>The wicked person makes sure everything is properly prepared
</para>
  <para style="q2">so he can oppress his unlucky victim.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 10:11"/>He convinces himself, “God is not recording what I do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is not paying attention; he will never notice.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 10:12"/>Do something, Yahweh! Prove that you are powerful, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Pay attention to oppressed people!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 10:13"/>Do not let wicked people curse you, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not let him believe that you do not care about his evil deeds!
<verse eid="PSA 10:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 10:14"/>Surely you see everything! You pay attention to how wicked people hurt and frustrate other people so that you can punish those wicked people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Unlucky people trust that you will protect them. You help orphans.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 10:15"/>Cause people who are always doing very evil things to become powerless!
</para>
  <para style="q2">When someone tries to oppress other people may he discover he cannot do it.
<verse eid="PSA 10:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 10:16"/>Yahweh reigns eternally!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Foreign people no longer occupy his land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 10:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 10:17"/>Yahweh, when oppressed people ask you to help, you listen
</para>
  <para style="q2">and encourage them. You pay close attention,
<verse eid="PSA 10:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 10:18"/>so you can act justly for the orphans and oppressed people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will stop any mere human from ever terrifying them again.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 10:18"/><verse eid="PSA 10:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 10"/>
  <chapter number="11" style="c" sid="PSA 11"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 11:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I trust that Yahweh will protect me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">So do not say to me, “You need to escape to the mountains like birds do,
<verse eid="PSA 11:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 11:2"/>because wicked people have hidden in the darkness.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They have pulled back their bowstrings and aimed their arrows
</para>
  <para style="q2">to shoot them at godly people {like you}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 11:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 11:3"/>When people are not punished for doing wrong things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is nothing righteous people can do.”
<verse eid="PSA 11:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 11:4"/>But Yahweh is in his holy sanctuary, he reigns from heaven,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he watches and examines {everything that} people do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 11:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 11:5"/>Yahweh examines what righteous people do and what wicked people do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he hates those who love to do violent things.
<verse eid="PSA 11:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 11:6"/>May he send down from the sky traps upon the wicked,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and may Yahweh punish them with fire and burning sulfur and scorching hot winds.
<verse eid="PSA 11:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 11:7"/>Yahweh is completely righteous, and he loves when people do what is righteous.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People who do what is right will be able to come into his presence.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 11:7"/><verse eid="PSA 11:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 11"/>
  <chapter number="12" style="c" sid="PSA 12"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song. Perform it in a low range.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 12:1"/>Yahweh, help us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{It seems like} people who honor you are no more.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 12:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 12:2"/>Everyone tells lies to other people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they deceive others by saying good things about them that they know are not true and by speaking insincerely.
<verse eid="PSA 12:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 12:3"/>Yahweh, we wish that you would cut off their tongues
</para>
  <para style="q2">{so that} they cannot continue to boast.
<verse eid="PSA 12:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 12:4"/>They say, “By speaking untruthfully we will get what we want;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we control what we say, no one can tell us what we should do!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 12:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 12:5"/>{But} Yahweh replies, “I have seen the oppressive things that they have done to helpless people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have heard those people groaning,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will take action and rescue the people who are wanting someone to help them.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 12:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 12:6"/>Yahweh, what you say is morally pure and you always do what you have said you will do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your words are {as precious and pure as} silver
</para>
  <para style="q2">that has been heated seven times in a furnace {to get rid of all the impure material}.
<verse eid="PSA 12:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 12:7"/>Yahweh, we know that you will continually protect us who honor you
</para>
  <para style="q2">from those wicked people.
<verse eid="PSA 12:7"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 12:8"/>When people praise wicked actions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">wicked people strut around {proudly}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 12:8"/><verse eid="PSA 12:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 12"/>
  <chapter number="13" style="c" sid="PSA 13"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 13:1"/>Yahweh, how long will you continue to not answer me?
</para>
  <para style="q2">How long will you hide yourself from me?
<verse eid="PSA 13:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 13:2"/>How long must I think about my problems within myself?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Must I be miserable every day?
</para>
  <para style="q2">How long will my enemy defeat me?

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 13:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 13:3"/>Yahweh, my God, pay attention to me and respond to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Restore my strength by giving me what I have hoped for, or I will die
<verse eid="PSA 13:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 13:4"/>and then my enemy would say, “I have defeated him,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">and those who are against me would celebrate when they had defeated me.
<verse eid="PSA 13:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 13:5"/>But I trust that you will faithfully love me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may I rejoice when you rescue me.
<verse eid="PSA 13:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 13:6"/>Yahweh will do good things for me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will sing to him.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 13:6"/><verse eid="PSA 13:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 13"/>
  <chapter number="14" style="c" sid="PSA 14"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 14:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{Only} foolish people say to themselves, “There is no God!”
</para>
  <para style="q1">People who say those things do corrupt deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they do detestable deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q1">hardly anyone does what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 14:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 14:2"/>Yahweh looks down from heaven and sees humans;
</para>
  <para style="q1">{he looks} to see if there are any wise people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{with the result that they are} wise enough that they desire to know him.
<verse eid="PSA 14:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 14:3"/>But they all do evil and corrupt things;
</para>
  <para style="q1">no one does what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 14:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 14:4"/>All the people who make a practice of doing wicked things do not take seriously the fact that Yahweh is going to punish them!
</para>
  <para style="q1">They act violently toward Yahweh’s people and want to consume them like they consume bread.
</para>
  <para style="q1">These evil people never pray to Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 14:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 14:5"/>{But in the future,} at the place God will judge wicked people, they will become very terrified
</para>
  <para style="q1">because God will help those who act righteously.
<verse eid="PSA 14:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 14:6"/>You evil people try to humiliate poor people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but Yahweh will protect them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 14:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 14:7"/>I wish that Yahweh would come from where he dwells in Jerusalem and rescue us Israelite people!
</para>
  <para style="q1">When Yahweh blesses us, his people again,
</para>
  <para style="q1">then all of us Israelite people will rejoice.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 14:7"/><verse eid="PSA 14:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 14"/>
  <chapter number="15" style="c" sid="PSA 15"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 15:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, who is allowed to enter your sacred tent?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Who is allowed to live on your sacred mountain?
<verse eid="PSA 15:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 15:2"/>Those whose behavior is faultless
</para>
  <para style="q1">and who do righteous things,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and who speak the truth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 15:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 15:3"/>They do not slander others.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They do not do to others things that are wrong,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they do not say bad things about their friends.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 15:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 15:4"/>They despise the people God abhors,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they respect those who revere Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They do what they have promised to do,
</para>
  <para style="q1">even if it causes them trouble to do that.
<verse eid="PSA 15:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 15:5"/>They lend money to others without charging interest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they never accept bribes in order to lie about people who have not done anything wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those who do those things will always live in safety.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 15:5"/><verse eid="PSA 15:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 15"/>
  <chapter number="16" style="c" sid="PSA 16"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 16:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God, protect me, because I go to you to keep me safe!
<verse eid="PSA 16:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 16:2"/>I said to Yahweh, “You are my Lord;
</para>
  <para style="q1">all the good things that I have come from you.”
<verse eid="PSA 16:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 16:3"/>People who try to live holy lives, they are wonderful;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I greatly delight in them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 16:4"/>Those who choose to worship other gods will have many things that cause them to be sad.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not join them when they make sacrifices {to their gods},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will not join them in speaking the names of their gods.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 16:5"/>Yahweh, you have granted to me that I would belong to you, and you supply all of my needs.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You control what happens to me.
<verse eid="PSA 16:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 16:6"/>Yahweh has greatly blessed me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am delighted with all the things that he has given me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 16:7"/>I will praise Yahweh, the one who teaches me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">even during the night he puts in my mind the right things for me to do.
<verse eid="PSA 16:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 16:8"/>I have chosen to always think about Yahweh. Because he is the one who strengthens and supports me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he will save me from anything that might trouble me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 16:9"/>Therefore I am very glad,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I can rest securely,
<verse eid="PSA 16:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 16:10"/>because you, Yahweh, will save me from going to the place where dead people go,
</para>
  <para style="q1">yes, you will save me, a godly person, from dying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 16:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 16:11"/>You reveal to me how to live in a way that will make me joyful now and will result in receiving eternal life in the future.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You make me joyful when I am with you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You give pleasures forever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 16:11"/><verse eid="PSA 16:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 16"/>
  <chapter number="17" style="c" sid="PSA 17"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 17:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A prayer of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, listen to me while I plead with you to act justly toward me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Hear me while I call out to you to help me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Pay attention to what I say while I pray
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am speaking honestly.
<verse eid="PSA 17:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 17:2"/>May you declare that I am innocent;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may you decide what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 17:3"/>You know what I think, {even} during the night.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have examined me and not found anything that grieves you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have determined that I will not sin by what I say.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 17:4"/>Regarding the actions of people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">according to what you have commanded, I have carefully avoided living a violent life.
<verse eid="PSA 17:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 17:5"/>I have carefully obeyed what you told me to do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have not failed to do those things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 17:6"/>O God, I am praying to you because I know that you will answer me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please listen to what I am saying.
<verse eid="PSA 17:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 17:7"/>Wonderfully show how you faithfully love me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you who rescue with your great power the people who trust you to protect them from their enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 17:8"/>Protect me as carefully as people protect their own eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q2">protect me like mother birds protect their babies under their wings.
<verse eid="PSA 17:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 17:9"/>Do not allow wicked people to attack me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those enemies of mine who surround me, wanting to kill me.
<verse eid="PSA 17:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 17:10"/>They never pity anyone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they are always speaking boastfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 17:11"/>They have searched for me and found me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They surround me, watching for an opportunity to attack and kill me.
<verse eid="PSA 17:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 17:12"/>These wicked people are like lions that are ready to tear {apart their prey}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are like young lions that are hiding, waiting {to pounce on their prey}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 17:13"/>Yahweh, come and oppose my enemies and make them fall to the ground when you defeat them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Take violent action and deliver me from wicked men!
<verse eid="PSA 17:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 17:14"/>Yahweh, by your power rescue me from those people who are interested {only} in things here in this world.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You provide them with many good things.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They have many children and {when they die,} they leave their wealth to their descendants.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 17:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 17:15"/>{Yahweh}, because I act in the right way, I will see you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When I wake up I will see you, and then I will be happy.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 17:15"/><verse eid="PSA 17:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 17"/>
  <chapter number="18" style="c" sid="PSA 18"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: David, God’s servant, wrote this psalm. He sang this song to Yahweh after Yahweh had rescued him from Saul and his other enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 18:1"/>This is what he sang: “Yahweh, I love you, the one who enables me to be strong.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 18:2"/>Yahweh, you are like a huge rock and like a fortress {where I can go to be safe}. I can be confident that you will rescue me when I am in trouble. You are my God. You protect me. I am as safe as I would be if I were hiding on top of a cliff. It is as if you are a shield that defends me. You are the powerful God who saves me. You are like a high place {where I am safe from my enemies}.
<verse eid="PSA 18:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 18:3"/>You deserve for people to praise you, Yahweh. When I cry to you {for help}, you rescue me from my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 18:4"/>{Someone was trying to kill me, and} I was in such danger of dying that it was as if someone was trying to tie ropes around me. His wicked plans against me were like floodwaters that were carrying me away, and this made me very afraid.
<verse eid="PSA 18:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 18:5"/>I did not think I could escape going to the place where dead people go. It was as if that place had wrapped ropes around me and was pulling me down into it. It was as if the only direction I could walk was right into a trap where I would surely die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 18:6"/>But when I was very distressed, I cried out to you, Yahweh my God. From your temple in heaven you could hear me calling to you, and you listened to my prayer.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 18:7"/>It made you so angry {that someone was trying to kill me, and you responded so powerfully} that it was as if there was a great earthquake and as if you shook the foundations of the mountains.
<verse eid="PSA 18:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 18:8"/>{Your power was so great that} it was as if there was a volcano from which smoke was rising, a stream of fire was flowing out that burned up everything in its path, and hot coals were flying into the air that started fires where they landed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 18:9"/>{Your power was so great} when you came {to help me that} it was as if there was a great thunderstorm, with only a little sky visible below the low-hanging dark clouds.
<verse eid="PSA 18:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 18:10"/>He flew, riding on the back of an angel traveling fast, which the wind was blowing along.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 18:11"/>It was as if you had made the darkness of the storm a safe place for you to stay. Yes, it was as if you had a temporary shelter within the dark storm clouds that were full of moisture.
<verse eid="PSA 18:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 18:12"/>It was as if it became bright where you were within the clouds, and then hailstones and lightning bolts came from there.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 18:13"/>It was as if there was a loud sound of thunder in the sky because you, Yahweh, the God who is greater than all other spirit beings, had spoken {to announce that you were coming to rescue me}, and as if hailstones and coals of fire {continued to come}.
<verse eid="PSA 18:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 18:14"/>It was as if you sent many flashes of lightning that made my enemies so afraid that they ran away in different directions, as if you had shot arrows at them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 18:15"/>The bottom of the ocean became visible, and the water uncovered the foundations of the earth when Yahweh rebuked his enemies
</para>
  <para style="q1">with the breath that came in his anger!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 18:16"/>It was as if you reached down from heaven and grabbed me so that you could pull me up out of the deep water of the ocean.
<verse eid="PSA 18:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 18:17"/>There was a powerful man who wanted to harm me, and there were people who hated me. They were too strong for me to defeat, but you rescued me from them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 18:18"/>They attacked me, and they would have destroyed me, but you, Yahweh, protected me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 18:19"/>You brought me to a place where I was safe. You love me, and so you rescued me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 18:20"/>Yahweh, you did good things for me because I did what was right. I did not harm my enemies, so you made sure that they did not harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 18:21"/>Yahweh, I have lived as you want people to live. I have not stopped obeying you, my God, and done wicked things instead.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 18:22"/>I have remained aware of what you have said people should do, and I have continued to obey all your laws.
<verse eid="PSA 18:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 18:23"/>I have not done anything for which you would blame me. I have been careful not to do anything for which you would punish me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 18:24"/>You have done good things for me because I did what is right. You recognize that I am innocent.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 18:25"/>When people are loyal to you, you act loyally toward them; when people are careful to do what you want them to do, you do good things for them.
<verse eid="PSA 18:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 18:26"/>You allow sincere people to recognize how sincere you are. But when people try to trick others, you show that you are much more clever than they are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 18:27"/>You rescue people whom others are afflicting, but you humiliate those who are proud.
<verse eid="PSA 18:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 18:28"/>Yahweh my God, it is as if you light my lamp so that I can see even when it is dark.
<verse eid="PSA 18:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 18:29"/>With your help I have caught and defeated a band of raiders. With your help I have captured a city that had walls around it, as if I had leaped over those walls.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 18:30"/>My God, everything that you do is perfect. Everything that you say is right. You protect everyone who depends on you, as if you are a shield that defends them.

<verse eid="PSA 18:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 18:31"/>Yahweh, you are the only real God. Only you are like a huge rock {where I can go to be safe}.
<verse eid="PSA 18:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 18:32"/>My God, you enable me to be strong like someone who equips me for war. You make sure that nothing prevents me from doing what you want me to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 18:33"/>You enable me to walk about safely in the mountains, as a deer does, without falling.
<verse eid="PSA 18:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 18:34"/>You teach me how to fight in a battle. You give me the strength to bend {and string} a bronze bow.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 18:35"/>You have saved me by protecting me like a shield, you are strong and therefore keep me safe. You humble yourself and answer my prayers and this is what has made me successful.
<verse eid="PSA 18:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 18:36"/>You have given me many ways to respond to each situation. As a result, I have been able to carry out my plans successfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 18:37"/>I chased my enemies and defeated them. I did not stop fighting them until I had killed them all.
<verse eid="PSA 18:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 18:38"/>I wounded them so badly that the ones who fell to the ground never got up because they died of their wounds.
<verse eid="PSA 18:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 18:39"/>You have given me the strength and courage to fight battles. When people revolted against me, you enabled me to subdue them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 18:40"/>You enabled me to defeat my enemies and step in triumph on their necks. You gave me power over those who hated me so that I was able to destroy them.

<verse eid="PSA 18:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 18:41"/>They called out for someone to rescue them, but no one did. They cried out {for help} to you, Yahweh, but you did not help them.
<verse eid="PSA 18:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 18:42"/>I defeated them so completely that they were no longer any threat to me, no more than tiny particles of dust that the wind blows away would be. It was as if they were dirt that I threw out into the street.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 18:43"/>You rescued me from the Israelites who tried to rebel against me. You appointed me as the ruler of many nations. Foreign people are now my subjects.
<verse eid="PSA 18:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 18:44"/>When they heard about what Yahweh enabled me to do, they obeyed me. Foreign rulers fearfully bow down in front of me {to show their submission}.
<verse eid="PSA 18:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 18:45"/>I defeat foreign armies that resist me so that they become weak, like a plant that dries up in the sun. They surrender and come out of their walled cities shaking with weakness and fear.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 18:46"/>Yahweh, you are the only real God! I praise you! You are like a huge rock {where I can go to be safe}! You are the God who rescues me. Everyone should exalt you.

<verse eid="PSA 18:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 18:47"/>You are the God who enables me to conquer enemies who have attacked me. You cause the people of other nations to be subject to my rule.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 18:48"/>You kept my enemies from capturing me. People rebelled against me, but it as if their armies had been floodwaters and you lifted me out of them to safety. You rescued me from men who tried to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 18:48"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 18:49"/>Because of all this, I thank you, Yahweh, so that all people groups will know that you are the one who has helped me. I will sing to praise you for what you have done that has made you famous.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 18:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 18:50"/>You chose me to be king, and you have done great things to save me from my enemies. You faithfully show kindness to me, David, whom you anointed as king, as well as to my descendants forever.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 18:50"/><verse eid="PSA 18:50"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 18"/>
  <chapter number="19" style="c" sid="PSA 19"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 19:1"/>{When people look at everything that} God {has placed} in the skies, they can see that he is very great.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, the way God made the sky shows people that he is powerful.
<verse eid="PSA 19:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 19:2"/>Day after day {it is as though the sun} proclaims the glory of God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and night after night {it is as though the moon and stars} say that God made them.
<verse eid="PSA 19:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 19:3"/>They do not really speak;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they do not say any words.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There is no sound from them for anyone to hear.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 19:4"/>But what they declare {about God} goes throughout all the world,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {even people who live in} the most distant places on earth can know it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The sun is in the skies where God placed it;
<verse eid="PSA 19:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 19:5"/>it rises each morning like a bridegroom {who is happy} as he comes out of his bedroom after his wedding.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is like a strong athlete who is very eager to start running in a race.
<verse eid="PSA 19:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 19:6"/>The sun rises at one side of the sky and goes across the sky and sets on the other side,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is nothing that is unaffected by its heat.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 19:7"/>The instructions that Yahweh has given us are perfect;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they keep us from living in a way that would cause God to condemn us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We can be sure that the things that Yahweh has told us are trustworthy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by learning them people who have not been previously taught will become wise.
<verse eid="PSA 19:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 19:8"/>Yahweh’s laws are fair;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{when we obey them,} we become joyful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The commands of Yahweh are morally perfect,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {by learning them} we start to understand {how God wants us to behave}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 19:9"/>The law of Yahweh causes people to revere him and therefore live in a morally upright way;
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is something that will endure forever.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The things Yahweh has decreed are true,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are completely righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 19:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 19:10"/>Yahweh’s commandments are more valuable than gold,
</para>
  <para style="q2">even great amounts of the purest gold.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Learning the things Yahweh teaches us through them is more pleasurable than eating honey,
</para>
  <para style="q2">than honey dripping from honeycombs.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 19:11"/>Furthermore, by your commandments I am warned {about what things I should not do}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You greatly reward those who obey them.
<verse eid="PSA 19:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 19:12"/>There is no one who can know all his sins;
</para>
  <para style="q2">so Yahweh, forgive me for these things which I do that I do not realize are wrong.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 19:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 19:13"/>Also, keep me from doing things that I know are wrong;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not let my sinful desires control me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If you do that, then I will be guiltless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will not be guilty of committing any great sin.
<verse eid="PSA 19:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 19:14"/>I pray that both what I say, and what I think about,
</para>
  <para style="q1">be pleasing to you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, you who enable me to be strong and who redeem me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 19:14"/><verse eid="PSA 19:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 19"/>
  <chapter number="20" style="c" sid="PSA 20"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 20:1"/>I desire that Yahweh will answer you {when you call out to him} when you are in a crisis!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I desire that Yahweh, the God whom {our ancestor} Jacob worshiped, will protect you {from your enemies}.
<verse eid="PSA 20:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 20:2"/>I desire that he may come from his sacred temple and help you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and aid you from {where he lives} on Mount Zion.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 20:3"/>I desire that he may accept all your grain offerings
</para>
  <para style="q2">and accept all your {other} offerings that you give him to be burned {on the altar}.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 20:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 20:4"/>I want him to give you what you desire,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I want him to allow you to be able to accomplish everything that you have planned to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 20:5"/>When you defeat your enemies, we will shout joyfully.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We will lift up a banner proclaiming that it is Yahweh our God {who helps us}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I desire Yahweh to do everything that you have requested him to do.
<verse eid="PSA 20:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 20:6"/>I know now that Yahweh rescues the one whom he has chosen {to be king}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">From his holy place in heaven he will answer him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will save him by his great power.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 20:7"/>Some {kings} trust that because they have chariots {they will be able to defeat their enemies},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and some trust that their horses {will enable them to defeat their enemies},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but we will trust in the power of Yahweh our God.
<verse eid="PSA 20:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 20:8"/>Some will stumble and fall down,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but we will be strong and not be moved.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 20:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 20:9"/>Yahweh, enable your king {to defeat our enemies}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We desire that the king answer us when we cry out {for help}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 20:9"/><verse eid="PSA 20:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 20"/>
  <chapter number="21" style="c" sid="PSA 21"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 21:1"/>Yahweh, {your} king is glad because you have enabled him to be strong
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because you have rescued him {from his enemies}; indeed, how exceedingly he rejoices.
<verse eid="PSA 21:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 21:2"/>You have given {your} king the things he desired,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have not refused to do what he requested you to do.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 21:3"/>In answer to his prayer, you bless him with many good things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You place a gold crown on his head.
<verse eid="PSA 21:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 21:4"/>He asked you to let him live for a long time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you have enabled him to live for a long time.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 21:5"/>People honor him greatly because you have helped him defeat his enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have made him famous.
<verse eid="PSA 21:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 21:6"/>You bless him forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you cause him to be joyful in your presence.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 21:7"/>The king trusts in you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and because you, who are much greater than all other spirit beings, faithfully love him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will protect him.
<verse eid="PSA 21:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 21:8"/>You, the king, will defeat all your enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, you will surely defeat all those who hate you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 21:9"/>When you, the king, appear, you will so completely destroy them that it will be as if you threw them into a fiery furnace.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Because Yahweh is angry with them, he will decimate them so completely that it will be as if he swallowed them whole or burned them up.
<verse eid="PSA 21:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 21:10"/>You, the king, will remove their children from this earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their descendants will all disappear.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 21:11"/>They want to harm you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what they plan will never succeed.
<verse eid="PSA 21:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 21:12"/>You will cause them to run away
</para>
  <para style="q2">by shooting arrows at them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 21:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 21:13"/>Yahweh, show everyone how very strong you are!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{When you do that,} we will sing and praise you because you are very powerful.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 21:13"/><verse eid="PSA 21:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 21"/>
  <chapter number="22" style="c" sid="PSA 22"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: David wrote this song. The tune is “The Doe of the Dawn.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 22:1"/>My God, my God, why have you abandoned me?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Why do you not come and help me?
</para>
  <para style="q2">Why do you not respond to me when {I am suffering so severely that} I am groaning?
<verse eid="PSA 22:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 22:2"/>My God, every day I call to you during the daytime and during the night,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you do not answer me, so I am not able to sleep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 22:3"/>But you are holy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You sit on your throne as king, and receive praise in your sacred tent from your people Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 22:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 22:4"/>Our ancestors trusted in you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They trusted in you and you rescued them.
<verse eid="PSA 22:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 22:5"/>When they cried out to you for help, you saved them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They trusted in you, and they were not disappointed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 22:6"/>But you have not rescued me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">People despise me and consider that I am not a man;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they think that I am a worm!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Everyone scorns me and despises me.
<verse eid="PSA 22:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 22:7"/>Everyone who sees me makes fun of me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They sneer at me and {insult me by} shaking their heads {at me}.
<verse eid="PSA 22:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 22:8"/>{My enemies say,} “He trusts in Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so Yahweh should save him!
</para>
  <para style="q1">{He says that} Yahweh is very pleased with him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">if that is so, Yahweh should rescue him!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 22:9"/>You, God, have been with me since I was in my mother’s womb,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you taught me to trust you when I was at my mother’s breasts.
<verse eid="PSA 22:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 22:10"/>It was as though you had adopted me right when I was born.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have been my God ever since I was born.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 22:11"/>Come near to me {and help me,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">because my enemies are near me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is no one who is helping me.
<verse eid="PSA 22:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 22:12"/>My enemies surround me {like} a group of wild bulls.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Fierce people, like those} strong bulls that {graze on the hills} in {the region of} Bashan, surround me.
<verse eid="PSA 22:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 22:13"/>{They are like} roaring lions that are attacking the animals that they want to kill.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They rush toward me to kill me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they {are like lions that} have their mouths open, ready to tear their victims to pieces.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 22:14"/>I am completely exhausted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and am in much pain!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I feel greatly discouraged!
<verse eid="PSA 22:14"/><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 22:15"/>My strength is all dried up
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a broken piece of a clay jar that has dried {in the sun}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have allowed {me to become so thirsty that} my tongue sticks to the roof of my mouth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Oh God, I think that you are about to let} my body die and become dust!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 22:16"/>My enemies surround me like a pack of wild dogs.
</para>
  <para style="q2">A group of evil men has encircled me{, ready to attack me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have pierced my hands and my feet.
<verse eid="PSA 22:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 22:17"/>{I am so weak and thin that} I can see and count my bones.
</para>
  <para style="q2">My enemies stare at me and gloat {about what has happened to} me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 22:18"/>{They looked at} the clothes that I {was wearing}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and gambled to determine which piece each of them would get.
<verse eid="PSA 22:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 22:19"/>Yahweh, do not be like my enemies; rather be concerned for me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You who are the one who strengthens me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">come quickly and help me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 22:20"/>Rescue me from {those who want to} kill me with their swords.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save me from those who are {like wild} dogs.
<verse eid="PSA 22:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 22:21"/>Snatch me away from my enemies who are like lions whose jaws {are already open}, ready to chew me up!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Grab me away from those men who are like wild oxen {that attack other animals with} their horns!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 22:22"/>{Because you have saved me,} I will proclaim to my fellow Israelites how great you are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise you among the group of your people gathered together {to worship you}.
<verse eid="PSA 22:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 22:23"/>You people who have an awesome respect for Yahweh, praise him!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All you who are descended from Jacob, honor Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All you Israelite people, revere him!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 22:24"/>Yahweh does not despise or ignore those who are suffering.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He pays attention to them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he responds when they call out to him {for help}.
<verse eid="PSA 22:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 22:25"/>Yahweh, in the great gathering {of your people,} I will praise you for what you have done.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the presence of those who revere Yahweh, I will offer {the sacrifice} that I promised {to make to you because you delivered me}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 22:26"/>The poor people {whom I have invited to the meal} will eat as much as they want.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All who come to worship Yahweh will praise him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I pray that {God will enable} you all to live a long and happy life!
<verse eid="PSA 22:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 22:27"/>People in all nations, even in the remote areas, will think about Yahweh and turn to him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People from all the clans in the world will bow down before you,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 22:28"/>because Yahweh is the king!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He rules the people of all nations.
<verse eid="PSA 22:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 22:29"/>All the rich people on the earth will celebrate and bow before him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All those who are close to dying will kneel in worship {before him}, yes, those who are not able to keep themselves alive.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 22:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 22:30"/>People who have not been born yet will {also} serve Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We will tell our descendants what Yahweh {has done}.
<verse eid="PSA 22:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 22:31"/>People will come and will proclaim to people not yet born, {who will live in future years,} that because Yahweh is righteous {he has delivered those who prayed to him for help}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{People will tell them} that, “Yahweh did {it}!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 22:31"/><verse eid="PSA 22:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 22"/>
  <chapter number="23" style="c" sid="PSA 23"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 23:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh {cares for} me {like} a shepherd {cares for his sheep},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{so} I {know that I} will have everything that I need.
<verse eid="PSA 23:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 23:2"/>Yahweh nourishes and encourages my inner person and enables me to rest in peace,
</para>
  <para style="q1">like a shepherd who leads {his sheep} to places where there is plenty of green grass {for them to eat}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and leads them to streams where the water is flowing slowly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 23:3"/>Yahweh renews my strength.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He gives me good guidance for how I should live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I, and others, will honor him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 23:4"/>Even when I am in dangerous and scary circumstances
</para>
  <para style="q2">in which evil men might kill or hurt me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will fear nothing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you are with me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I feel comforted and reassured because you protect and care for me like a shepherd protects his sheep by using his club and his walking stick to protect them from being attacked by wild animals.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 23:5"/>You {richly} provide food for me and protect me from my enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You joyfully welcome me and honor me
</para>
  <para style="q2">as people joyfully receive the guests they have invited by pouring olive oil over their heads.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have given me very many blessings!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 23:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 23:6"/>I am certain that Yahweh will be good to me and will continue to love me faithfully as long as I live.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will worship Yahweh in his sanctuary throughout my life.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 23:6"/><verse eid="PSA 23:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 23"/>
  <chapter number="24" style="c" sid="PSA 24"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 24:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">The earth and everything in it belongs to Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All the people in the world belong to him too,
<verse eid="PSA 24:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 24:2"/>because he caused the ground to be above the water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">above the water that was deep below the surface of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 24:3"/>This is the type of person who Yahweh will allow to go up onto his mountain, Mount Zion {in Jerusalem},
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to stand {and worship} him in his sacred tent.
<verse eid="PSA 24:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 24:4"/>Only those whose actions and thoughts are pure,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who have not worshiped idols,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who do not tell lies when they have solemnly promised to speak truthfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 24:5"/>Yahweh will bless this type of person.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When Yahweh {judges them,} he who has saved them, he will say that they are righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 24:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 24:6"/>Such are the ones who seek Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the descendants of Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who seek you, Yahweh.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah

</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 24:7"/>Open up the gates {of the sacred tent},
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that our glorious king may enter!
<verse eid="PSA 24:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 24:8"/>I will tell you who this glorious king is.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He is} Yahweh, the one who is very strong;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He is} Yahweh, who conquers {all his enemies} in battles!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 24:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 24:9"/>Open up the gates {of the sacred tent},
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that our glorious king may enter!
<verse eid="PSA 24:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 24:10"/>I will tell you who he, this glorious king, is.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He is} Yahweh, who commands armies;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is our glorious king!
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 24:10"/><verse eid="PSA 24:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 24"/>
  <chapter number="25" style="c" sid="PSA 25"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 25:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I come to you in prayer and tell you all that I need.
<verse eid="PSA 25:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 25:2"/>I trust in you, my God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not allow my enemies {to defeat me},
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the result that they would rejoice and I would be ashamed.
<verse eid="PSA 25:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 25:3"/>Truly, you will not allow any of those who trust in you to be ashamed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will cause those who act treacherously toward others to be ashamed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 25:4"/>Yahweh, show me how I should conduct my life as you want me to.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Teach me how to act in the manner that is pleasing to you.
<verse eid="PSA 25:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 25:5"/>Teach me to conduct my life by obeying your truth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you are my God, the one who saves me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I trust in you at all times.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 25:6"/>Yahweh, please act mercifully to me and faithfully love me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because that is the way that you have acted since long ago.
<verse eid="PSA 25:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 25:7"/>Forgive me for the sinful things I did when I was young and for my rebellious actions {as an adult}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I ask that, because you faithfully love your people, you treat me kindly and forgive me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I ask that you do this because you are good!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 25:8"/>Yahweh is good and acts righteously,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so he shows sinful people the right way to conduct their lives.
<verse eid="PSA 25:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 25:9"/>He shows humble people what is right for them to do
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teaches them what he wants them to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 25:10"/>Yahweh always faithfully loves and does what he has promised
</para>
  <para style="q2">to those who obey his covenant and who do what he requires.
<verse eid="PSA 25:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 25:11"/>Yahweh, forgive me for all my sins, which are many,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I and others may honor you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 25:12"/>To all those who revere Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he shows them the right way to conduct their lives.
<verse eid="PSA 25:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 25:13"/>They will always be prosperous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their descendants will continue to live in {this} land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 25:14"/>Yahweh is a friend of those who revere him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he teaches them the covenant that he made {with them}.
<verse eid="PSA 25:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 25:15"/>I always ask Yahweh to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he will rescue me when my enemies attempt to hurt me.
<verse eid="PSA 25:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 25:16"/>{Yahweh,} pay attention to me and be merciful to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I have no one to help me and I am suffering.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 25:17"/>{Because of my present circumstances} there are many things that cause me to worry.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me from the things that are causing me to be distressed.
<verse eid="PSA 25:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 25:18"/>Take notice that I am in difficult circumstances and troubled,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and forgive me for every sinful thing I have done.
<verse eid="PSA 25:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 25:19"/>Take notice that I have many enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that they hate me very much.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 25:20"/>Protect me and rescue me {from them};
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not allow {them to defeat me
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the result that} I would be ashamed,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because I go to you to keep me safe.
<verse eid="PSA 25:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 25:21"/>Protect me because I do what is good and honest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because I trust in you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 25:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 25:22"/>God, rescue {us} Israelite people from all of our troubles!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 25:22"/><verse eid="PSA 25:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 25"/>
  <chapter number="26" style="c" sid="PSA 26"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 26:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, show that I am innocent.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have done what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have trusted in Yahweh without doubting him.
<verse eid="PSA 26:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 26:2"/>Yahweh, examine what I have done and test me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">thoroughly evaluate what I think in my inner being.
<verse eid="PSA 26:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 26:3"/>I never forget that you faithfully love me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I conduct my life according to what you say is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 26:4"/>I do not spend my time with liars,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I stay away from hypocrites.
<verse eid="PSA 26:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 26:5"/>I do not like to be with evil people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I avoid wicked people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 26:6"/>Yahweh, I wash my hands to show that I have not done what was wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q1">As I join with others marching around your altar,
<verse eid="PSA 26:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 26:7"/>we sing songs to thank you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we tell others the wonderful things that you have done.
<verse eid="PSA 26:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 26:8"/>Yahweh, I love {to be in} the sanctuary where you dwell,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the place where your glory appears.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 26:9"/>Do not get rid of me like you get rid of sinners.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not cause me to die like you cause those who murder people to die,
<verse eid="PSA 26:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 26:10"/>and people who are ready to do wicked things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people who are always taking bribes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 26:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 26:11"/>But as for me, I always try to do what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So rescue me and act kindly toward me.
<verse eid="PSA 26:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 26:12"/>{Because I have conducted myself righteously} I am secure,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when all Yahweh’s people gather together, I praise him among them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 26:12"/><verse eid="PSA 26:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 26"/>
  <chapter number="27" style="c" sid="PSA 27"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 27:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh encourages me and nourishes my inner being. He is the one who saves me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will not fear anyone.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh is the one to whom I go for refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will not dread anyone.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 27:2"/>When those who do evil things come near me to attack and destroy me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh enables me to defeat them so that they fall down.
<verse eid="PSA 27:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 27:3"/>Even if an army sets up their tents in order to attack me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not be afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Even if they attack me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will trust {in God}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 27:4"/>There is one thing that I have requested from Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that one thing I will repeatedly ask Yahweh for.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{This is the one thing I ask of Yahweh}: that I may worship in Yahweh’s sanctuary every day during my life,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to experience how wonderful Yahweh is.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When I am in his sanctuary then I will ask him {for guidance}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 27:5"/>When I have troubles he will protect me in his tabernacle;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, he will keep me safe in his sacred tent.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will keep me safe as if he were setting me high upon a rock {where my enemies cannot reach me}.
<verse eid="PSA 27:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 27:6"/>Then I will triumph over my enemies who surround me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will shout joyfully as I offer sacrifices in his sacred tent,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise Yahweh as I sing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 27:7"/>Yahweh, listen to me while I call {to you in prayer}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Act kindly toward me and answer my prayer.
<verse eid="PSA 27:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 27:8"/>{I sensed that I heard you say,} “Seek me and my help,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">{so,} Yahweh, I will respond by seeking you and your help.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 27:9"/>I am your servant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not be angry with me, or turn away from me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have always helped me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are the one who has saved me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so do not abandon me now.
<verse eid="PSA 27:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 27:10"/>My father and mother have left me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh will take care of me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 27:11"/>Yahweh, teach me to do what you want me to do,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and guide me so that I remain safe
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I have enemies {who want to hurt me}.
<verse eid="PSA 27:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 27:12"/>Do not allow my enemies to do to me what they want,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they say false things about me and want violent things to happen to me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 27:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 27:13"/>I would have died if I had not trusted you
</para>
  <para style="q2">to be good to me as long as I live.
<verse eid="PSA 27:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 27:14"/>Trust in Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Have a strong and courageous attitude,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wait expectantly for Yahweh {to help you}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 27:14"/><verse eid="PSA 27:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 27"/>
  <chapter number="28" style="c" sid="PSA 28"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 28:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I call out to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are like a huge rock {on top of which I am safe}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not refuse to answer me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because if you refuse to answer me, I will soon be with those who are in their graves.
<verse eid="PSA 28:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 28:2"/>Pay attention to me and respond when I call out for you to help me
</para>
  <para style="q2">when I pray, lifting up my hands as I face your very holy place in your sacred tent.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 28:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 28:3"/>Do not get rid of me when you get rid of wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those who do wicked deeds.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those people speak peacefully toward others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">while in their inner beings, they hate them and devise evil plans.
<verse eid="PSA 28:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 28:4"/>Punish those people in the way that they deserve for what they have done;
</para>
  <para style="q2">punish them for their evil deeds.
<verse eid="PSA 28:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 28:5"/>Yahweh will get rid of them permanently and not let them appear again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh {will do this} because these evil people do not pay attention to the righteous things he has taught his people and do not take notice that he always judges evil deeds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 28:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 28:6"/>Praise Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he responded to me when I called out for him to help me.
<verse eid="PSA 28:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 28:7"/>Yahweh strengthens me and he protects me like a shield;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I trust in him, and he helps me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">As a result I am glad in my inner being,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise him with my songs {of praise}.
<verse eid="PSA 28:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 28:8"/>Yahweh strengthens and protects his people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh saves the one he appointed to be king.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 28:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 28:9"/>Yahweh, rescue your people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and bless those who belong to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Take care of them like a shepherd takes care of his sheep;
</para>
  <para style="q2">take care of them forever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 28:9"/><verse eid="PSA 28:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 28"/>
  <chapter number="29" style="c" sid="PSA 29"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 29:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">You heavenly beings, praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Declare that he is very glorious and powerful.
<verse eid="PSA 29:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 29:2"/>Proclaim that Yahweh is glorious.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Bow down and worship Yahweh in holy attire.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 29:3"/>{People hear} Yahweh’s voice above the sea;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the glorious God thunders.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh’s {voice thunders} over the large sea.
<verse eid="PSA 29:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 29:4"/>Yahweh’s voice is powerful and majestic.
<verse eid="PSA 29:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 29:5"/>The sound of Yahweh’s voice breaks cedar trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the cedars that grow in Lebanon.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 29:6"/>He causes {the mountains in} Lebanon to jump like calves jump,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he causes Mount Hermon to jump as a young wild bull jumps.
<verse eid="PSA 29:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 29:7"/>Yahweh tells the lightning to flash {upon the mountains} and it hews out rocks.
<verse eid="PSA 29:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 29:8"/>The sound of Yahweh’s voice causes the wilderness to shake;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he shakes the wilderness of Kadesh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 29:9"/>The sound of Yahweh’s voice makes the deer give birth
</para>
  <para style="q2">and strips the leaves from the trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">while the people in Yahweh’s sacred tent say, “Praise Yahweh!”
<verse eid="PSA 29:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 29:10"/>Yahweh rules as king over the waters that are above the sky;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh rules as king forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 29:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 29:11"/>Yahweh will strengthen his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will bless them by giving them good things and causing them to be happy and peaceful.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 29:11"/><verse eid="PSA 29:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 29"/>
  <chapter number="30" style="c" sid="PSA 30"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">David wrote this psalm to be sung at the dedication of the tabernacle.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 30:1"/>Yahweh, I praise you
</para>
  <para style="q1">because you rescued me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You did not allow {me to die with the result that}
</para>
  <para style="q1">my enemies could gloat.
<verse eid="PSA 30:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 30:2"/>Yahweh my God,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I called out for you to help me {when I was sick,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">you healed me.
<verse eid="PSA 30:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 30:3"/>Yahweh, when I was dying you restored me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I was nearly dead,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but you caused me to get well.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 30:4"/>All you who are faithful to Yahweh, sing praise to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Think about what Yahweh, the holy one,
</para>
  <para style="q2">has done, and thank him.
<verse eid="PSA 30:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 30:5"/>When he becomes angry,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he is angry for only a very short time,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he is good {to us} all of our lives.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We may cry during the night,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but the next morning we will be joyful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 30:6"/>As for me, when my life was going well,
</para>
  <para style="q1">I said {to myself},
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Nothing will ever trouble me.”
<verse eid="PSA 30:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 30:7"/>Yahweh, because you were good to me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">at first you caused me to be secure as a mountain.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{But then you let me become ill when}
</para>
  <para style="q2">you stopped protecting me {from illness},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I became greatly disturbed.
<verse eid="PSA 30:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 30:8"/>{Then} I called out to you, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I pleaded for you, the Lord, to help me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 30:9"/>{I said,} “{Yahweh,} you will gain nothing if I die.
</para>
  <para style="q1">It will not benefit you at all if I go
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the place where the dead people are.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Dead people certainly are not able to praise you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they are not able to tell others that you are faithful.
<verse eid="PSA 30:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 30:10"/>Yahweh, listen to me, and act mercifully to me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, help me.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 30:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 30:11"/>{But now} you have changed my circumstances
</para>
  <para style="q2">and healed me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and as a result I have stopped grieving
</para>
  <para style="q2">and now dance joyfully.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have caused me to change from the clothes that showed that I was very sad
</para>
  <para style="q1">and to put on clothes that show that I am very joyful.
<verse eid="PSA 30:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 30:12"/>{You did that} so that I would not be silent
</para>
  <para style="q1">but would sing out to praise you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, you are my God, and I will thank you forever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 30:12"/><verse eid="PSA 30:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 30"/>
  <chapter number="31" style="c" sid="PSA 31"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 31:1"/>Yahweh, I come to you to protect me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Never allow {them to defeat me, with the result that} I would be ashamed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Since you always do what is right and just,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please rescue me.
<verse eid="PSA 31:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 31:2"/>Respond to my prayers for help, and save me right now!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Be {like} a huge rock where I can flee for refuge,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {like} a strong fortress in which my enemies cannot harm me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 31:3"/>{Yes,} you are {like} a huge rock and {like} a fortress {where I can go to be safe}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">For the sake of your reputation you guide me {so that no harm comes to me}.
<verse eid="PSA 31:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 31:4"/>You are the one who protects me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so you will rescue me from the evil plans my enemies have secretly made to hurt me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 31:5"/>I put myself into your care.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have rescued me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, you are faithful.
<verse eid="PSA 31:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 31:6"/>I hate those who worship useless idols,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I trust in Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 31:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 31:7"/>I will be very glad because you faithfully love me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have noticed that I have suffered,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and have known the troubling things I have experienced.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 31:8"/>You have not allowed my enemies to capture me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">instead, you brought me to a place where I was safe.
<verse eid="PSA 31:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 31:9"/>Yahweh, act kindly toward me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am distressed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Because I cry so much that my eyes are tired,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am completely exhausted.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 31:10"/>I have become very weak because I am so miserable;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my life is getting shorter.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have become weak because of the sinful things that I have done.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am totally exhausted.
<verse eid="PSA 31:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 31:11"/>All of my enemies make fun of me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my neighbors, especially, despise me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My friends are afraid of me {because they think that you, God, are punishing me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When they see me on the streets, they run away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 31:12"/>People have forgotten me like they forget people who are dead.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am {as useless as} a broken pot.
<verse eid="PSA 31:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 31:13"/>There are terrifying things all around me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I hear people whispering {things about me}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My enemies are making plans
</para>
  <para style="q2">to kill me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 31:14"/>But Yahweh, I trust in you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I say {confidently} that you are the God I worship.
<verse eid="PSA 31:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 31:15"/>You control the events and circumstances of my life.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save me from my enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from those who pursue me.
<verse eid="PSA 31:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 31:16"/>Act kindly toward me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and rescue me because you always faithfully love me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 31:17"/>Yahweh, I call out to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so do not allow others to shame me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I desire that you cause wicked people to be ashamed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I desire that they {soon die and} go down to the place where the dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 31:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 31:18"/>I desire that you will cause people who tell lies to be unable to speak.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Do that to} people who arrogantly say disrespectful things about righteous people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 31:19"/>Many indeed are the good things which you have prepared for the people who revere you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You do good things for those who go to you for protection.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone sees you protect them.
<verse eid="PSA 31:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 31:20"/>You protect people {who trust in you} by being near to them and saving them from people who devise evil schemes {to harm them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You keep them safe from their enemies who accuse them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 31:21"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">When my enemies surrounded the city {in which I was living,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">he showed me in a wonderful way that he faithfully loves me.
<verse eid="PSA 31:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 31:22"/>I was alarmed and cried out, “I have been separated from Yahweh!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">But in fact you heard me {and answered} my cry for help.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 31:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 31:23"/>You people who belong to Yahweh, love him!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Those who are loyal to him, he protects,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but those who are proud, he punishes them severely like they deserve to be punished.
<verse eid="PSA 31:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 31:24"/>You who confidently expect Yahweh {to do great things for you,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">be strong and be courageous!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 31:24"/><verse eid="PSA 31:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 31"/>
  <chapter number="32" style="c" sid="PSA 32"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 32:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those whom God has forgiven for rebelling against him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and those whose sin God has atoned for,
</para>
  <para style="q2">these are the ones who will have a truly good life!
<verse eid="PSA 32:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 32:2"/>Those whose record of sins Yahweh no longer takes into account,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and those who are not deceitful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">these are the ones who will have a truly good life!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 32:3"/>When I did not confess my sins,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my body felt weak and sick,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I groaned all day long.
<verse eid="PSA 32:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 32:4"/>Day and night, Yahweh, you afflicted me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">My strength was sapped like it would be on a hot summer day.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 32:5"/>{Then} I confessed my sinful actions to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I stopped trying to hide them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I said to myself,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“I will tell Yahweh the wrong things that I have done.”
</para>
  <para style="q1">When I confessed them, you forgave me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so now I am no longer guilty for the sinful things I did.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 32:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 32:6"/>Therefore all the people who are godly should pray to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they realize they have sinned.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{If they do that,} then it is certain that difficulties will not overwhelm them like a great flood.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 32:7"/>You are like a place where I can hide from my enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you protect me from troubles and surround me with people who are joyfully praising you for saving me from my enemies.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>
<verse eid="PSA 32:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 32:8"/>I will teach you about how you should conduct your life.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will teach you personally.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 32:9"/>Do not be like horses and mules that do not have understanding;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they need pieces of metal put in their mouth and ropes fastened to their head
</para>
  <para style="q2">so they will go in the direction you want them to go.
<verse eid="PSA 32:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 32:10"/>Wicked people will have many difficult things in their lives that will make them sad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but those who trust in Yahweh will experience him faithfully loving them all the time.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 32:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 32:11"/>{So, all} you righteous people, rejoice about {what} Yahweh {has done for you}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All you whose inner beings are pure, be glad and shout joyfully!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 32:11"/><verse eid="PSA 32:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 32"/>
  <chapter number="33" style="c" sid="PSA 33"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 33:1"/>You people who do what is right, shout joyfully because of Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because praising him is what upright people should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 33:2"/>Praise Yahweh by playing songs on the harp.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise him as you make music for him with instruments that have many strings.

<verse eid="PSA 33:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 33:3"/>Sing a new song to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">play those instruments well, and shout joyfully as you play them!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 33:4"/>Do this because everything that Yahweh says is true,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we can trust that everything that he does is right.

<verse eid="PSA 33:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 33:5"/>He loves everything that people do that is right and just.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh faithfully loves people all over the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 33:6"/>Yahweh created everything in the sky by commanding it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He created all of the stars by speaking.

<verse eid="PSA 33:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 33:7"/>He gathered all the water of the sea into one huge mass
</para>
  <para style="q2">as though scooping it into a container.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 33:8"/>Everyone on the earth should deeply revere Yahweh.

<verse eid="PSA 33:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 33:9"/>They should revere him because he is the one who spoke, making the world exist.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everything started to exist because he is the one who commanded it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 33:10"/>Yahweh stops the nations from doing what they plan to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He prevents the peoples from carrying out what they decide.

<verse eid="PSA 33:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 33:11"/>However, what Yahweh decides to do will last forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">What he plans to do will never change.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 33:12"/>What a good life people have when Yahweh is the God of their nation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he chose those people to belong to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 33:13"/>Yahweh looks down from heaven; he sees all human beings.

<verse eid="PSA 33:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 33:14"/>From the place where he lives he watches
</para>
  <para style="q2">everyone who lives on the earth.

<verse eid="PSA 33:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 33:15"/>He created each person’s heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he knows everything that they do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 33:16"/>It is not because a king has a great army that he is able to win {battles},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it is not because a soldier is very strong that he is able to defeat {his enemy}.

<verse eid="PSA 33:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 33:17"/>It is foolish to hope that a horse can save anyone;
</para>
  <para style="q2">even with its great strength, it cannot rescue {its rider}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 33:18"/>Note this: Yahweh watches over those who deeply revere him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">He watches over those who confidently expect him to faithfully love them,

<verse eid="PSA 33:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 33:19"/>to save them from dying
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to preserve them alive through any famine.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 33:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 33:20"/>We trust that Yahweh will take care of us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will help us and protect us.

<verse eid="PSA 33:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 33:21"/>Indeed, he makes us very joyful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we trust him because he is holy.

<verse eid="PSA 33:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 33:22"/>Yahweh, we pray that you will always faithfully love us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">while we confidently wait for you {to help us}.


<verse eid="PSA 33:22"/><verse eid="PSA 33:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 33"/>
  <chapter number="34" style="c" sid="PSA 34"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">David wrote this psalm about when he pretended to be insane in front of King Abimelech so that the king would send him away.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 34:1"/>I will always thank Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will constantly praise him out loud.
<verse eid="PSA 34:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 34:2"/>I will boast about {what} Yahweh {has done for me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of the humble people who hear me will rejoice.
<verse eid="PSA 34:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 34:3"/>Join with me in telling others that Yahweh is great,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and let us together proclaim how glorious he is!
<verse eid="PSA 34:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 34:4"/>I prayed to Yahweh, and he answered me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he rescued me from everything that I was afraid of.
<verse eid="PSA 34:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 34:5"/>Those who ask him {to help them} will be joyful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may Yahweh always provide for them.
<verse eid="PSA 34:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 34:6"/>I was suffering, but I called out to Yahweh, and he heard me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He saved me from all of the things that were troubling me.
<verse eid="PSA 34:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 34:7"/>An angel representing Yahweh guards people who deeply revere Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the angel rescues them {from bad things}.
<verse eid="PSA 34:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 34:8"/>Experience for yourselves how good Yahweh is!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone who trusts in Yahweh will be truly happy!
<verse eid="PSA 34:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 34:9"/>All you people who belong to Yahweh, deeply revere him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because those who deeply revere him will always have everything that they need.
<verse eid="PSA 34:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 34:10"/>{Even} young lions {sometimes} go hungry and have nothing to eat,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who trust in Yahweh for help will always have the good {things that they need}.
<verse eid="PSA 34:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 34:11"/>You who are my students, come and listen to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will teach you how to deeply revere Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 34:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 34:12"/>If any of you want to truly live
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to enjoy a good, long life,
<verse eid="PSA 34:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 34:13"/>then be careful to not say things that are harmful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to not tell lies.
<verse eid="PSA 34:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 34:14"/>Stop doing what is evil and instead do what is good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">always strive to live peacefully with others.
<verse eid="PSA 34:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 34:15"/>Yahweh pays attention to people who do what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he listens when they call {to him to help them}.
<verse eid="PSA 34:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 34:16"/>But Yahweh opposes people who do what is evil.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He does not allow their descendants to remain on the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 34:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 34:17"/>People who do what is right cry out to Yahweh, and he hears them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he rescues them from all the things that trouble them.
<verse eid="PSA 34:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 34:18"/>Yahweh is always ready to help people who are very sad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he saves people who are deeply discouraged.
<verse eid="PSA 34:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 34:19"/>People who do what is right experience many bad things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh rescues them from all of those bad things.
<verse eid="PSA 34:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 34:20"/>Yahweh protects their whole body;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not allow {their enemies} to break even one of their bones.
<verse eid="PSA 34:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 34:21"/>Wicked people will cause themselves to die because of the evil things that they do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh will punish those who hate righteous people.
<verse eid="PSA 34:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 34:22"/>Yahweh saves those who serve him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will forgive all who trust in him.


<verse eid="PSA 34:22"/><verse eid="PSA 34:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 34"/>
  <chapter number="35" style="c" sid="PSA 35"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 35:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, be the enemy of my enemies!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Defend me against those who attack me!
<verse eid="PSA 35:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 35:2"/>Protect me like a soldier who has both of his shields,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and come to help me!
<verse eid="PSA 35:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 35:3"/>Take your spear and javelin and confront those who are pursuing me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Tell me, “I am the one who saves you.”
<verse eid="PSA 35:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 35:4"/>Please defeat and dishonor those who want to kill me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make those who plan to harm me become confused and turn back.
<verse eid="PSA 35:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 35:5"/>May an angel from Yahweh chase them away
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they disappear like chaff in the wind.
<verse eid="PSA 35:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 35:6"/>May their lives be like running on a path that is dark and slippery,
</para>
  <para style="q2">while an angel from Yahweh pursues them!
<verse eid="PSA 35:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 35:7"/>Please do these things to them, because I have not done anything wrong to them, yet they try to kill me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as though they hide nets and dig pits for me to walk into!
<verse eid="PSA 35:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 35:8"/>So let disaster suddenly surprise each of them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let it be as though the nets that they hid catch them instead,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and as though they fall into their own {pits} and die!
<verse eid="PSA 35:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 35:9"/>Then I will rejoice because of {what} Yahweh {has done for me},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will be glad because he has saved me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 35:10"/>With my whole being I will say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Yahweh, no one is like you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one else rescues weak people from those who are stronger,
</para>
  <para style="q2">no one else rescues poor and needy people from those who rob them.”
<verse eid="PSA 35:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 35:11"/>Hostile people tell lies {about me} in court
</para>
  <para style="q2">and accuse me of things that I know nothing about.
<verse eid="PSA 35:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 35:12"/>I was good to them. But instead of being good to me, they are evil to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That makes me feel completely alone.
<verse eid="PSA 35:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 35:13"/>Yet for my part, when they were sick, I put on rough cloth to mourn for them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I went without food as I prayed for them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">bowing my head over my chest.
<verse eid="PSA 35:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 35:14"/>I walked around grieving for them
</para>
  <para style="q2">as I would grieve for a friend or for a brother,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I bowed down mourning for them as though for my own mother.
<verse eid="PSA 35:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 35:15"/>But when I suffered, they all gathered together and celebrated.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People whom I did not even know gathered to attack me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They kept slandering me and would not stop.
<verse eid="PSA 35:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 35:16"/>Profane people mocked me for being lame
</para>
  <para style="q2">and ground their teeth at me {to show how angry they were}.
<verse eid="PSA 35:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 35:17"/>Lord, please do more than just watch what they do!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me from these people who want to destroy me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save me from these people who are as fierce as young lions!
<verse eid="PSA 35:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 35:18"/>Then I will thank you when the great crowd of your people gather together,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise you in front of all of them.
<verse eid="PSA 35:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 35:19"/>Do not let my enemies who lie about me celebrate {because they defeated me},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not let those who hate me for no reason wink at each other {to show how pleased they are about it}.
<verse eid="PSA 35:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 35:20"/>{Do not let them succeed,} because they do not speak peacefully {to anyone};
</para>
  <para style="q2">instead, they make up lies about quiet, peaceable people in the land.
<verse eid="PSA 35:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 35:21"/>They shout loudly to accuse me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">saying, “Yes! Yes! We saw {what you did}!”
<verse eid="PSA 35:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 35:22"/>Yahweh, you have seen all of this, so please do something about it!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lord, please help me!
<verse eid="PSA 35:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 35:23"/>Become active and do the right thing for me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God and my Lord, defend me!
<verse eid="PSA 35:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 35:24"/>Yahweh my God, because you are righteous, declare that I am innocent,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not let my enemies celebrate {that they have defeated} me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 35:25"/>Do not let them think to themselves, “Yes! We got what we wanted!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not let them say {to each other}, “We have completely destroyed him!”
<verse eid="PSA 35:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 35:26"/>Instead, make all those who celebrate when bad things happen to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">feel totally ashamed and disgraced.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, completely humiliate those who boast that they are greater than me.
<verse eid="PSA 35:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 35:27"/>But let those who want God to show that I am innocent
</para>
  <para style="q2">shout for joy and celebrate!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let them always say, “Yahweh is great!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He loves to make things go well for the one who serves him.”
<verse eid="PSA 35:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 35:28"/>Then I will tell everyone how righteous you are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise you all day long.


<verse eid="PSA 35:28"/><verse eid="PSA 35:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 35"/>
  <chapter number="36" style="c" sid="PSA 36"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">Note for the worship leader: David, a man who served Yahweh faithfully, wrote this psalm.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 36:1"/>Wicked people act as though they are obeying a voice from deep within themselves that is urging them to sin.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have no respect for God at all.
<verse eid="PSA 36:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 36:2"/>Indeed, they are so proud that they refuse
</para>
  <para style="q1">to recognize how wrongly they act
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they might hate {doing those things}.
<verse eid="PSA 36:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 36:3"/>Everything that they say is wicked and deceptive;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have stopped acting wisely and {stopped} doing what is right.
<verse eid="PSA 36:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 36:4"/>They plan sinful activities while lying on their beds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they commit themselves to a bad way of living;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they do not refuse to do evil things.

<verse eid="PSA 36:4"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 36:5"/>Yahweh, the amount that you faithfully love us is so much that it is as though it fills the heavens.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If we could measure how trustworthy you are, the amount would extend into the clouds.
<verse eid="PSA 36:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 36:6"/>Your way of doing what is right is {as permanent} as the highest mountains;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your way of acting justly is {as vast and mysterious} as the deepest oceans.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, you take care of {all living creatures,} both people and animals.
<verse eid="PSA 36:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 36:7"/>God, how precious it is that you faithfully love us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You protect people just as a bird shelters its young under its wings.
<verse eid="PSA 36:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 36:8"/>You provide for them plenty of food from the abundant supply that you have;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you satisfy them with good things that they enjoy, as if from a never-ending stream.
<verse eid="PSA 36:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 36:9"/>Indeed, you are the one who causes everything to live;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are the one who makes it possible for us to understand what is true.

<verse eid="PSA 36:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 36:10"/>Please continue to faithfully love those who know you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and continue to do right for those who sincerely want to do what is right.
<verse eid="PSA 36:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 36:11"/>Do not let arrogant people overcome me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not let wicked people force me to flee.
<verse eid="PSA 36:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 36:12"/>See how the people who do evil have fallen!
</para>
  <para style="q2">God has thrown them down, and they can never get up again.


<verse eid="PSA 36:12"/><verse eid="PSA 36:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 36"/>
  <chapter number="37" style="c" sid="PSA 37"/>
  <para style="q1">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 37:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not let what wicked people do upset you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not wish that you had what people who do evil things have.
<verse eid="PSA 37:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 37:2"/>{Do not worry about them} because they will soon disappear, just as grass dries up {in the sun}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and green plants quickly wither and die.

<verse eid="PSA 37:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 37:3"/>Trust in Yahweh and do what is right;
</para>
  <para style="q2">live in the land {that he has given you},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and be faithful {to him}.
<verse eid="PSA 37:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 37:4"/>Also, enjoy Yahweh more than anything else;
</para>
  <para style="q2">then he will give you what you desire most.

<verse eid="PSA 37:4"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 37:5"/>Entrust everything that you plan to do to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">trust in him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then, for his part, he will do {whatever you need him to do}.
<verse eid="PSA 37:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 37:6"/>He will show everyone as clearly as the light of the noonday sun that you do what is right
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that you are innocent of doing anything wrong.

<verse eid="PSA 37:6"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 37:7"/>Be calm before Yahweh and wait patiently for him {to act}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not become upset when you see {evil} people succeed
</para>
  <para style="q2">as they do the {wicked} things that they have planned.
<verse eid="PSA 37:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 37:8"/>Stop being angry {about what wicked people do};
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not want to punish them yourself; that only leads to doing evil.
<verse eid="PSA 37:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 37:9"/>Do not do that because Yahweh will destroy people who do evil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but as for the people who trust Yahweh to act, they will possess the land.

<verse eid="PSA 37:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 37:10"/>Soon wicked people will disappear.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will look for them where they used to be, but they will be gone.
<verse eid="PSA 37:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 37:11"/>Humble people, however, will possess the land
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will enjoy living {there} very peacefully and well.

<verse eid="PSA 37:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 37:12"/>Wicked people plan to harm people who do what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They grind their teeth at people who do what is right {to show how much they hate them}.
<verse eid="PSA 37:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 37:13"/>But the Lord scoffs at wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he knows that the time when he will judge them is coming.

<verse eid="PSA 37:13"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 37:14"/>Wicked people draw their swords and string their bows
</para>
  <para style="q2">to kill people who are poor and helpless
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to slaughter people who live honestly.
<verse eid="PSA 37:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 37:15"/>But their swords will pierce their own hearts,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the Lord will break their bows.

<verse eid="PSA 37:15"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 37:16"/>It is better to be a person who does what is right and to have only a few possessions
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to have the abundant wealth of many wicked people.
<verse eid="PSA 37:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 37:17"/>{This is so} because Yahweh will make wicked people unable to do what they want to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he will take care of people who do what is right.

<verse eid="PSA 37:17"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 37:18"/>Each day Yahweh watches over people who do not do wrong things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and what he gives them will last forever.
<verse eid="PSA 37:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 37:19"/>During times when bad things happen they will not despair;
</para>
  <para style="q2">even when there is a famine, they will still have enough {to eat}.

<verse eid="PSA 37:19"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 37:20"/>But wicked people will die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Those who hate Yahweh will be like wildflowers that look beautiful in the meadows;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but then they will disappear {as quickly} as a puff of smoke.

<verse eid="PSA 37:20"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 37:21"/>Wicked people borrow {money} and never repay {it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people who do what is right are generous and give {freely to others}.
<verse eid="PSA 37:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 37:22"/>Moreover, those whom Yahweh blesses will possess the land,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he will destroy those whom he has cursed.

<verse eid="PSA 37:22"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 37:23"/>Yahweh directs a person to live securely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he is pleased with how that person lives.
<verse eid="PSA 37:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 37:24"/>Even if something bad happens to that person, he will not completely fail,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because Yahweh takes care of him.

<verse eid="PSA 37:24"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 37:25"/>I have been young, and now I am old,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but {in all those years} I have never seen Yahweh stop caring for any person who does what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">nor have I seen such a person’s children {needing to} beg for food.
<verse eid="PSA 37:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 37:26"/>People who do what is right are generous and lend freely {to others} every day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their children bless others.

<verse eid="PSA 37:26"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 37:27"/>Avoid doing evil and do what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do that, you {and your descendants} will live in the land forever.
<verse eid="PSA 37:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 37:28"/>Indeed, Yahweh loves it when people do what is just,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will never stop caring for those who are faithful to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will protect them forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he will destroy the descendants of wicked people.

<verse eid="PSA 37:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 37:29"/>People who do what is right will possess the land {that Yahweh gives them}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will live there forever.

<verse eid="PSA 37:29"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 37:30"/>People who do what is right speak wisely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they say what is just.
<verse eid="PSA 37:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 37:31"/>They continually think about the instructions that their God gave to them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they succeed in living {the way that God wants them to live}.

<verse eid="PSA 37:31"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 37:32"/>Wicked people observe people who do what is right
</para>
  <para style="q2">and look for ways to kill them.
<verse eid="PSA 37:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 37:33"/>But Yahweh will keep protecting them from what the wicked people want to do to them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will not let a judge {wrongly} condemn the people who do what is right.

<verse eid="PSA 37:33"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 37:34"/>Patiently rely on Yahweh {to help you} and obey what he commands.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{If you do that,} he will honor you by giving you the land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When God destroys the wicked people, you will see it happen.
<verse eid="PSA 37:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 37:35"/>I once saw a wicked and tyrannical person who was becoming powerful, like a large tree that was spreading out its branches over its native soil.
<verse eid="PSA 37:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 37:36"/>But then he passed away! Suddenly, he was gone!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I looked for him, but he was not there.

<verse eid="PSA 37:36"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 37:37"/>Observe {and imitate} people who are honest and who live rightly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because people who live peacefully will have a long life.
<verse eid="PSA 37:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 37:38"/>But Yahweh will destroy all people who rebel against him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will make the lives of wicked people short.

<verse eid="PSA 37:38"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 37:39"/>Yahweh saves people who do what is right;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he protects them when bad things are happening.
<verse eid="PSA 37:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 37:40"/>Yahweh helps them and rescues them
</para>
  <para style="q2">from {what} wicked people {want to do to them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He saves them because they have trusted in him {to help them}.


<verse eid="PSA 37:40"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 37"/>
  <chapter number="38" style="c" sid="PSA 38"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">
</para>
  <para style="q2">no, please do not punish me wrathfully.
<verse eid="PSA 37:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 38:2"/>{I feel as though} you have shot arrows into me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that you have struck me with your hand.
<verse eid="PSA 38:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 38:3"/>Because you are so angry with me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my whole body suffers.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My body is restless
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I have sinned.

<verse eid="PSA 38:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 38:4"/>Indeed, all my sins {are like flood waters that} rise above my head;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are like a heavy load that is too much for me to bear.
<verse eid="PSA 38:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 38:5"/>Because I have acted foolishly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have sores that keep getting worse and stink.
<verse eid="PSA 38:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 38:6"/>My body is twisted and bent over very low.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I go around sad and grieving constantly.
<verse eid="PSA 38:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 38:7"/>This is because there is a fever inside me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my whole body is sick.

<verse eid="PSA 38:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 38:8"/>I am exhausted and feel completely broken.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I moan loudly because I feel so distressed.

<verse eid="PSA 38:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 38:9"/>Lord, you know everything that I long for,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you hear every time that I sigh.
<verse eid="PSA 38:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 38:10"/>My heart beats rapidly and I am very weak.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even my eyesight is failing me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 38:11"/>My friends and the people I love keep away from me because of my disease;
</para>
  <para style="q2">even my own family stays far away from me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 38:12"/>Those who want to kill me set traps for me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and those who want to harm me talk about how to destroy me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they constantly plot how they will deceive me.
<verse eid="PSA 38:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 38:13"/>But I act like someone who is deaf, and I do not listen {to them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I act like someone who cannot speak, and I say nothing {to them}.
<verse eid="PSA 38:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 38:14"/>I have become like a man who cannot hear
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who cannot argue back.
<verse eid="PSA 38:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 38:15"/>{This is} because I wait for you, Yahweh{, to help me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will be the one who will respond, Lord my God.
<verse eid="PSA 38:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 38:16"/>{I know this} because I prayed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Do not let my enemies celebrate over me. Do not let them gloat over me if something bad happens to me.”

<verse eid="PSA 38:16"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 38:17"/>Indeed, I feel that something bad will soon happen,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am constantly in pain.
<verse eid="PSA 38:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 38:18"/>Certainly, I confess all the wrong things that I have done;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I feel terrible about my sin.
<verse eid="PSA 38:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 38:19"/>But my vigorous enemies are powerful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there are many people who hate me for no reason.
<verse eid="PSA 38:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 38:20"/>When I do good things for people, some of them do evil things to me in return.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Those people accuse me {of doing evil things}, even though I am trying to do what is right.

<verse eid="PSA 38:20"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 38:21"/>Yahweh, please do not leave me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">My God, please stay near me!
<verse eid="PSA 38:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 38:22"/>Come quickly to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lord, you who save me!


<verse eid="PSA 38:22"/><verse eid="PSA 38:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 38"/>
  <chapter number="39" style="c" sid="PSA 39"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: David wrote this song. Perform in the style of Jeduthun.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 39:1"/>I thought to myself, “I must be very careful about how I act
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I do not sin by what I say.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I must keep myself from speaking
</para>
  <para style="q2">while wicked people are near me.”
<verse eid="PSA 39:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 39:2"/>So I kept completely silent; I did not say anything, not even anything good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but my suffering only became worse.
<verse eid="PSA 39:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 39:3"/>I felt very agitated inside me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the more I pondered, the more agonized I became.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then finally I spoke and said,

<verse eid="PSA 39:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 39:4"/>“Yahweh, let me know when I will die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Tell me how many days I have left to live.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Help me to understand how short my life really is.
<verse eid="PSA 39:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 39:5"/>Indeed, you have made my days very few;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the time that I have to live is practically nothing to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Truly, every person appears and disappears as quickly as vapor.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 39:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 39:6"/>Truly, each person does not do anything more substantial than a shadow would do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Truly, people become agitated about things that do not matter.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They pile up {wealth}, but they do not know
</para>
  <para style="q2">who will get it {after they die}.
<verse eid="PSA 39:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 39:7"/>So now, Lord, I realize that it is useless for me to expect any person to make my life purposeful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are the only one who can do anything worthwhile for me.
<verse eid="PSA 39:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 39:8"/>Please save me from all the ways that I sin against you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not let me be someone whom foolish people ridicule.
<verse eid="PSA 39:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 39:9"/>I kept silent and did not say anything,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because {I knew that} you were the one who caused {me to suffer}.
<verse eid="PSA 39:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 39:10"/>{But now,} please stop punishing me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">As for me, because you have afflicted me, I am about to die.
<verse eid="PSA 39:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 39:11"/>When you correct a person for the wrong things that he has done,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you destroy what he treasures, just as moths destroy clothing.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Truly, every person lives only a very short time.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 39:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 39:12"/>Yahweh, please hear me as I pray {to you}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and listen {to me} when I cry out for help.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not ignore my tears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am only living before you {on the earth} for a short time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a temporary resident, just like all of my ancestors.
<verse eid="PSA 39:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 39:13"/>Please leave me alone in order that I may be happy {for awhile}
</para>
  <para style="q2">before I die.”


<verse eid="PSA 39:13"/><verse eid="PSA 39:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 39"/>
  <chapter number="40" style="c" sid="PSA 40"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">A note for the worship leader: David wrote this psalm.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 40:1"/>I patiently waited for Yahweh {to help me,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he was attentive to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and listened when I called out to him.
<verse eid="PSA 40:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 40:2"/>When bad things were happening to me, it was as though I was in a dangerous pit
</para>
  <para style="q2">that was full of mud and slime
</para>
  <para style="q1">but he rescued me from those terrible things
</para>
  <para style="q2">as though he had lifted me out of the pit and set me onto a solid rock
</para>
  <para style="q2">where I could stand securely.
<verse eid="PSA 40:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 40:3"/>He gave me reason to sing a new song,
</para>
  <para style="q2">praising him, our God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Many people will see {what he did for me} and will revere him
</para>
  <para style="q2">and will trust in Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 40:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 40:4"/>What a good life the person has
</para>
  <para style="q2">who trusts confidently in Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q1">and does not imitate proud people
</para>
  <para style="q2">who are loyal to what is false.
<verse eid="PSA 40:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 40:5"/>Yahweh my God, you are the one who has done many wonderful things
</para>
  <para style="q2">and made {great} plans for us!
</para>
  <para style="q1">No one compares to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If I tried to tell others about all of those wonderful things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">there would be too many for me to mention.

<verse eid="PSA 40:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 40:6"/>It is not the sacrifices and offerings that you have wanted {from me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">instead, you gave me the ability to hear and obey you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Burnt offerings and sin offerings are not what you require {to forgive my sins}.
<verse eid="PSA 40:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 40:7"/>So I said, “Yahweh, here I am,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{ready to do the things that} the scroll of your instruction says about me.”
<verse eid="PSA 40:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 40:8"/>My God, I gladly do what you desire;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I deeply treasure your instruction.

<verse eid="PSA 40:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 40:9"/>Whenever your people gather together in the large congregation,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I tell them about the righteous things {that you do}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, Yahweh, certainly you know that I do not stop talking {about this}.
<verse eid="PSA 40:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 40:10"/>I have not kept to myself {the good news} that you are righteous;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have told the large gathering of your people that you are faithful and that you save us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have not hidden from them that you faithfully love us and are always trustworthy.

<verse eid="PSA 40:10"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 40:11"/>Yahweh, you will not stop being merciful to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you faithfully love me and are always trustworthy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I know that} you will continually protect me.
<verse eid="PSA 40:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 40:12"/>I assure myself of this because so many bad things are happening to me that it seems that I cannot even count them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">the wrong things that I have done are now affecting me badly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I cannot see {a way to fix them}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">It seems that they are more numerous than the hairs on my head,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am very discouraged.

<verse eid="PSA 40:12"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 40:13"/>Yahweh, please rescue me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, please come quickly to help me!
<verse eid="PSA 40:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 40:14"/>May God completely disgrace
</para>
  <para style="q2">all of the people who want to kill me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May God frustrate the people who want me to suffer
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may he humiliate them.
<verse eid="PSA 40:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 40:15"/>May those who mock me, saying, “Ha, Ha!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">feel horrified because God has so humiliated them.
<verse eid="PSA 40:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 40:16"/>May all those who come to worship you
</para>
  <para style="q2">be very joyful because of you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May those who love that you save them say continually,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Yahweh is great!”

<verse eid="PSA 40:16"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 40:17"/>As for me, I am very poor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the Lord cares about me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are the one who rescues me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God, please do not wait any longer!


<verse eid="PSA 40:17"/><verse eid="PSA 40:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 40"/>
  <chapter number="41" style="c" sid="PSA 41"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">Note for the worship leader: David wrote this psalm.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 41:1"/>What a good life those people have who help powerless people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">When bad things happen to them, Yahweh will rescue them.
<verse eid="PSA 41:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 41:2"/>Yahweh will protect them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people will see that things turn our well for them as they live in the land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Yahweh,} please do not let their enemies do what they want with them.
<verse eid="PSA 41:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 41:3"/>Yahweh will strengthen them when they are sick;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Yahweh,} you completely restore them whenever they become ill.
<verse eid="PSA 41:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 41:4"/>As for me, I said, “Yahweh, please be merciful to me and heal me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I am sick} because I have sinned against you.”
<verse eid="PSA 41:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 41:5"/>My enemies say hateful things about me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they say, “We want him to die so that everyone will forget him!”
<verse eid="PSA 41:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 41:6"/>Whenever one of them comes to visit {me}, he says things that mean nothing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He secretly collects harmful information,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then he goes outside and tells {it to everyone}.
<verse eid="PSA 41:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 41:7"/>Everyone who hates me whispers about me to one another;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they plot how to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 41:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 41:8"/>{They say about me,} “Something terrible has happened to him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will never get up from where he is lying.”
<verse eid="PSA 41:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 41:9"/>Even my closest friend, the one I trusted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who shared meals with me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">has greatly betrayed me.
<verse eid="PSA 41:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 41:10"/>However, Yahweh, please be merciful to me and make me well,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I can do to them what they did to me.
<verse eid="PSA 41:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 41:11"/>When you do this, I will know that you are pleased with me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when my enemies {will not be able to defeat me and so} cannot rejoice about it.
<verse eid="PSA 41:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 41:12"/>As for me, you have helped me because I live honestly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you will allow me to be with you forever.
<verse eid="PSA 41:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 41:13"/>We should all praise Yahweh, the God whom the people of Israel worship!
</para>
  <para style="q2">People should praise him at all times, now and forever!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, let it be so!


<verse eid="PSA 41:13"/><verse eid="PSA 41:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 41"/>
  <chapter number="42" style="c" sid="PSA 42"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Two

</para>
  <para style="m"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 42:1"/>When a wild deer is very thirsty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it takes short, quick breaths because it wants so badly
</para>
  <para style="q2">to find a brook from which it can drink water.
</para>
  <para style="q1">That is how much I want you, God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if I am taking short, quick breaths.
<verse eid="PSA 42:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 42:2"/>You are the only true God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I desire very greatly to be in your temple again
</para>
  <para style="q2">and worship in your presence.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I desire that so much
</para>
  <para style="q2">that it is as if I am very thirsty.
<verse eid="PSA 42:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 42:3"/>I have been crying continually.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have been crying so much that I have not been able to eat.
</para>
  <para style="q1">This is because my enemies keep telling me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Your God will certainly not help you!”
<verse eid="PSA 42:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 42:4"/>It is appropriate for me to weep to express my great sorrow.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But {to encourage myself,} I should also remember
</para>
  <para style="q1">how I used to go with large groups of people
</para>
  <para style="q2">to celebrate festivals at God’s temple.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{Because I was one of the worship musicians,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">I would lead the people as they walked to the temple.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{On the way there,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">we all shouted joyfully and praised God.
<verse eid="PSA 42:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 42:5"/>So I certainly should not be so sad and upset!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I can confidently expect God to rescue me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">When he does, I will have the opportunity
</para>
  <para style="q2">to praise him as my savior and
<verse eid="PSA 42:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 42:6"/>my God. But I do feel very sad.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So {even though I am a long distance from your temple, God}
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will remember you from here at Mount Mizar
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the land near Mount Hermon where the Jordan River begins.
<verse eid="PSA 42:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 42:7"/>The waterfalls you created make such a loud sound
</para>
  <para style="q2">that it is as if one deep stream were shouting to another deep stream within the river.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I feel such anguish that it is as if
</para>
  <para style="q2">one wave after another were crashing over me.
<verse eid="PSA 42:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 42:8"/>Yahweh continually loves me faithfully as he promised.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In response, as he inspires me, I continually sing prayers to him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the God who keeps me alive.
<verse eid="PSA 42:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 42:9"/>God is like a huge rock on top of which I am safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So I will pray to him,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“Please pay attention to me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am living sorrowfully because my enemies are afflicting me!”
<verse eid="PSA 42:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 42:10"/>Those enemies are continually insulting me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They keep telling me, “Your God will certainly not help you!”
</para>
  <para style="q1">When they insult me like that,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is as painful as if they were breaking my bones.
<verse eid="PSA 42:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 42:11"/>But I certainly should not be so sad and upset!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I can confidently expect God to rescue me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">When he does, I will have the opportunity
</para>
  <para style="q2">to praise him as my savior and my God.


<verse eid="PSA 42:11"/><verse eid="PSA 42:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 42"/>
  <chapter number="43" style="c" sid="PSA 43"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 43:1"/>Please protect me, God, from the people who are being so cruel to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please consider that I do not deserve that.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Rescue me from people who would deceive me and treat me unfairly.
<verse eid="PSA 43:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 43:2"/>{I ask you to do this} because you are the God who protects me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and yet I feel as if you have abandoned me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am living sorrowfully because my enemies are afflicting me.
<verse eid="PSA 43:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 43:3"/>Treat me favorably, as if you were smiling at me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Help me, as you have promised to do for those who are loyal to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Guide me so that I can return
</para>
  <para style="q2">to your temple on Mount Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 43:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 43:4"/>{When I do come to Zion,} I will go to your altar {to worship you}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">O God, you make me very joyful!
{At your altar,} I will sing praise to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the God whom I worship, as I play the harp.
<verse eid="PSA 43:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 43:5"/>So I certainly should not be so sad and upset!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I can confidently expect God to rescue me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">When he does, I will have the opportunity
</para>
  <para style="q2">to praise him as my savior and my God.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 43:5"/><verse eid="PSA 43:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 43"/>
  <chapter number="44" style="c" sid="PSA 44"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 44:1"/>God, we listened carefully when our ancestors told us
</para>
  <para style="q2">about the great things you did long ago
</para>
  <para style="q2">when the Israelites first came into the land of Canaan.
<verse eid="PSA 44:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 44:2"/>{They told us about} how powerfully you forced the other nations to leave
</para>
  <para style="q2">and established our ancestors securely in their land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It was as if they had been plants that you put firmly in the ground.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You destroyed the people groups that had lived there
</para>
  <para style="q2">and enabled our ancestors to settle there.
<verse eid="PSA 44:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 44:3"/>Our ancestors did not conquer this land with their own weapons
</para>
  <para style="q2">or by their own power.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Instead, you helped them and defeated their enemies
</para>
  <para style="q2">by your own great power.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You did that because you loved them.
<verse eid="PSA 44:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 44:4"/>You are our real king, O God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please enable the people of Israel to defeat their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 44:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 44:5"/>You enable us to defeat our enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you help us, we destroy armies that fight against us.
<verse eid="PSA 44:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 44:6"/>We do not expect to win victories
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of the weapons we have.
<verse eid="PSA 44:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 44:7"/>Instead, you rescue us from our enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You disgrace our opponents {by defeating them}.
<verse eid="PSA 44:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 44:8"/>We regularly celebrate what God has done for us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We will always praise him.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 44:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 44:9"/>But now it appears that you no longer want to help us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This has embarrassed us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When our armies march out to fight a battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you no longer enable them to win victories.
<verse eid="PSA 44:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 44:10"/>You make us retreat from our enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We must leave behind weapons and possessions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they take as many of those as they want.
<verse eid="PSA 44:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 44:11"/>You have allowed our enemies to slaughter us as if we were sheep.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Foreign armies have captured many of our people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and taken them back to their countries as slaves.
<verse eid="PSA 44:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 44:12"/>You did not even receive any money
</para>
  <para style="q2">for allowing others to take your people as their slaves.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You did not become any richer
</para>
  <para style="q2">as a result of that.
<verse eid="PSA 44:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 44:13"/>Because you no longer help us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the people groups around us insult us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They express contempt for us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and laugh at us.
<verse eid="PSA 44:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 44:14"/>People in other nations are using us Israelites
</para>
  <para style="q2">as an example of an unfortunate people group.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They are shaking their heads at us
</para>
  <para style="q2">to ridicule us.
<verse eid="PSA 44:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 44:15"/>I am constantly aware of my disgrace.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I feel complete shame
<verse eid="PSA 44:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 44:16"/>because people are speaking so harshly to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Those people are my enemies, and they want to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 44:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 44:17"/>These things have happened to us
</para>
  <para style="q2">even though we have not stopped worshiping you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we have not disobeyed the solemn agreement that you made with our ancestors.
<verse eid="PSA 44:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 44:18"/>We still love you as our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we have continued to do what you have commanded us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 44:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 44:19"/>But {you have allowed} our enemies to ruin our land and leave it desolate.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have left us feeling as though we are going to die.
<verse eid="PSA 44:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 44:20"/>If we had stopped worshiping you as our God
</para>
  <para style="q2">and had started worshiping a foreign god,
<verse eid="PSA 44:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 44:21"/>you would surely have known that.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That is because you know even what people secretly think.
<verse eid="PSA 44:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 44:22"/>Because you are not helping us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">our enemies are continuing to kill our people.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They believe they can kill us
</para>
  <para style="q2">as easily as if we were sheep,
</para>
  <para style="q2">which people slaughter easily.
<verse eid="PSA 44:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 44:23"/>Protect us! Do not fail to act, Lord, as if you were asleep!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Defend us! Do not keep treating us as if we were not your people!
<verse eid="PSA 44:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 44:24"/>Please be favorable to us and help us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Consider how badly our enemies are harming us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and how greatly we are suffering!
<verse eid="PSA 44:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 44:25"/>We ask you to do this because we are helpless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if we had fallen down
</para>
  <para style="q2">and were lying on the ground and could not get up.
<verse eid="PSA 44:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 44:26"/>You have promised to love us faithfully because we belong to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So please do something to rescue us from our enemies!


<verse eid="PSA 44:26"/><verse eid="PSA 44:26"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 44"/>
  <chapter number="45" style="c" sid="PSA 45"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this song. It is a love song. The tune is “Lilies.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 45:1"/>There is something wonderful that I feel so strongly about that I must sing about it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing a song that I have composed in honor of the king.
</para>
  <para style="q1">As I sing, I will express my ideas in an orderly and complete way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just like a scribe who records quickly and accurately what he hears people say.
<verse eid="PSA 45:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 45:2"/>O King, you are the most handsome man in the world!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You speak very graciously!
</para>
  <para style="q1">So we know that God has always blessed you.
<verse eid="PSA 45:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 45:3"/>Prepare yourself to keep fighting powerfully {for justice}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are glorious and majestic when you do that.
<verse eid="PSA 45:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 45:4"/>Go and win victories to establish yourself as a king who is honest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who does not proudly oppress his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who does what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q1">As you do that, may you find that your skill as a warrior
</para>
  <para style="q2">terrifies anyone who would resist you.
<verse eid="PSA 45:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 45:5"/>Your sharp arrows pierce into the hearts of your enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You defeat the people groups that fight against you.
<verse eid="PSA 45:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 45:6"/>Your Majesty, you will be the king for a very long time.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You decide people’s cases fairly as you rule your kingdom.
<verse eid="PSA 45:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 45:7"/>You love it when people do what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you hate it when people do what is wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q1">That is why God, whom you worship, has made you so happy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are happier than all the people around you.
<verse eid="PSA 45:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 45:8"/>Your royal robes smell beautifully of {the spices} myrrh, aloes, and cassia.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From within your palace, which has ivory decorations,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you hear people playing stringed instruments.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That music makes you happy.
<verse eid="PSA 45:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 45:9"/>The honored women of your court include foreign princesses.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Your bride,} the queen, is standing at your right side.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Threads of gold fine gold from Ophir
</para>
  <para style="q2">decorate her robe.
<verse eid="PSA 45:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 45:10"/>And as for you, dear bride,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please listen carefully to my advice.
</para>
  <para style="q1">From now on, regard this as your country
</para>
  <para style="q2">and these people as your family.
<verse eid="PSA 45:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 45:11"/>If you do that, the king will love and appreciate you even more.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Bow down in front of him to honor him as your husband and king.
<verse eid="PSA 45:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 45:12"/>Representatives of {foreign kingdoms such as the wealthy kingdom} of Tyre will bring gifts to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The wealthy people of this kingdom will ask you to treat them favorably.
<verse eid="PSA 45:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 45:13"/>This royal princess looked so beautiful in her private room where she had dressed for the wedding!
</para>
  <para style="q2">She had put on a robe that gold threads richly decorated.
<verse eid="PSA 45:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 45:14"/>As she came in procession to where you are, O king,
</para>
  <para style="q2">people could see that her robe also had beautiful designs of colored thread.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Other young women, her bridesmaids,
</para>
  <para style="q2">followed her in that procession.
<verse eid="PSA 45:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 45:15"/>As they came in procession into your palace,
</para>
  <para style="q2">this made everyone very happy.
<verse eid="PSA 45:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 45:16"/>You will be famous not because of your ancestors but because of your descendants.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will have influence and authority all over the world.
<verse eid="PSA 45:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 45:17"/>{By this song,} I want to make the people of future generations remember what a great king you are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then people will always say good things about you.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 45:17"/><verse eid="PSA 45:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 45"/>
  <chapter number="46" style="c" sid="PSA 46"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this song. The tune is “Maidens.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 46:1"/>God keeps us safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if he were a secure place where we could go if we were in danger.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God strengthens us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is always present to help us when we have troubles.
<verse eid="PSA 46:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 46:2"/>So we would not be afraid even if there were an earthquake
</para>
  <para style="q2">that caused huge chunks of mountains to fall deep into the sea.
<verse eid="PSA 46:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 46:3"/>We would not be afraid even if there were a great storm in the ocean
</para>
  <para style="q2">whose surging waves battered the coastline.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 46:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 46:4"/>A stream flows down from the mountains into Jerusalem.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Its cool waters refresh the people who live there.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Jerusalem is the location of God’s holy temple.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is greater than all other spirit beings.
<verse eid="PSA 46:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 46:5"/>God is present in Jerusalem in a special way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so no one destroys it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God rescues the people of that city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it is as if a dark night ends and a bright new day begins.
<verse eid="PSA 46:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 46:6"/>Sometimes foreign armies invade kingdoms and conquer them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{But that does not happen to us, because} God powerfully defends us and defeats our enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 46:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 46:7"/>Yahweh, the commander of the heavenly armies, helps us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The God whom we Israelites worship keeps us safe.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 46:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 46:8"/>Let me tell you what Yahweh does.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He destroys our enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 46:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 46:9"/>He stops wars all over the world.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if he breaks bows and arrows, destroys spears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and burns up war wagons.
<verse eid="PSA 46:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 46:10"/>God says, “Calm down and remember that I am God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The people of nations throughout the earth will honor me.”
<verse eid="PSA 46:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 46:11"/>Yahweh, the commander of the heavenly armies, helps us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The God whom we Israelites worship keeps us safe.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 46:11"/><verse eid="PSA 46:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 46"/>
  <chapter number="47" style="c" sid="PSA 47"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 47:1"/>People all over the world, clap your hands!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Shout joyfully to praise God!
<verse eid="PSA 47:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 47:2"/>Everyone should revere Yahweh, who is much greater than any other spirit being.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He rules powerfully over the whole world!
<verse eid="PSA 47:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 47:3"/>He enables us to conquer people groups that oppose us.
<verse eid="PSA 47:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 47:4"/>He loved our ancestor Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so he chose this land to be our possession.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We are proud of the land he gave us.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 47:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 47:5"/>People have acclaimed Yahweh their God as their king
</para>
  <para style="q2">by shouting and blowing ram’s horns.
<verse eid="PSA 47:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 47:6"/>Sing songs to praise God our King!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, sing songs to praise him!
<verse eid="PSA 47:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 47:7"/>Do that because God rules the whole world.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Sing a special song about that.
<verse eid="PSA 47:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 47:8"/>God rules over all people groups.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He rules them completely fairly, not the way many human kings do.
<verse eid="PSA 47:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 47:9"/>The rulers of the people groups will assemble
</para>
  <para style="q2">to join those who worship the same God whom Abraham worshiped.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They will do that because the leaders of the world must obey God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the supreme ruler of the world.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 47:9"/><verse eid="PSA 47:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 47"/>
  <chapter number="48" style="c" sid="PSA 48"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">One of the Korahites wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 48:1"/>Yahweh is great, and he deserves to have people praise him greatly
</para>
  <para style="q2">in {Jerusalem}, the city that belongs to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">That city is high up on the mountain that he chose
</para>
  <para style="q2">as the place where people would worship him.
<verse eid="PSA 48:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 48:2"/>The height of Mount Zion is magnificent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People from all over the world are happy when they see it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The city {of Jerusalem,} where Yahweh rules as the great king,
</para>
  <para style="q2">is on the northern ridge of that mountain.
<verse eid="PSA 48:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 48:3"/>God is present {as a defender} in the city’s fortifications.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He has shown that he protects the people of the city.
<verse eid="PSA 48:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 48:4"/>Listen to why Yahweh deserves our praise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Kings joined together and led their armies to attack our city.
<verse eid="PSA 48:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 48:5"/>However, when they saw it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">its secure position and defenses amazed them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They became so frightened
</para>
  <para style="q2">that they ran away.
<verse eid="PSA 48:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 48:6"/>Their bodies shook because they were so afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They screamed as if they were women who were giving birth.
<verse eid="PSA 48:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 48:7"/>Just as you, Yahweh, can sent a strong east wind
</para>
  <para style="q2">that wrecks even the sturdiest ships at sea{,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so you destroyed the armies
</para>
  <para style="q2">that were attacking us}.
<verse eid="PSA 48:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 48:8"/>Jerusalem belongs to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the commander of the heavenly armies, who is our God.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We had heard {from our ancestors} that God would always keep the city secure.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Now we who live in the city have seen for ourselves that this is true.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 48:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 48:9"/>We went into your temple, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and recognized that you faithfully kept your covenant when you protected us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We acknowledged that you had been just as faithful to us
</para>
  <para style="q2">as you were to our ancestors.
<verse eid="PSA 48:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 48:10"/>People throughout the world praise you as you deserve.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You use your power to make sure that people treat each other right.
<verse eid="PSA 48:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 48:11"/>The people who live in Jerusalem and in other parts of the kingdom of Judah
</para>
  <para style="q2">should celebrate the way you judge people fairly.
<verse eid="PSA 48:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 48:12"/>You Judeans should walk around the walls of the city of Jerusalem.
</para>
  <para style="q2">See how many defensive towers it has!
<verse eid="PSA 48:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 48:13"/>You should observe the strength of the walls and the fortifications
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that you can tell your descendants about them.
<verse eid="PSA 48:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 48:14"/>The people of Judah and Jerusalem should praise Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he is our God and he will always be our God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will lead us for as long as we live.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 48:14"/><verse eid="PSA 48:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 48"/>
  <chapter number="49" style="c" sid="PSA 49"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 49:1"/>Listen to me, members of people groups
</para>
  <para style="q2">from throughout the world,
<verse eid="PSA 49:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 49:2"/>whether or not you are famous
</para>
  <para style="q2">and whether or not you are rich!
<verse eid="PSA 49:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 49:3"/>I have thought carefully about what I am going to say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so it will be wise, and it will help you understand things better.
<verse eid="PSA 49:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 49:4"/>There is a popular saying about something that people find difficult to understand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have considered it, and I will explain it as I {sing and} play my harp.
<verse eid="PSA 49:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 49:5"/>I do not have to be afraid during difficult times
</para>
  <para style="q2">when wicked people around me try to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 49:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 49:6"/>These wicked people believe that they will be able to use their money to overcome any difficulty.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They boast about how rich they are.
<verse eid="PSA 49:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 49:7"/>No one can use his money to keep a person from dying.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No, no one can pay God money so that another person will not die.
<verse eid="PSA 49:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 49:8"/>No matter how much money a person has,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is never enough to keep someone else from dying
<verse eid="PSA 49:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 49:9"/>so that the person will live forever
</para>
  <para style="q2">and never leave this world.
<verse eid="PSA 49:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 49:10"/>Whether people are wise or foolish and brutish, they all die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then other people inherit their money.
<verse eid="PSA 49:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 49:11"/>They imagine that the houses they live in will always exist.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They call their properties by their own names
</para>
  <para style="q2">{as if they would always have them}.
<verse eid="PSA 49:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 49:12"/>Even if someone is great, he does not stay that way.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He still dies, just as animals do.
<verse eid="PSA 49:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 49:13"/>Those who think and act as if they will never die are living in a foolish manner.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even so, some other people admire them and approve of what they say.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 49:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 49:14"/>God has determined that they will die, as easily as sheep die,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and go to the place where dead people are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will remain there, as if death were a shepherd keeping them in a pen.
</para>
  <para style="q1">One day God will make righteous people rule over wicked people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wicked people will no longer live in comfortable homes.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Instead, their bodies will decay in their graves.
<verse eid="PSA 49:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 49:15"/>But God will take me to himself.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In that way, he will rescue me from the place where dead people are.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 49:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 49:16"/>Do not let it trouble you when a person becomes rich
</para>
  <para style="q2">and has many valuable possessions.
<verse eid="PSA 49:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 49:17"/>After all, when that person dies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will take nothing with him {to the place where dead people are}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will not be able to bring his money there with him.
<verse eid="PSA 49:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 49:18"/>While a rich person is alive, he says to himself that he is successful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">(People tend to praise anyone who is successful.)
<verse eid="PSA 49:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 49:19"/>Nevertheless, he will die and go to where his dead ancestors are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of them will remain in that dark place forever.
<verse eid="PSA 49:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 49:20"/>If someone is great but does not understand these things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will die, just as animals do.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 49:20"/><verse eid="PSA 49:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 49"/>
  <chapter number="50" style="c" sid="PSA 50"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 50:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh is the only true God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He has decreed that people from all over the world
</para>
  <para style="q2">should come to him.
<verse eid="PSA 50:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 50:2"/>Mount Zion is as wonderful as a place can be {because God’s temple is there}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God’s presence there is like a light that shines brightly.
<verse eid="PSA 50:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 50:3"/>Our God is approaching us {to judge us}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will now tell us {what we have done right and what we have done wrong}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He is coming very powerfully, as he did at Mount Sinai,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when there was a great thunderstorm and a burning fire on the mountain as he approached it.
<verse eid="PSA 50:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 50:4"/>He calls upon the sky and the land {to serve as witnesses of his covenant with the Israelites}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This demonstrates that he will judge them fairly {according to that covenant}.
<verse eid="PSA 50:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 50:5"/>He says, “Summon those who worship me faithfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those who made a covenant with me
</para>
  <para style="q2">that involved offering sacrifices to me.”
<verse eid="PSA 50:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 50:6"/>The sky displays the character of God so clearly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is as though it is saying,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“God is righteous, and he is the supreme judge.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 50:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 50:7"/>God says, “You Israelite people who belong to me, listen as I speak to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am the God whom you worship. I am going to tell you what you have done right and what you have done wrong.
<verse eid="PSA 50:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 50:8"/>You continually burn animals completely on the temple altar as sacrifices to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I have no complaint that you have failed to offer sacrifices to me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 50:9"/>However, I do not really need the bulls from your herds
</para>
  <para style="q2">or the goats from your pens {that you sacrifice to me}.
<verse eid="PSA 50:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 50:10"/>I do not need them, because all of the animals that live in the forests belong to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of the cattle everywhere on earth also belong to me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 50:11"/>I own all the birds that live in the mountains.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All the little creatures that move around in the fields also belong to me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 50:12"/>Because everything in the world belongs to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">if I were hungry, I would not tell you
</para>
  <para style="q2">{so that you would bring me some food to eat}.
<verse eid="PSA 50:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 50:13"/>When you sacrifice bulls to me, I do not eat their flesh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when you offer goats to me, I do not drink their blood.
<verse eid="PSA 50:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 50:14"/>I want you to offer sacrifices to me, your God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you have promised to do that to thank me for helping you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am the God who is greater than all other spirit beings.
<verse eid="PSA 50:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 50:15"/>So pray to me when you are in trouble.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do that, I will rescue you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then you will honor me {publicly by offering a sacrifice}.”
<verse eid="PSA 50:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 50:16"/>But God says to wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“You should not be reciting my commandments
</para>
  <para style="q2">or talking about the covenant that I made with you!
<verse eid="PSA 50:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 50:17"/>You should not do that, because you hate it when I correct you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when I tell you to do something, you refuse to obey me.
<verse eid="PSA 50:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 50:18"/>When you see someone stealing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you decide that it is acceptable for him to steal.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When you learn that people are having sexual relations with people other than their spouses,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you do the same thing.
<verse eid="PSA 50:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 50:19"/>You do not restrain yourselves from saying wicked things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you make up things to say to deceive people.
<verse eid="PSA 50:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 50:20"/>You consistently say bad things about members of your own family,
</para>
  <para style="q2">even about your closest relatives.
<verse eid="PSA 50:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 50:21"/>You do all those things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have not said anything to you about them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so you think that I do not care about them any more than you do.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But now I am going to show you {all the wicked things you have done},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am going to judge and punish you for doing them.
<verse eid="PSA 50:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 50:22"/>Many of you have been ignoring me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Pay attention to what I am saying now!
</para>
  <para style="q1">If you do not, I will destroy you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one will be able to rescue you.
<verse eid="PSA 50:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 50:23"/>When people publicly offer sacrifices to thank me for helping them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that honors me greatly.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If people live as I want people to live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will rescue them when they are in trouble.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 50:23"/><verse eid="PSA 50:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 50"/>
  <chapter number="51" style="c" sid="PSA 51"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: King David wrote this song after the prophet Nathan came and rebuked him for having sexual relations with {another man’s wife,} Bathsheba.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 51:1"/>Oh God, since you promised to faithfully love me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please act mercifully toward me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You gently love people in many ways,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please forgive me for disobeying you so badly.
<verse eid="PSA 51:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 51:2"/>Remove my sin completely, as if it were dirt that you were washing off me
</para>
  <para style="q2">to make me clean.
<verse eid="PSA 51:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 51:3"/>I ask this because I know that I have disobeyed you in many ways.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am continually aware of that.
<verse eid="PSA 51:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 51:4"/>What grieves me most is how I have sinned against you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have done things that you consider to be very wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q1">So when you declare that I am guilty, you are right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When you judge me, you are completely fair.
<verse eid="PSA 51:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 51:5"/>Indeed, I have been a sinner from birth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In fact, I have been a sinner since my mother conceived me.
<verse eid="PSA 51:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 51:6"/>I know that you want me to have honest intentions.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You help me understand very well how to act wisely.
<verse eid="PSA 51:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 51:7"/>Make me acceptable to you again,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if you were using hyssop to sprinkle water on me to purify me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Remove my sin as if it were dirt that you were washing off me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then I will be completely pure, like snow that has just fallen.
<verse eid="PSA 51:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 51:8"/>Please tell me {that you have forgiven me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That would make me very happy.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My guilt feels like a heavy weight on me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but may I rejoice {in your forgiveness}.
<verse eid="PSA 51:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 51:9"/>Please forgive all the wrong things I have done
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that it will be as if I never did them.
<verse eid="PSA 51:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 51:10"/>O God, please make me want to do only things that please you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Help me to be loyal to you consistently.
<verse eid="PSA 51:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 51:11"/>Please allow me to come into your presence.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do not make your Holy Spirit leave me.
<verse eid="PSA 51:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 51:12"/>Please save me {from the guilt and punishment of my sin}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That will make me very happy again.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Please make me eager to obey you
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I do not sin again.
<verse eid="PSA 51:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 51:13"/>Please make me so obedient that I can even teach people who are doing wrong things
</para>
  <para style="q2">how you want them to live instead.
</para>
  <para style="q1">That way people who have been disobeying you
</para>
  <para style="q2">will start obeying you again.
<verse eid="PSA 51:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 51:14"/>God, I admit that I deserve to die because I murdered someone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but please rescue me from that punishment.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You can save me {from the guilt and punishment of my sin} because you are God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When you do that, I will sing joyfully about how good you are.
<verse eid="PSA 51:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 51:15"/>Lord, {please do these things so that} I will have a reason to speak publicly
</para>
  <para style="q2">and say things to praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 51:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 51:16"/>If you had wanted me to offer a sacrifice {because of the sin I committed},
</para>
  <para style="q2">I would certainly have done that.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But you do not accept burnt offerings
</para>
  <para style="q2">{from people who bring them to try to make things right with you after committing murder}.
<verse eid="PSA 51:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 51:17"/>What you really want is for people to pray to you in genuine humility {and ask for forgiveness}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When a person is very sorrowful for his sin, you, God, do not reject him.
<verse eid="PSA 51:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 51:18"/>Please regard us Israelites favorably and help us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Protect us from our enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 51:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 51:19"/>Then people will offer sacrifices to you for the right reasons.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will bring animals that they will burn completely as offerings to you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They will completely burn up young bulls on your altar.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will gladly accept these sacrifices.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 51:19"/><verse eid="PSA 51:19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 51"/>
  <chapter number="52" style="c" sid="PSA 52"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song when Doeg the Edomite went to King Saul and told him, “David went to Ahimelech’s house.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 52:1"/>{Doeg,} you are boasting as if you were a great warrior because you killed so many people{,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you are wrong to boast, because they were helpless}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God always protects me because he is kind to me.
<verse eid="PSA 52:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 52:2"/>You say things that you know will cause great harm to other people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if your tongue is a sharp knife slashing people.
</para>
  <para style="q1">People did something innocently,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you reported it in such a way that they seemed to be guilty.
<verse eid="PSA 52:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 52:3"/>You like to do what is wrong more than you like to do what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You like to tell lies more than you like to tell the truth.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 52:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 52:4"/>You like to say anything that will cause harm to people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">What you say causes innocent people to suffer.
<verse eid="PSA 52:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 52:5"/>But God will destroy you permanently, just as you have destroyed others.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You may feel safe in your home, but God will take you from there
</para>
  <para style="q2">and remove you from this world in which people are alive.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 52:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 52:6"/>When good people see that, they will respect God {for being just}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will laugh at you.
<verse eid="PSA 52:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 52:7"/>{They will say,} “Look what happened to this man who did not trust God to protect him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He thought that because he had a lot of money, he could avoid trouble.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He believed that harming other people would make him powerful.”
<verse eid="PSA 52:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 52:8"/>But I am safe, just like the olive trees that the priests plant and care for in the courtyard of the place where we worship God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that God will always be kind to me.
<verse eid="PSA 52:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 52:9"/>I am confident that you, God, are going to do what I have described,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will always praise you for that.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You have demonstrated to the people who are faithful to you that you are good.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So I will wait patiently for you to act according to your good character.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 52:9"/><verse eid="PSA 52:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 52"/>
  <chapter number="53" style="c" sid="PSA 53"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song to the tune of “Weakness.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 53:1"/>People who do not want to obey God tell themselves that God does not exist.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People like that are bad. They do terrible things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Every one of them acts wickedly.
<verse eid="PSA 53:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 53:2"/>God looks down from heaven at the people on the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He wants to find out whether any of them are wise and want to know him.
<verse eid="PSA 53:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 53:3"/>But they have all chosen to disobey God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have all become bad people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Every single one of them acts wickedly.
<verse eid="PSA 53:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 53:4"/>They take away people’s possessions until they have nothing left.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do that as easily as they would eat a loaf of bread.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The people who do such bad things ought to realize {that God is going to punish them}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But they do not worship God.
<verse eid="PSA 53:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 53:5"/>An army came and attacked the Israelites.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Its soldiers did not have to be afraid that the Israelites would defeat them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But God made them lose in battle so badly that the survivors were not even able to bury the dead soldiers.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This made them very afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God regarded this army as insignificant {compared with his great power}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He helped} the Israelites{, and so they} were able to humiliate those soldiers {by defeating them}.
<verse eid="PSA 53:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 53:6"/>I wish that God, whose sanctuary is on Mount Zion, would rescue the Israelite people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">When God makes his people prosperous again, the Israelites, those descendants of Jacob, will be very happy.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 53:6"/><verse eid="PSA 53:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 53"/>
  <chapter number="54" style="c" sid="PSA 54"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Musicians playing stringed instruments should accompany this song. David wrote this song when the people of the region of Ziph went to Saul and told him that David was hiding in their area.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 54:1"/>God, please use your power to save me {from my enemies}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you do that, people will realize that I have not done anything wrong.
<verse eid="PSA 54:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 54:2"/>God, please listen to what I say
</para>
  <para style="q2">as I pray to you.
<verse eid="PSA 54:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 54:3"/>I am praying for your help because even my fellow Judeans are treacherously acting against me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">These are violent men, and they want to kill me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do not respect you.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 54:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 54:4"/>But God is helping me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The Lord is helping the people who are protecting me so that I stay alive.
<verse eid="PSA 54:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 54:5"/>My enemies want to do harmful things to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God will cause those things to happen to them instead.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Because you faithfully do what you promise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">destroy them {so that they do not kill me}!
<verse eid="PSA 54:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 54:6"/>I promise that {when you rescue me,} I will publicly offer a sacrifice to honor you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise you, Yahweh, for how good you are.
<verse eid="PSA 54:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 54:7"/>I will be able to do this because he rescues me from all my troubles
</para>
  <para style="q2">and, as a result, I see that he has defeated my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 54:7"/><verse eid="PSA 54:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 54"/>
  <chapter number="55" style="c" sid="PSA 55"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Musicians playing stringed instruments should accompany this song. David wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 55:1"/>God, please listen to me as I pray to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do not ignore me as I am pleading with you.
<verse eid="PSA 55:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 55:2"/>Please pay attention to me and do what I ask.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The things I am praying about are agitating me and making me moan {in distress}.
<verse eid="PSA 55:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 55:3"/>This is because my enemies are saying things {to threaten me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Wicked people are attacking me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They are causing me to have great troubles.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because they are so hostile to me, they never stop trying to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 55:4"/>My heart is pounding inside me because I am so upset.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I strongly feel many fears because I know that my enemies are trying to kill me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 55:5"/>I am shaking because I am so afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The only thing I feel is fear.
<verse eid="PSA 55:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 55:6"/>I have been thinking, “How good it would be if I had wings like a dove!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I would fly away and find a place to rest.
<verse eid="PSA 55:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 55:7"/>If I could, I would go far away
</para>
  <para style="q2">and stay in a desolate area.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 55:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 55:8"/>I would quickly find a safe place
</para>
  <para style="q2">where my enemies could not harm me in the way that a powerful storm causes damage.”
<verse eid="PSA 55:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 55:9"/>Lord, please destroy my enemies!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make them disagree about what to do {so that they cannot make successful plans against me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I ask this because I know that they are fighting with people in the city and hurting them.
<verse eid="PSA 55:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 55:10"/>The fighting is constant, and the people in the city cannot get away from it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Bad people are causing much trouble right in the middle of the city.
<verse eid="PSA 55:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 55:11"/>These bad people harm others right in the middle of the city.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Dishonest people continually deceive and cheat others in the marketplace.
<verse eid="PSA 55:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 55:12"/>If it were an enemy who was saying bad things about me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I could endure it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If it were someone who hated me who was powerfully opposing me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I could hide from him.
<verse eid="PSA 55:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 55:13"/>But the person who is doing those things to me is someone I treated not as a subject but as an equal.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I knew him well, and we were together often.
<verse eid="PSA 55:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 55:14"/>We used to talk together in a wonderful way.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We also used to go to the temple courtyard together {to worship God} with the other Israelites who gathered there.
<verse eid="PSA 55:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 55:15"/>My enemies are so wicked in their inner beings that it is as if wickedness lives in their homes {and influences what they do}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So I hope that bad things happen to them that destroy them!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I wish that {the earth would open up under them so that}
</para>
  <para style="q2">they would go down alive to the place where dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 55:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 55:16"/>But I will ask Yahweh, my God, to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will rescue me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 55:17"/>I will continually pray to him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">whether I can express my concerns in words
</para>
  <para style="q2">or whether I am only able to moan {as a plea to him}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He will answer my prayer by helping me.
<verse eid="PSA 55:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 55:18"/>My enemies are coming with many soldiers to fight against me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God will keep me safe and save my life when we fight a battle.
<verse eid="PSA 55:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 55:19"/>My enemies have no difficulties in life,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so they do not respect God.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

</para>
  <para style="q1">But God, who has ruled forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">will answer my prayer and punish them as they deserve.
<verse eid="PSA 55:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 55:20"/>The man I knew well is attacking me even though I was his friend.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He should have remained loyal to me, but he has not.
<verse eid="PSA 55:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 55:21"/>What he said was as easy to believe as butter is easy to swallow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but secretly he hated me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The words he spoke were as soothing as olive oil,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but all along he intended to use words to hurt people as sharp swords do.
<verse eid="PSA 55:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 55:22"/>Depend on Yahweh to help you when you are in trouble, and he will take care of you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will never allow anyone to destroy people who are righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 55:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 55:23"/>God, you will cause people who deceive and kill others
</para>
  <para style="q2">to die before they have lived half as long as most people do.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But as for me, I will trust you {to protect me}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 55:23"/><verse eid="PSA 55:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 55"/>
  <chapter number="56" style="c" sid="PSA 56"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song when the Philistines made him their prisoner in the city of Gath. The tune is “A Faraway Silent Dove.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 56:1"/>O God, men are attacking me, so please help me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They keep fighting me and making me suffer.
<verse eid="PSA 56:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 56:2"/>Many proud enemies are fighting against me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so there is continually someone attacking me.
<verse eid="PSA 56:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 56:3"/>But whenever I am afraid,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I trust you {to help me}.
<verse eid="PSA 56:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 56:4"/>I praise you, God, because you have promised {to take care of me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I trust you to do that, so I am not afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that mere humans will not be able to harm me!
<verse eid="PSA 56:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 56:5"/>My enemies are continually trying to interfere in my activities. They keep planning ways to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 56:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 56:6"/>Together they secretly watch where I am going
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they are looking for an opportunity to kill me.
<verse eid="PSA 56:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 56:7"/>They should not be able to avoid punishment for the wicked things they are doing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">O God, in your anger, please defeat all of our foreign enemies!
<verse eid="PSA 56:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 56:8"/>You have watched me carefully as I have wandered to this place.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please stay close to me as I have sad experiences here.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that you have watched me closely as I have had these experiences.
<verse eid="PSA 56:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 56:9"/>When I cry to God for help, my enemies will stop attacking me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that will happen because God favors me.
<verse eid="PSA 56:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 56:10"/>I praise you, Yahweh my God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you have promised {to take care of me}.
<verse eid="PSA 56:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 56:11"/>I trust you to do that, so I am not afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that mere humans will not be able to harm me!
<verse eid="PSA 56:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 56:12"/>God, I have vowed {that I will thank you publicly when you help me},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will offer a sacrifice to thank you.
<verse eid="PSA 56:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 56:13"/>I will be able to do that because you will have rescued me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one will have killed me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Because you protect me, I will be able to live in your presence
</para>
  <para style="q2">here in this world where people are alive.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 56:13"/><verse eid="PSA 56:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 56"/>
  <chapter number="57" style="c" sid="PSA 57"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song when he fled into a cave to escape from Saul. The tune is “Do Not Destroy.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 57:1"/>O God, please help me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I ask you to do that because I depend on you to protect me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I pray that you will protect me just as a mother bird protects her chicks under her wings.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I ask you to do that until the troubles I am having are over.
<verse eid="PSA 57:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 57:2"/>I am crying {for help} to God, who is greater than all other spirit beings.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God will complete what he has begun to do for me.
<verse eid="PSA 57:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 57:3"/>May he act from where he is in heaven to rescue me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Someone is trying to harm me; may God prevent him from doing that.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

</para>
  <para style="q1">God is kind and loyal to the people who trust him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so may he help me.
<verse eid="PSA 57:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 57:4"/>Men who are as dangerous as lions are all around me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have no safe place to sleep far away from those men who are trying to kill me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They say things about me that make other people want to harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 57:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 57:5"/>May you have the most glory, God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">of anyone in heaven or on earth!
<verse eid="PSA 57:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 57:6"/>My enemies are trying to capture me, as if they had set out a net to trap me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This has distressed me greatly.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yes, they are trying to capture me, as if they had dug a deep pit along the path where I walk, hoping that I would fall into it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But I believe that God will use what they are doing against them, as if they had fallen into that pit themselves.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 57:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 57:7"/>God, I trust you completely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So {instead of worrying,} I will sing praises to you.
<verse eid="PSA 57:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 57:8"/>I will do that enthusiastically.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will begin the day by praising you as I play my harp and lyre.
<verse eid="PSA 57:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 57:9"/>I will sing songs to praise you, Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that people of other nations can find out about you.
<verse eid="PSA 57:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 57:10"/>You deserve this praise because your kindness and loyalty are much greater than anything on earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as the clouds in the sky are much higher than anything on earth.
<verse eid="PSA 57:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 57:11"/>May you have the most glory, God, of anyone in heaven or on earth!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 57:11"/><verse eid="PSA 57:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 57"/>
  <chapter number="58" style="c" sid="PSA 58"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">Here is a note to the worship leader: The tune is “Do Not Destroy.” David wrote this song.

</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 58:1"/>You {judges} should not think that you can ensure justice if you do not speak out {to condemn wickedness}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are not judging cases fairly, and that shows that you are acting only as humans{, not as God’s representatives}.
<verse eid="PSA 58:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 58:2"/>In fact, you keep thinking about doing things that are wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The decisions that you make encourage people to commit violent crimes.
<verse eid="PSA 58:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 58:3"/>Wicked people do wrong things and tell lies
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the time when they are born.
<verse eid="PSA 58:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 58:4"/>Wicked people harm other people just as poisonous snakes harm people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They do not pay attention to God’s commandments, as if they were cobras that refused to listen
<verse eid="PSA 58:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 58:5"/>and so did not respond to the music that snake charmers were playing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even the most skillful charmer could not get them to respond to music.
<verse eid="PSA 58:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 58:6"/>Yahweh my God, wicked people are as dangerous as young lions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but destroy them as if you were breaking the large teeth of such lions.
<verse eid="PSA 58:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 58:7"/>Make them disappear like water that flows away.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When they try to harm people as if they were shooting arrows at them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">keep them from hurting those people, as if those arrows had no heads!
<verse eid="PSA 58:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 58:8"/>May they be like a snail that dissolves as it moves along.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May they be like a baby that never lives on earth because it dies before its mother gives birth to it.
<verse eid="PSA 58:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 58:9"/>God will punish and destroy them as powerfully as if a whirlwind were carrying them away.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will do that more quickly than thorns can catch fire and heat a pot, even if the thorns are dry, not fresh.
<verse eid="PSA 58:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 58:10"/>Righteous people will celebrate when they see God punish wicked people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It will be as if wicked people were an army that God destroyed
</para>
  <para style="q2">and righteous people were walking triumphantly through the battlefield afterwards.
<verse eid="PSA 58:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 58:11"/>Then people will say, “It is true that there is a reward for righteous people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is true that God judges fairly the people who live on the earth!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 58:11"/><verse eid="PSA 58:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 58"/>
  <chapter number="59" style="c" sid="PSA 59"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song when Saul sent men to watch his house so that they could kill him {when he left it}. The tune is “Do Not Destroy.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 59:1"/>My God, please rescue me from my enemies!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Protect me from those who want to attack me!
<verse eid="PSA 59:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 59:2"/>Rescue me from wicked men
</para>
  <para style="q2">who are trying to kill me!
<verse eid="PSA 59:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 59:3"/>Look! They are hiding and waiting for a chance to kill me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Fierce men have gathered to harm me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, they are doing that even though I have not done anything that is wrong!
<verse eid="PSA 59:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 59:4"/>I have not committed any sin, but they are hurrying to get ready to attack me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please consider my situation and come quickly to help me.
<verse eid="PSA 59:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 59:5"/>Yahweh, you are the God who commands the heavenly armies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are the God whom we Israelites worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">So I ask you to take action and punish all the people who do not honor you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not act mercifully toward those wicked people who have acted treacherously toward me.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 59:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 59:6"/>They are like wild dogs that come out in {the cool of} the evening
</para>
  <para style="q2">and growl as they roam around this city {looking for scraps of food}.
<verse eid="PSA 59:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 59:7"/>They make violent threats so loudly that it is as if they are belching.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They think, “No one who hears us {will stop us}!”
<verse eid="PSA 59:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 59:8"/>But you mock them, Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You scoff at people who do not honor you.
<verse eid="PSA 59:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 59:9"/>Because you, God, are the one who protects me and makes me strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will depend on you.
<verse eid="PSA 59:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 59:10"/>You, God, are faithfully loving to me, and you will come to help me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will defeat my enemies so that I can look triumphantly at them.
<verse eid="PSA 59:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 59:11"/>But do not kill them {right away}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Otherwise, the Israelite people might forget how you punished them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Instead, use your power to make them wander around helplessly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then destroy them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lord, you are like a shield that protects us.
<verse eid="PSA 59:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 59:12"/>The things that they say are sinful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They curse people falsely.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May their pride be like a trap that catches them
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and keeps them from doing what they are planning}.
<verse eid="PSA 59:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 59:13"/>Become angry with them and destroy them so that they do not exist anymore.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That way people will know that you, God, rule over the Israelite people and the entire world.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 59:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 59:14"/>They are like wild dogs that come out in {the cool of} the evening
</para>
  <para style="q2">and growl as they roam around this city {looking for scraps of food}.
<verse eid="PSA 59:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 59:15"/>They roam around searching for food.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If they do not get enough to eat, they keep roaming around all night.
<verse eid="PSA 59:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 59:16"/>But as for me, I will sing each morning about how powerful you are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing joyfully about how faithfully loving you are to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing about how you protect me when I am in danger.
<verse eid="PSA 59:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 59:17"/>I will praise you, who enables me to be strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you, God, protect me and faithfully love me as you promised.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 59:17"/><verse eid="PSA 59:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 59"/>
  <chapter number="60" style="c" sid="PSA 60"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: The tune is “The Lily.” David wrote this song when he was leading the Israelite army to fight against Aramean armies from Naharaim and Zobah and his general Joab had to leave and fight the Edomites in the Valley of Salt, where he killed 12, 000 of their soldiers. David wanted to testify to the Israelite people so that they would learn from this song {that they should depend on God to help them}.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 60:1"/>God, you have stopped helping us Israelites!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you have become angry with us, our enemies have been able to break through our ranks.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please enable us to fight victoriously again!
<verse eid="PSA 60:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 60:2"/>It is as if you have caused a great earthquake that has split open the ground.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Our army is struggling, but please make it strong again.
<verse eid="PSA 60:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 60:3"/>You have caused us Israelites to experience great difficulties.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if you have made us drink strong wine that is making us fall down as if we were drunk.
<verse eid="PSA 60:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 60:4"/>But you have raised a battle flag for those who honor you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They can rally around it when their enemies attack them.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 60:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 60:5"/>That way you will rescue the people whom you love.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please answer my prayer and use your power to save us.
<verse eid="PSA 60:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 60:6"/>God is holy {and does not lie}, and he has said,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“I delight in the territory that I have measured and divided up for you Israelites to live in.
</para>
  <para style="q1">That territory includes land on the east side of the Jordan River, where the Valley of Succoth is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and land on the west side of the Jordan River, where Shechem is.
<verse eid="PSA 60:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 60:7"/>I own the region of Gilead {east of the Jordan River},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I own the territory of Manasseh {west of the Jordan River}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The mighty soldiers of the tribe of Ephraim {who fight to protect Israel} are like my helmet,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have given Israel a ruler from the tribe of Judah.
<verse eid="PSA 60:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 60:8"/>The Moabites are my servants, like slaves who wash my feet.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I own the land of Edom; it is as if I have thrown my sandal onto it to show that it belongs to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">And you Philistines might shout your battle cry against me{, but I will defeat you}.”
<verse eid="PSA 60:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 60:9"/>But I still need someone to lead my army to the land of Edom
</para>
  <para style="q2">and conquer their {capital} city that has strong walls around it.
<verse eid="PSA 60:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 60:10"/>It seems that you, God, have stopped helping us Israelites.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It seems that you do not enable our armies to defeat our enemies when they march out to fight them.
<verse eid="PSA 60:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 60:11"/>Any help that human beings could give us would not be at all sufficient.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So we need you to help us to defeat our enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 60:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 60:12"/>If you, God, help us defeat our enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then we will be able to fight very valiantly.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 60:12"/><verse eid="PSA 60:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 60"/>
  <chapter number="61" style="c" sid="PSA 61"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: A musician playing a stringed instrument should accompany this song. David wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 61:1"/>O God, I am calling to you for help.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do what I ask.
<verse eid="PSA 61:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 61:2"/>I am far from home, and I feel sad, so I am calling out to you {for help}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please keep me safe, as if you had put me on top of a high rock.
<verse eid="PSA 61:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 61:3"/>You protect me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are like a strong tower into which I can go so that my enemies cannot harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 61:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 61:4"/>I wish I could always be a guest in your home!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Keep me as safe as a baby bird is under its mother’s wings.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 61:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 61:5"/>God, you know that I have solemnly promised to offer sacrifices to acknowledge you, so please help me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have given me the blessings that belong to people who honor you.
<verse eid="PSA 61:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 61:6"/>Please allow me, the king of Israel, to live and rule for many years.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please allow my descendants to rule also.
<verse eid="PSA 61:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 61:7"/>May I reign for a long time as you watch over me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are faithful, and you keep your promises, so please protect me.
<verse eid="PSA 61:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 61:8"/>If you do that, I will always sing songs to praise you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and each day I will offer the sacrifices that I promised to give you.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 61:8"/><verse eid="PSA 61:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 61"/>
  <chapter number="62" style="c" sid="PSA 62"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Perform in the style of Jeduthun. David wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 62:1"/>God is the one who saves me from my enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am waiting quietly for him to do that.
<verse eid="PSA 62:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 62:2"/>He is the only one who can save me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He protects me as if he were a rock I could climb onto in order to be safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one would harm me at all.
<verse eid="PSA 62:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 62:3"/>My enemies are threatening me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they will not be able to keep doing that.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God will destroy all of them, just as a leaning wall falls down
</para>
  <para style="q2">and just as people can push a fence onto the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 62:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 62:4"/>My enemies are plotting together to do one thing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They want to remove me from my important position.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They enjoy telling lies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They say things to bless people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but in their inner beings, they are cursing those people.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 62:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 62:5"/>Because I am expecting God to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will wait quietly for him alone to do that.
<verse eid="PSA 62:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 62:6"/>He is the only one who can save me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He protects me as if he were a rock I could climb onto in order to be safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one would harm me.
<verse eid="PSA 62:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 62:7"/>God is the one who saves me and honors me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God is like a huge rock to which I can go to be safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He makes me strong.
<verse eid="PSA 62:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 62:8"/>You Israelite people should always trust in God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Pray earnestly to him in his presence.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who keeps us safe.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 62:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 62:9"/>Certainly, ordinary people lack the power to help,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and important people are not as powerful as they seem.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If you put them all on a scale,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it would be as if they weighed less than air.
<verse eid="PSA 62:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 62:10"/>It is foolish to expect to get rich by cheating other people or by stealing from them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If you become wealthy, do not rely on your money.
<verse eid="PSA 62:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 62:11"/>God has said very reliably
</para>
  <para style="q2">that he is the one who truly has power.
<verse eid="PSA 62:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 62:12"/>God is also the one who always keeps his promises.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He punishes people who do wrong things but rewards people who do good things.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 62:12"/><verse eid="PSA 62:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 62"/>
  <chapter number="63" style="c" sid="PSA 63"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">David wrote this song when he was in the desolate area that belongs to the tribe of Judah.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 63:1"/>God, you are the God whom I worship.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I greatly desire to be with you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">It is as if my body aches for you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as a person in a dry, hot wilderness greatly desires water.
<verse eid="PSA 63:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 63:2"/>I have worshiped you in your sanctuary
</para>
  <para style="q2">and recognized how powerful and glorious you are.
<verse eid="PSA 63:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 63:3"/>You are always kind to me, as you promised in your covenant.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This is worth more to me than even being alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will always praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 63:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 63:4"/>I will praise you for as long as I am alive.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will lift up my hands and pray to you.
<verse eid="PSA 63:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 63:5"/>You satisfy me as if I had just eaten a delicious banquet of rich foods.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise you very joyfully.
<verse eid="PSA 63:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 63:6"/>Sometimes I think about you when I am lying in bed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When that happens, I reflect during the night on how wonderful you are.
<verse eid="PSA 63:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 63:7"/>{I realize that you are wonderful} because you have always helped me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I sing to you joyfully because I am aware that you protect me
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as a mother bird protects her chicks under her wings.
<verse eid="PSA 63:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 63:8"/>I remain completely loyal to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you protect me by your power.
<verse eid="PSA 63:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 63:9"/>Some people are trying to kill me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they will die and go to the place where dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 63:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 63:10"/>They may die in a battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then wild dogs will eat their corpses.
<verse eid="PSA 63:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 63:11"/>But I, the king {of Israel}, will rejoice in what God has done for me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All those who swear oaths in the name of God will praise him
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he will have stopped people from saying things that are not true.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 63:11"/><verse eid="PSA 63:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 63"/>
  <chapter number="64" style="c" sid="PSA 64"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 64:1"/>God, please listen to me as I tell you about what worries me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am afraid of my enemies; please save me from them.
<verse eid="PSA 64:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 64:2"/>Protect me from what wicked men are planning to do to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Protect me from that group of men who do evil things.
<verse eid="PSA 64:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 64:3"/>The hostile things they say are like sharp swords;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their cruel words are like arrows.
<verse eid="PSA 64:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 64:4"/>They are not afraid of anyone.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They falsely accuse people who have done nothing wrong. They are like a person who suddenly jumps up from a hiding place
</para>
  <para style="q2">and shoots an arrow at someone.
<verse eid="PSA 64:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 64:5"/>They encourage each other to do the evil things they are planning.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They boast about how they have deceived people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They say, “No one will realize what we are doing!”
<verse eid="PSA 64:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 64:6"/>They carefully plan the wicked things they want to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They brag, “We have planned this out perfectly!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is very difficult to know what people are thinking privately.
<verse eid="PSA 64:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 64:7"/>But God will suddenly judge and punish them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if he were shooting an arrow at them and wounding them.
<verse eid="PSA 64:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 64:8"/>The deceitful things they say will get them into trouble.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone who sees what happens to them will stay away from them.
<verse eid="PSA 64:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 64:9"/>People will think about how God has punished them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will tell others about it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As a result, people will not dare to be wicked.
<verse eid="PSA 64:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 64:10"/>People who do what is right will be very happy that Yahweh has punished those wicked people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will trust Yahweh to protect them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, those who really want to do good things will be glad.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 64:10"/><verse eid="PSA 64:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 64"/>
  <chapter number="65" style="c" sid="PSA 65"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 65:1"/>God, when you come to your sanctuary on Mount Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will find that we have been waiting quietly to praise you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to do what we promised we would do to honor you.
<verse eid="PSA 65:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 65:2"/>Because you help people when they pray,
</para>
  <para style="q2">people everywhere will pray to you.
<verse eid="PSA 65:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 65:3"/>When we feel very badly because we have done wrong things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you forgive our sins and make it as if we had not committed them.
<verse eid="PSA 65:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 65:4"/>When you invite people to come and worship you in your sanctuary,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that makes them very happy!
</para>
  <para style="q1">When we come to your sanctuary,
</para>
  <para style="q2">we realize how good and holy you are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that satisfies us completely.
<verse eid="PSA 65:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 65:5"/>When we pray to you, you do good and powerful things to help us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are the God who saves us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Even people who live in very remote places on the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">on the other side of the oceans, trust in you.
<verse eid="PSA 65:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 65:6"/>You are so strong, you were able to use your power
</para>
  <para style="q2">to set the mountains in their places.
<verse eid="PSA 65:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 65:7"/>When there is a storm at sea, you can calm it
</para>
  <para style="q2">and stop its waves from crashing on the shore.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the same way, you can keep nations from causing trouble.
<verse eid="PSA 65:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 65:8"/>People who live in very remote places on the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">deeply respect you because of the miracles that you perform.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People who live all over the world celebrate what you do.
<verse eid="PSA 65:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 65:9"/>You send rain to make the soil fertile
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that it will produce good crops.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if you bring water to the fields in a stream.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That is how you prepare the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">to produce abundant crops.
<verse eid="PSA 65:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 65:10"/>You send rain on the plowed fields,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you fill their furrows with water.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You soften the hard clods of soil with showers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you help young plants to grow in the fields.
<verse eid="PSA 65:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 65:11"/>When harvest time comes, the fields are glorious with crops,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if you had put a golden crown on them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You provide food for people in great abundance.
<verse eid="PSA 65:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 65:12"/>There is plenty of food for sheep and goats to eat in the pastures where they graze.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So many crops grow on the hills that it is as if the hills were celebrating.
<verse eid="PSA 65:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 65:13"/>Flocks of sheep and goats cover the meadows like a garment,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there is so much grain in the valleys that the ground is not visible.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if the meadows and valleys are singing and shouting joyfully.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 65:13"/><verse eid="PSA 65:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 65"/>
  <chapter number="66" style="c" sid="PSA 66"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 66:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: This is a song, a psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Everyone on earth should shout joyfully to praise God!
<verse eid="PSA 66:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 66:2"/>They should sing songs that tell how glorious God is
</para>
  <para style="q2">and how much he deserves praise for being glorious.
<verse eid="PSA 66:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 66:3"/>Everyone should tell God, “You do such amazing things!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are so powerful
</para>
  <para style="q2">that your enemies come and bow down fearfully in front of you.
<verse eid="PSA 66:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 66:4"/>Everyone on earth should worship you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sing to praise you
</para>
  <para style="q2">for your excellent character.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 66:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 66:5"/>Come and consider what God has done!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Think about the amazing things that he has done among people.
<verse eid="PSA 66:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 66:6"/>He made a dry path through the Sea of Reeds
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that our ancestors could walk right through it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They also walked across the Jordan River {when he stopped it from flowing}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">After they crossed, they celebrated what God had done,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we should still celebrate that today.
<verse eid="PSA 66:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 66:7"/>He is so powerful that he rules forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He observes what all the people groups do,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so anyone who considers rebelling against him
</para>
  <para style="q2">should not think that he will be able to do that.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 66:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 66:8"/>People from every nation, praise our God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise him loudly so that others will hear you as you praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 66:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 66:9"/>He has kept us alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he has not allowed anyone to destroy us.
<verse eid="PSA 66:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 66:10"/>God, you have allowed us to experience great difficulties {in order to make us pure},
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as people put silver in a hot fire so they can purify it.
<verse eid="PSA 66:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 66:11"/>It is as if you allowed someone to catch us in a trap
</para>
  <para style="q2">or made us carry a load that was almost too heavy for us.
<verse eid="PSA 66:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 66:12"/>It is as if you allowed our enemies to trample on us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We experienced troubles that were like walking through fires and floods.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But now you have brought us to a place where we are safe and have plenty of food.
<verse eid="PSA 66:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 66:13"/>God, I have come to your temple bringing offerings for the priests to burn completely on the altar.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am doing what I promised to do for you.
<verse eid="PSA 66:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 66:14"/>When I was experiencing great trouble,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I said that I would bring these offerings to you {if you rescued me}.
<verse eid="PSA 66:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 66:15"/>So I have brought fat sheep to burn on the altar,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have also brought bulls and goats.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When they are burning, you will enjoy the smell of the smoke.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 66:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 66:16"/>All you people who deeply respect God, come and listen
</para>
  <para style="q2">as I tell you what he has done for me.
<verse eid="PSA 66:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 66:17"/>I called out to him to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I praised him as I was praying to him.
<verse eid="PSA 66:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 66:18"/>If I had secretly intended to commit sins,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Lord would not have done what I asked.
<verse eid="PSA 66:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 66:19"/>{But I did not do that,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">so God has done what I asked.
<verse eid="PSA 66:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 66:20"/>I praise God
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he did what I asked him to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He has continued to be kind to me, as he promised.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 66:20"/><verse eid="PSA 66:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 66"/>
  <chapter number="67" style="c" sid="PSA 67"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: This is a song, a psalm. Musicians playing stringed instruments should accompany this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 67:1"/>May God always be kind to us and bless us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May he consider us favorably.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 67:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 67:2"/>God, please do that so that all of the people in the world will know
</para>
  <para style="q2">how you want them to live and that you are the one who saves them.
<verse eid="PSA 67:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 67:3"/>May all the people in the world praise you, God!
<verse eid="PSA 67:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 67:4"/>You judge those nations fairly and show them what they should do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So may they praise you loudly and joyfully!
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 67:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 67:5"/>May all the people in the world praise you, God!
<verse eid="PSA 67:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 67:6"/>Good crops have grown on our land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May the God whom we Israelites worship continue to give us good harvests.
<verse eid="PSA 67:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 67:7"/>May God bless us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may that cause people throughout the world to respect him greatly.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 67:7"/><verse eid="PSA 67:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 67"/>
  <chapter number="68" style="c" sid="PSA 68"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this psalm. It is a song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 68:1"/>God, take action and chase away your enemies!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make those who hate you run away from you.
<verse eid="PSA 68:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 68:2"/>Chase your enemies away just as wind blows smoke away.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make bad people go away, God, just as wax melts when it is near a fire.
<verse eid="PSA 68:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 68:3"/>But make good people happy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May they rejoice when they are in your presence;
</para>
  <para style="q2">may they be very joyful.
<verse eid="PSA 68:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 68:4"/>Sing praise to God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Sing a song for him who even cares for desolate regions.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His name is Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">be glad when you are in his presence.
<verse eid="PSA 68:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 68:5"/>God, who is present in his sanctuary,
</para>
  <para style="q2">is like a father to those who are orphans,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he protects widows.
<verse eid="PSA 68:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 68:6"/>He provides families for those who have no one to live with.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He frees prisoners and enables them to be successful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But those who rebel against him will not be successful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It will be as if they live in a place where it is very hard to grow crops.
<verse eid="PSA 68:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 68:7"/>God, you led your people out of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then you marched with them through the desert.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 68:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 68:8"/>After you did that, the earth shook at Mount Sinai when you appeared to your people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rain poured down from the sky, and your people worshiped you.
<verse eid="PSA 68:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 68:9"/>You caused much rain to fall there in the wilderness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so you enabled good crops to grow again on that land that you gave to us Israelites.
<verse eid="PSA 68:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 68:10"/>Your people built homes there.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You were kind to poor people and provided food for them.
<verse eid="PSA 68:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11-12" style="v" sid="PSA 68:11-12"/>Kings led their armies to fight against the Israelites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God defeated them and they ran away.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The Lord declared victory over them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and a great crowd of Israelite women sang and danced to celebrate.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The men who fought against these enemies captured many valuable possessions
</para>
  <para style="q2">and brought them back to the women who were at home.
<verse eid="PSA 68:11-12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 68:13"/>Some men had to take care of the sheep {instead of fighting},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but the soldiers captured enough valuable possessions to give them some as well.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They received treasures such as a dove statue with silver wings and feathers shimmering with fine gold.
<verse eid="PSA 68:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 68:14"/>Shaddai defeated the enemy kings and their armies
</para>
  <para style="q2">by making it snow on Mount Zalmon!
<verse eid="PSA 68:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 68:15"/>Mount Bashan is a very high mountain.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It has many peaks.
<verse eid="PSA 68:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 68:16"/>Because it is such a great mountain, if it could think,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it might think that God should have chosen it as the place for his sanctuary.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But Yahweh chose Mount Zion instead, and he will always be present there.
<verse eid="PSA 68:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 68:17"/>God is so powerful that it is as if he has thousands and thousands of chariots.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In fact, it is as if he has ten thousands and ten thousands of them!
</para>
  <para style="q1">The same God who appeared to the Israelites on Mount Sinai
</para>
  <para style="q2">is now present in his sanctuary on Mount Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 68:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 68:18"/>{After he defeated his enemies,} he went up to the sacred mountain where his sanctuary is.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He led many captured prisoners in a victory procession.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He received gifts from the enemies whom he had defeated.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He even received gifts from those who had rebelled against him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Now Yahweh, our God, will always be present in his sanctuary.
<verse eid="PSA 68:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 68:19"/>Praise the Lord, who helps us every day as if he were carrying a heavy load for us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the God who saves us.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 68:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 68:20"/>Our God is the God who saves us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh our Lord is the one who rescues us from dying.
<verse eid="PSA 68:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 68:21"/>But God will completely destroy his enemies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">If anyone continues to behave sinfully, God will destroy that person.
<verse eid="PSA 68:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 68:22"/>The Lord said, “Even if my enemies try to climb a high mountain to be safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or even if they try to hide at the bottom of the ocean, I will bring them back
<verse eid="PSA 68:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 68:23"/>so that you can trample on their heads.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your dogs will lick up the blood that comes out of their heads.”
<verse eid="PSA 68:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 68:24"/>And now you are parading triumphantly into your sanctuary, God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are our king, and you are leading a great crowd the way a king does.
<verse eid="PSA 68:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 68:25"/>There are singers at the front of the parade.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Musicians playing stringed instruments are at the back of the parade.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the middle there are girls playing tambourines.
<verse eid="PSA 68:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 68:26"/>Praise God, you who have gathered together!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise Yahweh, you descendants of Israel!
<verse eid="PSA 68:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 68:27"/>People from the tribe of Benjamin, the smallest tribe, are marching first.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Leaders and many other people from the tribe of Judah come next.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There are even leaders from the {far northern} tribes of Zebulun and Naphtali in the parade.
<verse eid="PSA 68:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 68:28"/>Our God has made our Israelite tribes strong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God, continue to help us with your power as you helped us in the past.
<verse eid="PSA 68:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 68:29"/>Since you have now established your sanctuary on a mountain above Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">kings will send tribute to you there.
<verse eid="PSA 68:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 68:30"/>Show the king of Egypt that even though he has a powerful army, he cannot defeat you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Many kings who are strong like bulls may gather together.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They may form armies from their subject nations, which are like bulls’ calves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but they will not be able to defeat you either}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Instead, they will come submissively and pay you tribute in silver.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Some nations are eager to fight wars; make their armies run away!
<verse eid="PSA 68:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 68:31"/>Then envoys will come from Egypt {bringing gifts to you}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The ruler of Cush will hasten to send tribute to God.
<verse eid="PSA 68:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 68:32"/>People of nations throughout the world, sing praise to God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the Lord
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 68:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 68:33"/>who dwells above the sky that he created long ago.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When you hear thunder, it is as if he is shouting with his very powerful voice.
<verse eid="PSA 68:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 68:34"/>Proclaim how powerful God is!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the king who reigns over Israel
</para>
  <para style="q2">as he rules powerfully from the sky.
<verse eid="PSA 68:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 68:35"/>God, you are in your sanctuary, and you are very powerful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This is the God whom we Israelite people worship.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He makes us very strong. Praise God!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 68:35"/><verse eid="PSA 68:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 68"/>
  <chapter number="69" style="c" sid="PSA 69"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this song. The tune is “Lilies.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 69:1"/>Please rescue me, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am in great danger, as if I were just about to drown in a flood.
<verse eid="PSA 69:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 69:2"/>It is as if I am sinking in deep mud where there is no solid ground for me to stand on.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if I am in deep water and a flood is swirling around me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 69:3"/>I am tired and my throat is dry
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I have been calling to you for help for so long.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I have been looking for so long for you to come and help me
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I have worn out my eyes.
<verse eid="PSA 69:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 69:4"/>There are people who hate me for no reason.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There are so many of these people, it is as if
 there are more of them than there are hairs on my head!
</para>
  <para style="q1">The enemies who want to harm me are powerful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they are telling lies about me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are demanding that I pay back things that I did not steal!
<verse eid="PSA 69:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 69:5"/>O God, you know that I have foolishly disobeyed your laws;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are aware of the sins that I have committed.
<verse eid="PSA 69:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 69:6"/>But Yahweh my Lord, commander of the heavenly armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">may the wrong things I have done not disappoint the people who trust you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are the God whom we Israelite people should worship.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do not let me embarrass those who do worship you.
<verse eid="PSA 69:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 69:7"/>People have insulted me because I am loyal to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have thoroughly humiliated me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 69:8"/>Even my own family members act as if they do not know me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 69:9"/>I care so much about your temple that people are causing trouble for me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People are speaking disrespectfully of you, and it is as if they are also insulting me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 69:10"/>I wept and fasted very sincerely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they mocked me for doing that.
<verse eid="PSA 69:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 69:11"/>I wore rough clothing {to show that I was sad},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they used me as an example of a foolish person.
<verse eid="PSA 69:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 69:12"/>Even the elders of the city say bad things about me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The drunkards in the city sing insulting songs about me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 69:13"/>But I will continue praying to you, Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are always very kind to me, as you have promised.
</para>
  <para style="q1">So at the time that you choose,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please answer my prayer by rescuing me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">since you love me faithfully.
<verse eid="PSA 69:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 69:14"/>Rescue me so that it will no longer be as if I were sinking in mud.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me from my enemies so that it will no longer be as if I were drowning.
<verse eid="PSA 69:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 69:15"/>Make it so that it will no longer be as if a flood were swirling around me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I was about to go down to the bottom of deep water.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me so that I do not go to the place where dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 69:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 69:16"/>Yahweh, it is so good that you faithfully love me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please do what I ask.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you are very merciful, please help me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 69:17"/>I am experiencing much trouble,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please consider my situation
</para>
  <para style="q2">and act quickly to help me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 69:18"/>Come and save me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please rescue me from my enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 69:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 69:19"/>You know personally how people are insulting, shaming, and dishonoring me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You know who all my enemies are.
<verse eid="PSA 69:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 69:20"/>Their insults have deeply offended me, and I feel very badly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I wanted someone to feel sorry for me and encourage me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but no one did.
<verse eid="PSA 69:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 69:21"/>Instead, they put poison in my food,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when I was thirsty, they gave me sour wine to drink.
<verse eid="PSA 69:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 69:22"/>May their own food be like a trap that they walk into!
</para>
  <para style="q2">May it harm their health.
<verse eid="PSA 69:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 69:23"/>May their eyes become dim so that they cannot see anything.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May their bodies keep getting weaker.
<verse eid="PSA 69:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 69:24"/>Become angry with them and punish them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Angrily pursue them until you catch them.
<verse eid="PSA 69:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 69:25"/>Make them abandon their towns
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that no one lives in them anymore.
<verse eid="PSA 69:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 69:26"/>Do this because they did things to harm
</para>
  <para style="q2">people whom you were already disciplining.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They said that people whom you were correcting
</para>
  <para style="q2">were suffering {because they had done bad things}.
<verse eid="PSA 69:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 69:27"/>Punish them for every wrong thing they have done.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not forgive them!
<verse eid="PSA 69:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 69:28"/>Remove their names from the book that records the names of people who have everlasting life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not include them in your list of righteous people.
<verse eid="PSA 69:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 69:29"/>As for me, I am in bad circumstances, and I am suffering.
</para>
  <para style="q2">O God, please protect me and save me.
<verse eid="PSA 69:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 69:30"/>When God does that, I will sing a song to praise God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will honor him by thanking him.
<verse eid="PSA 69:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 69:31"/>When I do that, it will please Yahweh more than if I had sacrificed oxen,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, he will like that better than if I had offered him full-grown bulls.
<verse eid="PSA 69:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 69:32"/>Humble people will be happy when they see {that God has rescued me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This will encourage people who worship God sincerely.
<verse eid="PSA 69:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 69:33"/>When needy people pray to Yahweh, he does what they ask.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He greatly respects people who suffer for him.
<verse eid="PSA 69:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 69:34"/>May the entire creation praise God:
</para>
  <para style="q2">the birds in the sky, the animals on the land, and the creatures in the sea.
<verse eid="PSA 69:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 69:35"/>May God protect the people who live in Jerusalem and in other places in Judah.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May he strengthen their cities so that they keep living in them as their territory.
<verse eid="PSA 69:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 69:36"/>May the descendants of the people who are loyal to him inherit that territory,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may those who love him live there safely.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 69:36"/><verse eid="PSA 69:36"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 69"/>
  <chapter number="70" style="c" sid="PSA 70"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: David wrote this psalm to remind {God that he had promised to help him}.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 70:1"/>Yahweh my God, please act quickly to rescue me!
<verse eid="PSA 70:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 70:2"/>Some people are trying to kill me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Embarrass them by making them fail to do that.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Some people would be happy to harm me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Humiliate them by making them abandon that plan.
<verse eid="PSA 70:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 70:3"/>Some people are saying that I am suffering because I am a bad person.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Make them ashamed of saying that so that they stop saying it.
<verse eid="PSA 70:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 70:4"/>{Rescue me so that} everyone who is loyal to you will greatly celebrate.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then the people who depend on you to rescue them will keep saying, “God certainly is great!”
<verse eid="PSA 70:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 70:5"/>But right now I am in very difficult circumstances,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please act quickly to help me, God!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, you are the one who helps me and saves me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please help me right away!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 70:5"/><verse eid="PSA 70:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 70"/>
  <chapter number="71" style="c" sid="PSA 71"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 71:1"/>You, Yahweh, are the one who keeps me safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May it always be clear that I was right to trust you.
<verse eid="PSA 71:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 71:2"/>Because you always do what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">take action to help me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Consider my situation and save me!
<verse eid="PSA 71:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 71:3"/>You declare that I will be safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">since you are the one who keeps me safe and protects me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please be like a huge rock on top of which I can always go to be safe.
<verse eid="PSA 71:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 71:4"/>My God, please rescue me from what wicked people want to do to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me from the power of violent, evil men.
<verse eid="PSA 71:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 71:5"/>Yahweh my Lord, you are the one whom I confidently expect to help me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have trusted in you ever since I was young.
<verse eid="PSA 71:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 71:6"/>I have depended on you for my entire life;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you even made sure that I was born safely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will always praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 71:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 71:7"/>It shocks many people to see me now,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you are my mighty protector.
<verse eid="PSA 71:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 71:8"/>I praise you lavishly throughout the day for how glorious you are.
<verse eid="PSA 71:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 71:9"/>Please keep helping me now that I have become an old man.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please help me even though I am not strong anymore.
<verse eid="PSA 71:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 71:10"/>My enemies are saying that they want to kill me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they are planning together how to do that.
<verse eid="PSA 71:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 71:11"/>They are saying, “No one will rescue him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">since God is not helping him anymore,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so we can pursue him and capture him.”
<verse eid="PSA 71:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 71:12"/>My God, do not neglect me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">hurry to help me!
<verse eid="PSA 71:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 71:13"/>Embarrass the people who want to kill me by making their plans fail.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, completely shame and disgrace those who want to harm me!
<verse eid="PSA 71:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 71:14"/>But as for me, I will always trust you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise you even more {now than I have in the past}.
<verse eid="PSA 71:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 71:15"/>I will tell people how you have saved me because you are good.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will do that continually because there will always be more for me to say about this.
<verse eid="PSA 71:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 71:16"/>Yahweh my Lord, you are the one who gives me great strength.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will recall {to others} how you do what is right in a way that no one else does.
<verse eid="PSA 71:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 71:17"/>God, you have taught me many things ever since I was young,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I still tell people today about the wonderful things you do.
<verse eid="PSA 71:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 71:18"/>God, please keep helping me now that I am old and my hair is gray.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That way I will be able to tell my descendants how powerfully you have helped me.
<verse eid="PSA 71:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 71:19"/>God, you do so many great things because you are good,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is as if they have piled up to the sky.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There is no one else like you, God!
<verse eid="PSA 71:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 71:20"/>You have allowed me to experience many very difficult things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it has seemed as if I was about to go to the place where dead people are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but now please give me a good life again.
<verse eid="PSA 71:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 71:21"/>Please make me even greater than I was before,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and comfort me rather than allow me to have difficult experiences.
<verse eid="PSA 71:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 71:22"/>When you do that, then I will play my lute and praise you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God, for faithfully helping me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will play my harp as I sing to praise you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are the holy God whom we Israelites worship.
<verse eid="PSA 71:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 71:23"/>I will shout joyfully while I sing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you will have rescued me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing to you wholeheartedly.
<verse eid="PSA 71:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 71:24"/>You will have defeated and disgraced the people who wanted to harm me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so throughout the day I will describe how you did what was right.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 71:24"/><verse eid="PSA 71:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 71"/>
  <chapter number="72" style="c" sid="PSA 72"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 72:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of Solomon.
</para>
  <para style="q1">O God, please enable the man who is now succeeding his father as king
</para>
  <para style="q2">to judge cases rightly, as you would do.
<verse eid="PSA 72:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 72:2"/>Enable him to judge the cases of Israelite people fairly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">especially for people who are vulnerable.
<verse eid="PSA 72:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 72:3"/>May the people live rightly so that they will be prosperous
</para>
  <para style="q2">as crops grow abundantly on the hillsides of the land.
<verse eid="PSA 72:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 72:4"/>Help the king to defend poor people and rescue needy people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and defeat those who are oppressing them.
<verse eid="PSA 72:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 72:5"/>May each successive generation of the people respect you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May they do that for as long as the sun and the moon are in the sky!
<verse eid="PSA 72:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 72:6"/>May this king make the nation prosperous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as heavy rains soak the soil
</para>
  <para style="q2">and enable more hay to grow after a first cutting.
<verse eid="PSA 72:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 72:7"/>May people who live rightly prosper during the time when he reigns,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may the nation be very prosperous for as long as the moon is in the sky.
<verse eid="PSA 72:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 72:8"/>May he rule over all of the surrounding territory, right up to the shores of the seas.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May his realm extend from the Euphrates River to the limits of the lands that people know.
<verse eid="PSA 72:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 72:9"/>May the leaders of the desert tribes bow down in front of him {to acknowledge him as their ruler},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may his enemies lie facedown on the ground {in submission to him}.
<verse eid="PSA 72:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 72:10"/>May the kings who rule the land of Tarshish and other coastal areas pay tribute to him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May the king of Sheba and the king of Seba give him gifts.
<verse eid="PSA 72:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 72:11"/>In fact, may all the kings in the world acknowledge him as their ruler,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may every nation obey him.
<verse eid="PSA 72:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 72:12"/>May all these things happen because he rescues needy people when they cry out for help
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he helps poor people who have no one else to help them.
<verse eid="PSA 72:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 72:13"/>May he feel compassion for people who are weak and needy and save their lives.
<verse eid="PSA 72:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 72:14"/>May their lives be important to him
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that he rescues them from people who are oppressing and harming them.
<verse eid="PSA 72:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 72:15"/>May this king live for a long time!
</para>
  <para style="q2">May he receive much fine gold.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May people always pray for him and ask God to bless him.
<verse eid="PSA 72:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 72:16"/>May the fields produce such abundant crops
</para>
  <para style="q2">that grain grows all the way up to the tops of the hills
</para>
  <para style="q1">and sways in the wind like the branches of the trees in Lebanon.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May the cities in Israel be as full of people as the fields are full of grass.
<verse eid="PSA 72:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 72:17"/>May people always remember what a good king this was,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for as long as the sun is in the sky!
</para>
  <para style="q1">May he do good things for many people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may the people of other nations say that he has a good life.
<verse eid="PSA 72:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 72:18"/>Praise Yahweh, the God whom we Israelites worship;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does amazing things that no one else can do.
<verse eid="PSA 72:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 72:19"/>Praise him forever for how glorious he is!
</para>
  <para style="q2">May his glory fill the whole world! Amen! Yes, amen!
<verse eid="PSA 72:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 72:20"/>This is the end of the prayers that David, the son of Jesse, wrote.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 72:20"/><verse eid="PSA 72:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 72"/>
  <chapter number="73" style="c" sid="PSA 73"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Three

</para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 73:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">Asaph wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God truly is good to us Israelite people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to those who want to do what pleases God.
<verse eid="PSA 73:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 73:2"/>As for me, I almost stopped trusting in God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I was almost guilty of committing a great sin against him
<verse eid="PSA 73:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 73:3"/>because I envied those who proudly acted as if they did not need God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">when I realized that they prospered even though they were wicked.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 73:4"/>Those people do not suffer;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they always have plenty of food to eat.
<verse eid="PSA 73:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 73:5"/>They do not experience the difficult things that other people do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they do not experience catastrophes and sicknesses like other people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 73:6"/>So they are proud and violent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Their being prideful is like a necklace that they show off to others, and they openly display their violent actions like people openly display the clothes they wear.
<verse eid="PSA 73:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 73:7"/>Their eyes protrude because their faces are fat,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they are always thinking about more evil things to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 73:8"/>They scoff at other people, and wickedly talk about doing unjust things to them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they speak pridefully.
<verse eid="PSA 73:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 73:9"/>They exalt themselves and talk as if they are God in heaven,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they go about the earth talking boastfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 73:10"/>The result is that people pay attention to them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and listen to everything they say.
<verse eid="PSA 73:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 73:11"/>Wicked people say to themselves, “God certainly does not care what we do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Most High certainly will not judge us for what we do!”
<verse eid="PSA 73:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 73:12"/>Look at how these wicked people live;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their lives are so easy that they never have to worry about anything, and they are always becoming richer.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 73:13"/>{When I saw this I thought that} certainly it is useless that I have thought about things that are pleasing to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and have not sinned.
<verse eid="PSA 73:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 73:14"/>Every day I suffer,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and every morning you punish me.
<verse eid="PSA 73:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 73:15"/>If I had said these things out loud in front of others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">surely I would have been sinning against your people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 73:16"/>When I tried to think about all this,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it was very difficult for me to understand it.
<verse eid="PSA 73:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 73:17"/>But when I went to the temple where people worship God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then I understood what will happen to wicked people in the future.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 73:18"/>I know that you make their future insecure;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will cause them to be ruined.
<verse eid="PSA 73:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 73:19"/>God will suddenly destroy these wicked people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will die in terrible ways.
<verse eid="PSA 73:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 73:20"/>Lord, when you act, you will cause the wicked to quickly vanish;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will vanish like a dream which disappears as soon as a person awakes from their sleep.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 73:21"/>When I was grieved in my inner being
</para>
  <para style="q2">and felt emotionally hurt,
<verse eid="PSA 73:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 73:22"/>I was stupid and ignorant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I behaved like an animal toward you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 73:23"/>Nevertheless I am always with you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you constantly stay close to me.
<verse eid="PSA 73:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 73:24"/>You lead me by instructing me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and when I die, you will take me into your glorious presence.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 73:25"/>You are the only one I have in heaven!
</para>
  <para style="q2">There is nothing on this earth that I desire more than you.
<verse eid="PSA 73:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 73:26"/>My body and my spirit may become very weak,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but God enables me to feel encouraged;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has granted to me that I would belong to him forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 73:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 73:27"/>People who abandon you will perish;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will ruin every person who is not loyal to you.
<verse eid="PSA 73:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 73:28"/>But for me, the only thing I need is to be close to God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I trust in the Lord Yahweh to keep me safe
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may tell others everything you have done for me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 73:28"/><verse eid="PSA 73:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 73"/>
  <chapter number="74" style="c" sid="PSA 74"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 74:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God, it feels as if you have permanently abandoned us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You care for us Israelites the way a shepherd cares for his flock.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So please do not continue to be angry with us.
<verse eid="PSA 74:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 74:2"/>Think about your people whom you chose long ago.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You rescued us from slavery so that we would belong to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Think about Mount Zion, where you have been present {in your temple}.
<verse eid="PSA 74:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 74:3"/>Come and walk through the ruins of your temple.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It seems that no one will ever rebuild it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Look at all the damage that the enemy soldiers did to your temple.
<verse eid="PSA 74:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 74:4"/>Your enemies shouted in triumph right there in the place where you met with us Israelites.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They set up their battle flags to show that they had conquered it.
<verse eid="PSA 74:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 74:5"/>They acted like woodsmen who were swinging axes to cut down trees in a forest.
<verse eid="PSA 74:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 74:6"/>They smashed all the carved wooden panels with their axes and hammers.
<verse eid="PSA 74:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 74:7"/>Then they burned down your temple completely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They treated the temple where you were present as if it were not a sacred place.
<verse eid="PSA 74:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 74:8"/>They said to themselves, “We will completely subdue the Israelites.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">They burned down every place in the land where people gathered to worship God.
<verse eid="PSA 74:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 74:9"/>You no longer give us any signs,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and there are no prophets anymore.
</para>
  <para style="q2">None of us knows how long this will last.
<verse eid="PSA 74:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 74:10"/>God, do not allow your opponents to continue to insult you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not allow your enemies to keep treating you with disrespect anymore!
<verse eid="PSA 74:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 74:11"/>You should not fail to use your great power.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Use your power to destroy your enemies!
<verse eid="PSA 74:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 74:12"/>God, I acknowledge that you have ruled from ancient times.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have been saving people throughout the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 74:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 74:13"/>By your great power, you pushed back the sea so that the dry land would appear.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You created order out of the watery chaos.
<verse eid="PSA 74:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 74:14"/>It was as if you smashed the heads of a chaos monster that lived in the sea
</para>
  <para style="q2">and left his body in the desert for scavengers to eat.
<verse eid="PSA 74:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 74:15"/>You are able to make springs and streams flow in dry areas,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you are also able to dry up rivers that usually flow all the time.
<verse eid="PSA 74:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 74:16"/>You determine when it becomes day and when it becomes night.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You make it light during the day when the sun shines.
<verse eid="PSA 74:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 74:17"/>You are the one who set all the boundaries of the earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are the one who created the seasons of summer and winter.
<verse eid="PSA 74:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 74:18"/>Yahweh, remember that your enemies have insulted you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that foolish people have mocked your reputation.
<verse eid="PSA 74:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 74:19"/>Do not allow cruel enemies to destroy the people whom you cherish.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save the lives of your vulnerable people before it is too late.
<verse eid="PSA 74:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 74:20"/>People are committing violent acts in places where they think others will not see them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So we need you to help us. Please do that because of the covenant that you made with us.
<verse eid="PSA 74:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 74:21"/>We are asking you to help us; please do not disappoint us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then we poor and needy people will praise you for what you have done.
<verse eid="PSA 74:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 74:22"/>Take action to defend yourself, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not allow foolish people to keep insulting you!
<verse eid="PSA 74:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 74:23"/>Do not ignore what your enemies are saying.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your opponents keep shouting things against you.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 74:23"/><verse eid="PSA 74:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 74"/>
  <chapter number="75" style="c" sid="PSA 75"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Asaph wrote this song. The tune is “Do Not Destroy.”
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 75:1"/>We thank you, God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We thank you because you are close {to us}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We tell people about the wonderful things that you have done.

<verse eid="PSA 75:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 75:2"/>{You say,} “I have set a time {to judge people}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">At that time, I will judge everyone fairly.
<verse eid="PSA 75:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 75:3"/>The earth may shake,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and everyone who lives on it may tremble.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But I am the one who holds it steady.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 75:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 75:4"/>I warn those who boast, “Stop boasting!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">I tell wicked people, “Do not be proud!
<verse eid="PSA 75:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 75:5"/>Do not brag about your power!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not speak arrogantly!”

<verse eid="PSA 75:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 75:6"/>{The one who judges and} honors people does not come from the east, west, or south.
<verse eid="PSA 75:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 75:7"/>God is the one who judges people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he shames and punishes some people, and he honors other people.
<verse eid="PSA 75:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 75:8"/>It is as if Yahweh holds a cup {full of punishment} in his hand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is full of {punishment that is like} foaming wine mixed with spices.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He pours it out {to punish the wicked},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all the wicked people on earth must drink it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He punishes them fully like} they were drinking the cup to the last drop.

<verse eid="PSA 75:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 75:9"/>But as for me, I will never stop saying what the God whom Jacob worshiped has done;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will never stop singing to praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 75:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 75:10"/>God promises this: “I will destroy the power of wicked people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but I will increase the power of righteous people.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 75:10"/><verse eid="PSA 75:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 75"/>
  <chapter number="76" style="c" sid="PSA 76"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: to be accompanied by stringed instruments. Asaph wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 76:1"/>People in Judah know God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is famous in Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 76:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 76:2"/>His home is in Jerusalem.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He lives on Mount Zion.
<verse eid="PSA 76:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 76:3"/>There he shattered the flaming arrows.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He destroyed the shields, the swords, and the weapons of war.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 76:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 76:4"/>You are glorious and excellent.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are more majestic than the mountains where you destroyed your enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 76:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 76:5"/>Enemy soldiers plundered the brave soldiers.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have fallen into their final sleep.
</para>
  <para style="q2">None of the warriors were able to lift their hands {to defend themselves}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 76:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 76:6"/>When you, the God whom Jacob worshiped, shouted at them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">their war horses and their riders fell down dead.
<verse eid="PSA 76:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 76:7"/>You are the one whom everyone must fear.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one can survive in your presence when you are angry.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 76:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 76:8"/>You gave your decision from heaven.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The whole world was scared and silent.
<verse eid="PSA 76:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 76:9"/>This happened when you stood up to judge, O God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to rescue all the oppressed people of the world.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 76:9"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 76:10"/>Even human anger will bring you praise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will use the rest of their anger as a weapon.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 76:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 76:11"/>Make promises to Yahweh your God and keep them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let everyone around him bring gifts to the Awesome One.
<verse eid="PSA 76:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 76:12"/>He humbles the leaders,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and terrifies all the kings.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 76:12"/><verse eid="PSA 76:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 76"/>
  <chapter number="77" style="c" sid="PSA 77"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Perform in the style of Jeduthun. Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 77:1"/>I cried out to God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I cried aloud to him, and he listened to me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 77:2"/>When I was in trouble, I prayed to the Lord;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all during the night I lifted up my hands {while I prayed},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I did not stop {praying}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But nothing could comfort me.
<verse eid="PSA 77:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 77:3"/>When I thought about God, I despaired;
</para>
  <para style="q2">as I thoughtfully considered {him}, I became weak and discouraged.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 77:4"/>All during the night he prevented me from sleeping;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I was so worried that I did not know what to say.
<verse eid="PSA 77:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 77:5"/>I thought about days that had passed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I remembered what had happened in previous years.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 77:6"/>During the night, I remembered the songs that I used to sing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I thoughtfully considered, and I pondered these things:
<verse eid="PSA 77:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 77:7"/>{I feared that} the Lord would reject {me} forever
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that he would never be kind {to me} again.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 77:8"/>{I wondered whether} {the Lord} had completely stopped being faithful
</para>
  <para style="q2">and had broken his promise to all future generations.
<verse eid="PSA 77:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 77:9"/>{I asked myself whether} God had forgotten to be gracious
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and whether} his anger had caused him to stop being compassionate.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 77:10"/>I said, “What causes me to be sad the most is that
</para>
  <para style="q2">it seems that God, who is greater than any other spirit being, is no longer using his power for us.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 77:11"/>But then, Yahweh, I recall your great deeds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I remember the wonderful things that you did in the past.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 77:12"/>I contemplated all that you have done,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I thought carefully about your mighty acts.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 77:13"/>God, everything that you do is amazing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is certainly no god who is great like you are!
<verse eid="PSA 77:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 77:14"/>You are God, the one who performs miracles;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you showed to the people of many people groups that you are powerful.
<verse eid="PSA 77:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 77:15"/>By your power you rescued your people {from Egypt};
</para>
  <para style="q2">you saved those who were descendants of Jacob and his son Joseph.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 77:16"/>It was as though the waters saw you and became very afraid,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and even the deepest part of the water shook.
<verse eid="PSA 77:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 77:17"/>Rain poured down from the clouds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it thundered very loudly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and lightning flashed in all directions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 77:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 77:18"/>Thunder crashed in the whirlwind—your voice!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lightning lit up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the earth shook violently.
<verse eid="PSA 77:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 77:19"/>Then you walked through the sea
</para>
  <para style="q2">in a path that you made through the deep water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but your footprints could not be seen.
<verse eid="PSA 77:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 77:20"/>You led your people as a shepherd leads his flock of sheep
</para>
  <para style="q2">while Moses and Aaron were the leaders of your people.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 77:20"/><verse eid="PSA 77:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 77"/>
  <chapter number="78" style="c" sid="PSA 78"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 78:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A song of Asaph.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My friends, listen to what I am going to teach you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">pay careful attention to what I will say.
<verse eid="PSA 78:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 78:2"/>I am going to give you some sayings that wise people have said.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They will be sayings about things that happened long ago,
</para>
  <para style="q2">things that were difficult to understand.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 78:3"/>These are things that we have heard and known previously,
</para>
  <para style="q2">things that our parents and grandparents told us.
<verse eid="PSA 78:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 78:4"/>We will tell these things to our children,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but we will also tell our grandchildren to praise Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">for his power and the glorious things that he has done.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 78:5"/>He gave requirements and instructions to the Israelites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those who are descended from Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he told our ancestors to teach them to their children.
<verse eid="PSA 78:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 78:6"/>He commanded this so that their children would also know them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so that they would teach them to their own children.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 78:7"/>In that way, they also would trust in God
</para>
  <para style="q2">and would not forget the things that he has done;
</para>
  <para style="q1">instead, they would obey his commandments.
<verse eid="PSA 78:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 78:8"/>They would not be like their ancestors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who were very stubborn and kept rebelling against God;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they did not continue firmly trusting in God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they did not worship him alone.

<verse eid="PSA 78:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 78:9"/>The soldiers of the tribe of Ephraim had bows and arrows,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but they ran away from their enemies on the day that they fought with their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 78:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 78:10"/>They did not do what they had agreed with God that they would do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they refused to obey his laws.
<verse eid="PSA 78:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 78:11"/>They forgot what he had done;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they forgot about the miracles that they had seen him perform.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 78:12"/>While our ancestors were watching,
</para>
  <para style="q1">God performed miracles in the area around the city of Zoan in Egypt.
<verse eid="PSA 78:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 78:13"/>Then he caused the Sea of Reeds to divide,
</para>
  <para style="q2">causing the water on each side to pile up like a wall,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the result that our ancestors walked through it on dry ground.
<verse eid="PSA 78:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 78:14"/>He led them by a bright cloud during the day
</para>
  <para style="q1">and by a fiery light during the night.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 78:15"/>He split rocks open in the wilderness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and gave to our ancestors plenty of water from deep inside the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 78:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 78:16"/>He caused a stream of water to flow from the rock;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the water flowed like a river.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 78:17"/>But our ancestors continued to sin against God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the desert they rebelled against the one who is greater than any other spirit being.
<verse eid="PSA 78:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 78:18"/>By demanding that God give them the food that they desired,
</para>
  <para style="q1">they tried to find out if he would always do what they requested him to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 78:19"/>They insulted God by saying,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“God surely cannot supply food for us here in this desert.
<verse eid="PSA 78:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 78:20"/>It is surely true that Moses struck the rock,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and God made a huge amount of water gush out,
</para>
  <para style="q1">but we, his people, {doubt} that he can also provide bread and meat for us.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 78:21"/>So when Yahweh heard that, he became very angry,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he sent a fire to burn up some of his Israelite people.
<verse eid="PSA 78:21"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 78:22"/>He did that because they did not trust in him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they did not believe that he would rescue them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 78:23"/>But God spoke to the sky above them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and commanded it to open like a door,
<verse eid="PSA 78:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 78:24"/>and then food fell down like rain,
</para>
  <para style="q3">food that they named “manna.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">God gave them grain from heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 78:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 78:25"/>So the people ate the food that angels eat.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God gave to them all the manna that they wanted.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 78:26"/>Later, he caused the wind to blow from the east,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and by his power he also sent wind from the south.
<verse eid="PSA 78:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 78:27"/>The wind brought birds to eat which fell like rain.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They were as uncountable as the grains of sand on the seashore.
<verse eid="PSA 78:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 78:28"/>God caused those birds to fall in the middle of their camp.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There were birds all around their tents.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 78:29"/>So the people {cooked the birds and} ate the meat; their stomachs were full
</para>
  <para style="q2">because God had given them what they wanted.
<verse eid="PSA 78:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 78:30"/>But they had not yet eaten all that they wanted,
<verse eid="PSA 78:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 78:31"/>when God angrily killed some of their strongest men.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He even sent young Israelite men to their graves.
<verse eid="PSA 78:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 78:32"/>In spite of all this, the people continued to sin;
</para>
  <para style="q1">in spite of all the miracles that God had performed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they still did not trust that he would take care of them.

<verse eid="PSA 78:32"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 78:33"/>So he shortened their lives so they seemed to only be a few days or like they were gone as quickly as a breath of air,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he terrified them during even those few years.
<verse eid="PSA 78:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 78:34"/>Whenever God caused some of the Israelites to die,
</para>
  <para style="q1">the others would repent;
</para>
  <para style="q1">they would be sorry and seriously ask God to save them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 78:35"/>They would remember that God was like a huge rock on which they would be safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that he, who was greater than any other spirit being, was the one who would buy them back.
<verse eid="PSA 78:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 78:36"/>But they tried to trick God by lying to him.
<verse eid="PSA 78:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 78:37"/>They were not loyal to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they did not keep the promises between God and them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 78:38"/>But God acted mercifully toward his people.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He forgave them for having sinned
</para>
  <para style="q2">and did not get rid of them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Many times he decided not to become angry with them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and did not furiously punish them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 78:39"/>He remembered that they were only humans who die,
</para>
  <para style="q2">humans who disappear as quickly as a wind that blows by and then is gone.

<verse eid="PSA 78:39"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 78:40"/>Many times our ancestors rebelled against God in the wilderness
</para>
  <para style="q1">and made him very sad.
<verse eid="PSA 78:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 78:41"/>Many times they did evil things to find out if they could do those things without God punishing them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They frequently caused the holy God whom the Israelites worship to become sad.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 78:42"/>They did not remember how powerfully he had acted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they {forgot} about the time when he rescued them from their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 78:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 78:43"/>They forgot about all the wonderfully powerful things he did near Zoan in Egypt.
<verse eid="PSA 78:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 78:44"/>He turned the rivers of {Egypt} to blood,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that the people could not drink their streams.
<verse eid="PSA 78:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 78:45"/>He sent swarms of flies among the people of Egypt that bit them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he sent frogs that destroyed everything.
<verse eid="PSA 78:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 78:46"/>He gave their crops to the locusts.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He let swarming locusts eat everything they had worked for.
<verse eid="PSA 78:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 78:47"/>He killed their grape vines with hail,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and killed their sycamore trees with frost.
<verse eid="PSA 78:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 78:48"/>He sent a terrible thunderstorm with hail to kill all their domestic animals.
<verse eid="PSA 78:48"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 78:49"/>Because God was fiercely angry with the people of Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he caused them to be very distressed.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The disasters that struck them were like a group of angels that destroyed everything.
<verse eid="PSA 78:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 78:50"/>He let himself be angry with them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he did not prevent them from dying;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he sent a serious illness that killed many of them.
<verse eid="PSA 78:50"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 78:51"/>In that plague he caused all the firstborn sons of the people of Egypt to die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:51"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 78:52"/>Then he led his people out of Egypt like a shepherd leads his sheep,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he guided them like a flock in the desert.
<verse eid="PSA 78:52"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="PSA 78:53"/>He led them safely, and they were not afraid,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but their enemies drowned in the sea.
<verse eid="PSA 78:53"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="PSA 78:54"/>Later God used his power to bring the Israelite people to the land he had set apart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to this hill country that he had taken for himself.

<verse eid="PSA 78:54"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="PSA 78:55"/>He drove out the people groups as the Israelites advanced;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he distributed the land for each tribe to possess as their own,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he settled the tribes of Israel in the homes of those peoples.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:55"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="PSA 78:56"/>But the Israelites defied the God who is greater than all other spirit beings and disobeyed him to see what he would do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They did not obey what he had required them to do.

<verse eid="PSA 78:56"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="PSA 78:57"/>They turned away and were unfaithful, just as their ancestors had been;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they were as unreliable as a bow that does not shoot straight.

<verse eid="PSA 78:57"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="PSA 78:58"/>They made God angry by worshiping at shrines on the hilltops,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they made him jealous by worshiping carved idols.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:58"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="PSA 78:59"/>When God saw what they were doing, he became very angry
</para>
  <para style="q2">and completely rejected the Israelite people.

<verse eid="PSA 78:59"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="PSA 78:60"/>He stopped living at Shiloh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the place where he had set up his tent and lived among people.

<verse eid="PSA 78:60"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="PSA 78:61"/>He let enemies capture the sacred chest which showed how strong and glorious he was.

<verse eid="PSA 78:61"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="PSA 78:62"/>He let enemies kill his people in battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he was very angry with the people who belonged to him.

<verse eid="PSA 78:62"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="PSA 78:63"/>Fire destroyed the young men,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no one sang wedding songs for the young women.

<verse eid="PSA 78:63"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="PSA 78:64"/>Enemies killed the priests in battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the wives they left behind were not able to mourn for them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:64"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="PSA 78:65"/>Then the Lord acted as though he had been sleeping and had woken up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a warrior who becomes alert after drinking wine.

<verse eid="PSA 78:65"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="PSA 78:66"/>He drove his enemies back
</para>
  <para style="q2">and disgraced them forever.

<verse eid="PSA 78:66"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="PSA 78:67"/>He did not choose the descendants of Joseph to be the leading tribe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he did not choose the tribe of Ephraim.

<verse eid="PSA 78:67"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="PSA 78:68"/>Instead he chose the tribe of Judah
</para>
  <para style="q2">whose capital is on Mount Zion, which he loves.

<verse eid="PSA 78:68"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="PSA 78:69"/>He had them build his temple there, high up like the heavens,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he established it to last as long as the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 78:69"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="PSA 78:70"/>He chose David, who served him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and took him away from tending the sheep.

<verse eid="PSA 78:70"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="PSA 78:71"/>He took David from caring for the mother sheep and their lambs
</para>
  <para style="q2">and appointed him to lead the people of Israel, the people who belonged to God.

<verse eid="PSA 78:71"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="PSA 78:72"/>David led them with a sincere and devoted heart,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he guided them with great skill.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 78:72"/><verse eid="PSA 78:72"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 78"/>
  <chapter number="79" style="c" sid="PSA 79"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 79:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God, foreign nations have invaded the land that belongs to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have made your holy temple unfit for worship,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they have made Jerusalem a pile of ruins.
<verse eid="PSA 79:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 79:2"/>They left the dead bodies of the people who were faithful to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">for birds and wild animals to eat.
<verse eid="PSA 79:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 79:3"/>They killed so many of your people that blood flowed like water all around Jerusalem.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There were not enough people still alive to bury them.
<verse eid="PSA 79:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 79:4"/>The people of the nations around us insult us and laugh at us.
<verse eid="PSA 79:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 79:5"/>Yahweh, please do not stay so very angry with us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">even though we sinned against you by worshiping other gods.
<verse eid="PSA 79:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 79:6"/>The people of other nations do not honor you as God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You should be angry with them and punish them,
<verse eid="PSA 79:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 79:7"/>because they are the ones who have killed so many Israelites
</para>
  <para style="q2">and destroyed the land in which they lived.
<verse eid="PSA 79:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 79:8"/>Please forgive the wicked things we did in the past.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Quickly be merciful to us,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because we are desperate.
<verse eid="PSA 79:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 79:9"/>God, you are the one who saves us, so please help us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do that for the sake of your glorious reputation.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Forgive us for our sins so that people will honor you.
<verse eid="PSA 79:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 79:10"/>Do not let the other nations say, “Their God was not able to help them!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">We want to see you punish those nations
</para>
  <para style="q1">for killing the people who serve you.
<verse eid="PSA 79:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 79:11"/>Listen to the moans of your people who are now captives,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and use your great power to save those who are about to die.
<verse eid="PSA 79:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 79:12"/>Lord, pay back our neighbors directly, seven times over,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the insults they have spoken against you!
<verse eid="PSA 79:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 79:13"/>Then we will always thank you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You care for us, your people, the way a shepherd cares for his sheep.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Each generation of Israelites will tell their children how wonderful you are.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 79:13"/><verse eid="PSA 79:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 79"/>
  <chapter number="80" style="c" sid="PSA 80"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: The tune is “Lilies.” A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song as an appeal to Yahweh for help.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 80:1"/>God, you are like a shepherd to the people of Israel, so please listen to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You lead the descendants of Joseph the way a shepherd leads his flock.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You were present with us in your temple above the statues of the cherubim;
</para>
  <para style="q2">reveal your glory to us again!
<verse eid="PSA 80:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 80:2"/>Just as you moved powerfully through the wilderness
</para>
  <para style="q2">right ahead of the tribes of Ephraim, Benjamin, and Manasseh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">come powerfully once again and save us.
<verse eid="PSA 80:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 80:3"/>God, make us strong again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Regard us favorably and save us.
<verse eid="PSA 80:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 80:4"/>Yahweh, you are the God who commands the heavenly armies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have been angry with us, and so you have not been doing what we ask
</para>
  <para style="q2">when we pray to you. But please now answer our prayers.
<verse eid="PSA 80:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 80:5"/>You have caused us to experience constant sorrow.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It feels as if you are punishing us three times as much as we deserve.
<verse eid="PSA 80:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 80:6"/>The nations around us have become hostile to us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our enemies make fun of us.
<verse eid="PSA 80:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 80:7"/>God, you who command the heavenly armies, make us strong again!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Regard us favorably and save us.
<verse eid="PSA 80:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 80:8"/>You brought your people out of Egypt as if you were transplanting a vine from there.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You forced other nations to leave this land
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you allowed your people to settle in it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if you were planting that vine here.
<verse eid="PSA 80:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 80:9"/>You removed the foreign nations, just as a farmer clears the ground for a new plant.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This enabled your people to become a strong nation that occupied the entire country.
<verse eid="PSA 80:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 80:10"/>It was as if that vine became so large that its shadow darkened the mountains
</para>
  <para style="q2">and its branches were like great cedar trees.
<verse eid="PSA 80:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 80:11"/>They controlled the territory from the Great Sea in the west
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the Euphrates River in the east.
<verse eid="PSA 80:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 80:12"/>But now you have allowed enemies to invade and conquer us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if you had torn down a fence that protected that vine,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so that everyone who walked past it
</para>
  <para style="q2">could take whatever fruit they wanted from it.
<verse eid="PSA 80:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 80:13"/>Those enemies have destroyed the country,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if a wild boar had chewed up that vine
</para>
  <para style="q2">and wild animals ate what remained.
<verse eid="PSA 80:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 80:14"/>God, commander of the heavenly armies, please help us again!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Look down from heaven and see what is happening to us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Come and care for your people, who are like a vine that you planted
<verse eid="PSA 80:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 80:15"/>and worked hard to make sure that it would grow well.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your people are also like your own son whom you helped grow up to be strong.
<verse eid="PSA 80:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 80:16"/>But now, because you do not regard them favorably,
</para>
  <para style="q2">their enemies are destroying them
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if someone had cut down that vine and burned it.
<verse eid="PSA 80:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 80:17"/>Even though we are human, we are like your own son
</para>
  <para style="q2">whom you helped grow up to be strong,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so please help us with your power.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Restore us to a position of honor.
<verse eid="PSA 80:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 80:18"/>Then we will not worship other gods again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Give us new life, and we will worship only you.
<verse eid="PSA 80:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 80:19"/>Yahweh, the God who commands the heavenly armies, make us strong again!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Regard us favorably and save us.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 80:19"/><verse eid="PSA 80:19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 80"/>
  <chapter number="81" style="c" sid="PSA 81"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Accompany the song with a stringed instrument. A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 81:1"/>Sing joyfully to God, who makes us strong!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Shout with joy to the God whom we Israelites worship!
<verse eid="PSA 81:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 81:2"/>Start playing music! Beat tambourines
</para>
  <para style="q2">and play lyres and pleasant-sounding harps.
<verse eid="PSA 81:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 81:3"/>Blow a ram’s horn for the new-moon festival {each month}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and on the day of the full moon when the Festival of Shelters begins.
<verse eid="PSA 81:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 81:4"/>Do this because the God whom we Israelite people worship
</para>
  <para style="q2">has commanded us to do it.
<verse eid="PSA 81:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 81:5"/>God told our ancestors to observe these festivals
</para>
  <para style="q2">when he delivered them from slavery to the Egyptians,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a people whose language they did not understand.
<verse eid="PSA 81:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 81:6"/>{Yahweh says,} “They had to hold on to heavy baskets full of bricks
</para>
  <para style="q2">as they carried them on their shoulders,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I freed them from doing that.
<verse eid="PSA 81:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 81:7"/>When they were suffering, they cried to me for help, and I rescued them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{At Mount Sinai,} I spoke to them from dark clouds {and gave them laws}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then I saw whether they trusted me
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they complained at Meribah that they had no water.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 81:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 81:8"/>Listen to me, my people, while I warn you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I wish that you Israelites would pay attention to me!
<verse eid="PSA 81:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 81:9"/>You must not make any idols that represent any of the gods that other nations worship.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You must never bow down to worship any of those gods.
<verse eid="PSA 81:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 81:10"/>I am Yahweh your God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am the one who rescued you from slavery in Egypt.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If you depend on me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will provide everything that you need.
<verse eid="PSA 81:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 81:11"/>However, my people would not listen to what I said;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Israelites refused to obey me.
<verse eid="PSA 81:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 81:12"/>So I let them do whatever they stubbornly wanted to do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they did whatever they had decided to do.
<verse eid="PSA 81:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 81:13"/>I wish that my people would obey me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, I wish that the Israelites would live the way I want them to!
<verse eid="PSA 81:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 81:14"/>Then I would use my power against those who are opposing them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I would easily defeat their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 81:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 81:15"/>Then those who had rebelled against Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">would bow down fearfully in front of him {to submit to his authority}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">But the Israelites would always prosper.
<verse eid="PSA 81:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 81:16"/>I would make their fields produce abundant crops,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they would even find all the honey they wanted
</para>
  <para style="q2">in wild bee hives in rocky places.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 81:16"/><verse eid="PSA 81:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 81"/>
  <chapter number="82" style="c" sid="PSA 82"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 82:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God has taken his place in the assembly that he governs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he pronounces judgment on the rulers there.
<verse eid="PSA 82:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 82:2"/>He says, “You must stop making unjust decisions
</para>
  <para style="q2">and favoring wicked people!
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 82:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 82:3"/>Defend poor people and orphans,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and decide cases fairly for people who have no one else to help them.
<verse eid="PSA 82:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 82:4"/>Save defenseless people
</para>
  <para style="q2">from what wicked people want to do to them!
<verse eid="PSA 82:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 82:5"/>You are foolish and ignorant!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You do not recognize the right things to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People are no longer living by the basic principles that make a society fair.
<verse eid="PSA 82:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 82:6"/>I said, ‘You are spiritual beings;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are all rulers over creation like the Most High.
<verse eid="PSA 82:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 82:7"/>But you will die as humans do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will lose your power just as rulers do.’”
<verse eid="PSA 82:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 82:8"/>God, you rule all the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so take action and judge the people who live on the earth!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 82:8"/><verse eid="PSA 82:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 82"/>
  <chapter number="83" style="c" sid="PSA 83"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">A Levite from the clan of Asaph wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 83:1"/>God, please take action to help us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do that right away!
<verse eid="PSA 83:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 83:2"/>I ask this because the enemies who hate you
</para>
  <para style="q2">are defiantly approaching us with a large army.
<verse eid="PSA 83:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 83:3"/>They have plotted deviously together
</para>
  <para style="q2">to fight against us Israelites whom you cherish.
<verse eid="PSA 83:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 83:4"/>They have said to each other, “Come on, let us destroy them so completely
</para>
  <para style="q2">that no one will ever remember that Israel existed!”
<verse eid="PSA 83:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 83:5"/>They have all agreed to do this,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they have made an alliance against you.
<verse eid="PSA 83:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 83:6"/>This army includes soldiers who are Edomites, Ishmaelites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Moabites, Hagrites,
<verse eid="PSA 83:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 83:7"/>Gebalites, Ammonites, Amalekites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Philistines, and Tyrians.
<verse eid="PSA 83:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 83:8"/>The Assyrians are helping them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They have given military support to the Moabites and Ammonites
</para>
  <para style="q2">{who are leading this army}.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 83:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 83:9"/>Defeat them just as you helped Gideon defeat the Midianites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and just as you helped Barak defeat Sisera{,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the commander of the Canaanite king} Jabin at the Kishon River!
<verse eid="PSA 83:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 83:10"/>You destroyed those Canaanites at En Dor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their dead bodies rotted on the ground.
<verse eid="PSA 83:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 83:11"/>Kill the leaders of this invading army
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as Gideon killed Oreb and Zeeb, the Midianite commanders.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Defeat all their rulers just as Gideon defeated Zebah and Zalmunna{, the Midianite rulers}.
<verse eid="PSA 83:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 83:12"/>They too had said, “Let us take for ourselves
</para>
  <para style="q2">the land where God’s people dwell.”
<verse eid="PSA 83:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 83:13"/>My God, please defeat them so that they run away
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as tumbleweed rolls away
</para>
  <para style="q2">and just as chaff flies away in the wind!
<verse eid="PSA 83:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 83:14"/>Just as a forest fire burns down trees
</para>
  <para style="q2">and flames burn up the dry vegetation on hillsides,
<verse eid="PSA 83:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 83:15"/>make them run away afraid
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if a great storm were driving them off.
<verse eid="PSA 83:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 83:16"/>Completely disgrace them
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they will acknowledge who you are, Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 83:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 83:17"/>Embarrass them and make them always afraid.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Humiliate them until they die.
<verse eid="PSA 83:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 83:18"/>Then they will know that you alone, Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">are the Most High God who rules over everyone in the world.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 83:18"/><verse eid="PSA 83:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 83"/>
  <chapter number="84" style="c" sid="PSA 84"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: Accompany the song with a stringed instrument. One of the Korahites wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 84:1"/>Yahweh, commander of the heavenly armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">what a wonderful place your temple is!
<verse eid="PSA 84:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 84:2"/>I long greatly, deep inside,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to be in the courtyards of Yahweh’s temple.
</para>
  <para style="q1">With my whole being I call out
</para>
  <para style="q2">to the only true God.
<verse eid="PSA 84:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 84:3"/>Even little birds have built their nests near your temple,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that is where they are taking care of their babies.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, commander of the heavenly armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are my king and my God.
<verse eid="PSA 84:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 84:4"/>What a good life people have who live by your temple!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They worship you continually there.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 84:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 84:5"/>What a good life people have whom you make strong
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they can travel to your temple as they greatly desire!
<verse eid="PSA 84:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 84:6"/>As they pass through the {arid} Valley of Baca, they dig wells to look for water,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and God sends autumn rains that fill those wells with life-giving water.
<verse eid="PSA 84:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 84:7"/>They become stronger as they go,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and each of them arrives at the temple in Zion
</para>
  <para style="q2">where God is present.
<verse eid="PSA 84:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 84:8"/>Yahweh, you are the God who commands the heavenly armies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please answer my prayer.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are the God whom we Israelite people worship.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do what I ask.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 84:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 84:9"/>God, please treat favorably the king you have appointed
</para>
  <para style="q2">to protect us.
<verse eid="PSA 84:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 84:10"/>It is better be in your temple courtyards for a single day
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to be anywhere else for a thousand days.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I would rather stand at the entrance to the courtyard of my God’s temple
</para>
  <para style="q2">than stay in any of the {comfortable} homes where wicked people live.
<verse eid="PSA 84:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 84:11"/>Yahweh our God makes us prosper, just as the sun makes crops grow,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he protects us, just as a shield protects a warrior.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is kind to us and honors us.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh gives people who live rightly
</para>
  <para style="q2">every good thing that they need.
<verse eid="PSA 84:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 84:12"/>Yahweh, commander of the heavenly armies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">what a good life people have who trust you!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 84:12"/><verse eid="PSA 84:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 84"/>
  <chapter number="85" style="c" sid="PSA 85"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: One of the Korahites wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 85:1"/>Yahweh, you have brought back the Israelites who were exiles
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that this land can be prosperous again.
<verse eid="PSA 85:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 85:2"/>You forgave all the sins that your people committed.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 85:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 85:3"/>You completely ceased being angry with us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and stopped punishing us severely.
<verse eid="PSA 85:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 85:4"/>God, you are the one who saves us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please stop being upset with us, and make us strong again.
<verse eid="PSA 85:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 85:5"/>Please do not be continually angry with us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and with our children and grandchildren.
<verse eid="PSA 85:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 85:6"/>Please help us so that we will thrive again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then we, your people, will be happy because of you.
<verse eid="PSA 85:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 85:7"/>Yahweh, please treat us kindly as you promised
</para>
  <para style="q2">and rescue us from our troubles.
<verse eid="PSA 85:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 85:8"/>I am going to listen to what Yahweh, my God, says to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I believe he will say that he will make his people thrive if they are loyal to him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">However, they must not do foolish things anymore.
<verse eid="PSA 85:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 85:9"/>He is surely ready to help people who deeply respect him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then he will be gloriously present with us in our land.
<verse eid="PSA 85:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 85:10"/>He will be faithfully kind and true to us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will do what is right and make us peaceful.
<verse eid="PSA 85:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 85:11"/>People on earth will be faithful to God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and God will act justly toward us from heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 85:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 85:12"/>Yes, Yahweh will give us good things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and our land will produce abundant harvests.
<verse eid="PSA 85:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 85:13"/>As he considers what to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will recognize what the right thing is to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will do that.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 85:13"/><verse eid="PSA 85:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 85"/>
  <chapter number="86" style="c" sid="PSA 86"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 86:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A prayer of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I am poor and helpless,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please do what I ask.
<verse eid="PSA 86:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 86:2"/>I am loyal to you, so please protect me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I worship you as my God and I trust you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please save me.
<verse eid="PSA 86:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 86:3"/>I have been crying out to you continually, Lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please be kind to me.
<verse eid="PSA 86:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 86:4"/>I am asking you to help me, Lord, as someone who worships you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please make me happy by doing that.
<verse eid="PSA 86:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 86:5"/>Do this, Lord, because you are good and you forgive people’s sins.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You very faithfully love everyone who prays to you.
<verse eid="PSA 86:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 86:6"/>Yahweh, I am pleading with you in prayer to help me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please do what I ask.
<verse eid="PSA 86:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 86:7"/>Whenever I am in trouble, I call out to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I know that you will help me.
<verse eid="PSA 86:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 86:8"/>Lord, among all the gods that the nations worship,
</para>
  <para style="q2">there is none like you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">none of them has done the great things that you have done.
<verse eid="PSA 86:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 86:9"/>Lord, the nations that you have made
</para>
  <para style="q2">will all come and bow down before you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 86:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 86:10"/>They will do this because you are great and you do amazing things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are the only true God.
<verse eid="PSA 86:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 86:11"/>Yahweh, please teach me how you want me to live
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I will act properly, as you wish.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Give me a sincere desire to honor you.
<verse eid="PSA 86:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 86:12"/>Lord my God, I will thank you wholeheartedly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise you forever.
<verse eid="PSA 86:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 86:13"/>I will do that because you have been so faithfully kind to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have kept me from going way down into the place where dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 86:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 86:14"/>God, proud people are attacking me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, a group of cruel people is trying to kill me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">those people do not respect you.
<verse eid="PSA 86:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 86:15"/>But you, Lord, are a God who is merciful and kind.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You do not quickly become angry,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you are so faithfully kind and true to us.
<verse eid="PSA 86:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 86:16"/>Consider my situation and be kind to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">make me, your servant, strong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Help me as if I had been born in your household.
<verse eid="PSA 86:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 86:17"/>Do something to show that you are helping me
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that my enemies will see it, and it will embarrass them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I believe that you, Yahweh, will help me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and comfort me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 86:17"/><verse eid="PSA 86:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 86"/>
  <chapter number="87" style="c" sid="PSA 87"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 87:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">One of the Korahites wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh established his city on mountains that he made holy.
<verse eid="PSA 87:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 87:2"/>He loves the city of Zion
</para>
  <para style="q2">more than any other place where Israelites live.
<verse eid="PSA 87:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 87:3"/>People say wonderful things about this city that belongs to God.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 87:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 87:4"/>{Yahweh says,} “When I talk about people who know me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">this will include Egyptians and Babylonians.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Indeed, I will also say about Philistines and Tyrians and Cushites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">‘This person is a native of Zion.’”
<verse eid="PSA 87:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 87:5"/>People will say about Zion, “Every one of those people is a native of that city,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">and God Most High will personally keep Zion strong.
<verse eid="PSA 87:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 87:6"/>When Yahweh registers each of those people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will record, “This person is a native of Zion.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 87:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 87:7"/>Singers and musicians {will celebrate and say},
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Zion, everything that makes me flourish comes from you!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 87:7"/><verse eid="PSA 87:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 87"/>
  <chapter number="88" style="c" sid="PSA 88"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">One of the Korahites wrote this song. This is a note for the worship leader: The tune is “Weakness of Afflicting.” Heman the Ezrahite wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 88:1"/>Yahweh, you are the God who saves me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I continually ask you to help me.
<verse eid="PSA 88:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 88:2"/>Please pay attention to what I am saying as I pray to you.
<verse eid="PSA 88:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 88:3"/>I ask this because I have experienced so many bad things that I cannot endure any more;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am about to die and go to the place where dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 88:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 88:4"/>People expect me to die soon
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I have so little strength left.
<verse eid="PSA 88:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 88:5"/>It is as if I belong among dead people
</para>
  <para style="q2">who are lying in their graves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It seems that you are no longer aware of such people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you stop taking care of them.
<verse eid="PSA 88:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 88:6"/>It is as though you have thrown me down to the bottom of a deep, dark pit.
<verse eid="PSA 88:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 88:7"/>I feel as if you are angry with me, and that is like an oppressive burden to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if I am drowning in your anger.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 88:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 88:8"/>Because my illness is so unpleasant and you have not healed me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my friends stay away from me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am not able to leave my home {to visit anyone}.
<verse eid="PSA 88:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 88:9"/>My eyes are swollen because I cry so much.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, throughout the day I call out to you for help
</para>
  <para style="q2">as I spread out my hands toward you {in prayer}.
<verse eid="PSA 88:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 88:10"/>If I were to die, it would be too late for you to do a miracle to help me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Dead people do not come back to life and praise you!
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 88:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 88:11"/>Dead bodies in graves do not talk about how you faithfully love us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">In the place where dead people go, no one talks about how faithful you are.
<verse eid="PSA 88:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 88:12"/>No one in that dark place sees the amazing things you do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no one in the place where no one remembers anything knows how good you are.
<verse eid="PSA 88:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 88:13"/>But I {am still alive,} Yahweh, and I am calling out to you to help me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as if my prayer is already there waiting for you when you get up in the morning.
<verse eid="PSA 88:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 88:14"/>Yahweh, please do not reject me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do not ignore me!
<verse eid="PSA 88:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 88:15"/>Since I was young, I have been so ill that I have nearly died.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have been sick for so long with this terrible illness that you permit
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I have no more hope.
<verse eid="PSA 88:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 88:16"/>I feel as if you are very angry with me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This terrible illness that you permit has destroyed the good life I could have had.
<verse eid="PSA 88:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 88:17"/>The bad things that are happening to me are like floodwaters
</para>
  <para style="q2">that continually surround me and are about to drown me.
<verse eid="PSA 88:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 88:18"/>Because you have allowed this illness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">my friends and family members stay away from me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I can no longer see where they are.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 88:18"/><verse eid="PSA 88:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 88"/>
  <chapter number="89" style="c" sid="PSA 89"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">Ethan the Ezrahite wrote this song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 89:1"/>Yahweh, I will always sing about how faithfully you love your people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will tell my children and grandchildren that you always do what you promise.
<verse eid="PSA 89:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 89:2"/>I know that you will always love us faithfully.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Just as the sky is permanent, so you will always be faithful to us.
<verse eid="PSA 89:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 89:3"/>Yahweh has said, “I made a covenant with the man I chose {to be the king of Israel}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That was David, who loyally obeyed me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I made a solemn promise to him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 89:4"/>I said, ‘I will make sure that your descendants always rule as kings;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, I will make sure that your dynasty never ends.’”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 89:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 89:5"/>Yahweh, the angels in heaven praise you for the wonderful things you do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">When those holy beings gather, they celebrate how you always do what you promise.
<verse eid="PSA 89:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 89:6"/>No one in the sky is equal to Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">None of the heavenly beings is like Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 89:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 89:7"/>When the holy beings gather together, they all respect God greatly.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone around his throne honors him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 89:8"/>Yahweh, you are the God who commands the heavenly armies.
</para>
  <para style="q2">No one is as mighty as you are!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are always faithful in every way.
<verse eid="PSA 89:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 89:9"/>You control the sea so that it does not become too violent;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when its waves become too large, you make them smaller.
<verse eid="PSA 89:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 89:10"/>It was you who {put the world in order as you created it, as if you had} completely destroyed the sea monster Rahab;
</para>
  <para style="q2">You used your great power to defeat your enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 89:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 89:11"/>Because you created the world and everything in it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the sky belongs to you, and the earth also belongs to you.
<verse eid="PSA 89:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 89:12"/>You created the full extent of the world around us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You made everything to the north and to the south.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You made everything to the west, where Mount Tabor is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you made everything to the east, where Mount Hermon is.
</para>
  <para style="q1">People throughout the world joyfully praise you because of who you are.
<verse eid="PSA 89:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 89:13"/>You are very powerful; yes, you are very strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you use your power to do great things.
<verse eid="PSA 89:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 89:14"/>As you rule, you always do what is right and just,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you are always faithful and true in everything you do.
<verse eid="PSA 89:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 89:15"/>Yahweh, the people who worship you with joyful shouts have truly good lives;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they enjoy your favor as they live.
<verse eid="PSA 89:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 89:16"/>They rejoice continually because of who you are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they celebrate how you always do what is right.
<verse eid="PSA 89:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 89:17"/>You make your people strong and glorious,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because you were pleased with us, you gave us a good king.
<verse eid="PSA 89:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 89:18"/>The one who protects us belongs to you, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, our king belongs to you, the holy God whom we Israelites worship.
<verse eid="PSA 89:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 89:19"/>Long ago you spoke in a vision to the Israelites who were loyal to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You said, “I have given strength to a mighty warrior;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have chosen a young man from among the people {to be the king}.
<verse eid="PSA 89:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 89:20"/>I have found David, who loyally obeys me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have had people anoint him with my holy oil {to appoint him as king}.
<verse eid="PSA 89:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 89:21"/>I will always support him with my power;
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed, I will make him strong.
<verse eid="PSA 89:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 89:22"/>He will never have to pay tribute to a foreign ruler,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no wicked enemy will defeat him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 89:23"/>I will defeat his opponents when they fight against him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, I will destroy his enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 89:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 89:24"/>I will always be faithful to him and treat him kindly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will make him a great ruler by my own authority.
<verse eid="PSA 89:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 89:25"/>I will make his realm extend from the Great Sea to the Euphrates River.
<verse eid="PSA 89:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 89:26"/>He will call out to me, ‘You are my Father;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are my God, the one who protects me and saves me!’
<verse eid="PSA 89:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 89:27"/>For my part, I will treat him as if he were my firstborn son,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will make him the greatest of all the kings on the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 89:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 89:28"/>I will always love him faithfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will always honor my covenant with him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 89:29"/>I will make sure that his descendants always rule as kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that his dynasty lasts as long as the sky exists.
<verse eid="PSA 89:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 89:30"/>However, if his descendants disobey my instructions
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not live according to what I have decreed,
<verse eid="PSA 89:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 89:31"/>if they treat my decrees as something they can ignore,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and if they do not obey my commands,
<verse eid="PSA 89:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 89:32"/>then I will punish them to correct them
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of the wrong things they have done
</para>
  <para style="q2">as if I were hitting them with a rod.
<verse eid="PSA 89:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 89:33"/>But I will not stop faithfully loving David;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not fail to do what I promised {for his descendants}.
<verse eid="PSA 89:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 89:34"/>I will not break my covenant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no, I will not take back what I said.
<verse eid="PSA 89:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 89:35"/>I guaranteed my promise to David by my own holy character.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I said that I was not lying to him, and I meant it.
<verse eid="PSA 89:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 89:36"/>I promised solemnly that his descendants would rule as kings forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, I said that I would preserve his dynasty
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as I have made the sun to shine in the sky always.
<verse eid="PSA 89:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 89:37"/>The moon appears in the sky dependably each month,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and in the same way, David’s dynasty will always endure.”
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 89:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 89:38"/>Yet now it appears that you have completely rejected
</para>
  <para style="q2">David’s descendant who was our king.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It appears that you have abandoned him.
<verse eid="PSA 89:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 89:39"/>It seems as though you are disregarding the covenant you made with David.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have allowed his dynasty to end, as if you had not promised to preserve it.
<verse eid="PSA 89:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 89:40"/>You have allowed enemies to break down
</para>
  <para style="q2">all the walls that protected his city {of Jerusalem}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It had strong defenses, but you have allowed those enemies to reduce them to ruins.
<verse eid="PSA 89:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 89:41"/>Now people can come along and steal the things that remain in the city.
</para>
  <para style="q2">People in the surrounding countries are ridiculing us Israelites.
<verse eid="PSA 89:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 89:42"/>You have allowed our enemies to become strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they are celebrating how they have defeated us.
<verse eid="PSA 89:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 89:43"/>Our armies have had to retreat from battles
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you have not helped us when we fight.
<verse eid="PSA 89:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 89:44"/>Our kingdom is no longer glorious,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we no longer have a king.
<verse eid="PSA 89:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 89:45"/>We are no longer strong, as young men are.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This has disgraced us completely.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 89:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 89:46"/>Yahweh, please help us, and do not delay! Do not keep neglecting us!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not keep being so angry with us!
<verse eid="PSA 89:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 89:47"/>Please remember how short human lives are!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please remember that you created us human beings as mere mortals!
<verse eid="PSA 89:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 89:48"/>No one can live forever and never die;
</para>
  <para style="q2">everyone must go to the place where dead people are.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 89:48"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 89:49"/>Lord, you promised David that you would faithfully love us Israelites, and you did.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You always keep your promises{, so please help us}!
<verse eid="PSA 89:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 89:50"/>Lord, consider the insulting things that many people are saying
</para>
  <para style="q2">about us who loyally obey you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I deeply feel the pain of all those insults.
<verse eid="PSA 89:50"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 89:51"/>Yahweh, do something to stop your enemies
</para>
  <para style="q2">from mocking the actions of the king you appointed.
<verse eid="PSA 89:51"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 89:52"/>May people always bless Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Amen! Yes, amen!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 89:52"/><verse eid="PSA 89:52"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 89"/>
  <chapter number="90" style="c" sid="PSA 90"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Four

</para>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">A prayer by the prophet Moses
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 90:1"/>Lord, you have been like a home for us
</para>
  <para style="q2">throughout our generations.
<verse eid="PSA 90:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 90:2"/>Before you created the mountains,
</para>
  <para style="q2">before you formed the earth and everything that is in it,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you were eternally God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you will be God forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 90:3"/>{When people die,} you cause their corpses to become soil again;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you change their corpses to become dirt like that from which {the first} man was created.
<verse eid="PSA 90:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 90:4"/>When you consider time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">a thousand years are {as short as} one day that passes;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you consider that they are {as short as} a few hours in the night.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 90:5"/>You cause people to die suddenly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they live {only a short time} as a dream lasts {only a short time}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are like grass in the morning that comes and goes.
<verse eid="PSA 90:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 90:6"/>In the morning the grass sprouts and develops,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then in the evening it dries up and completely withers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 90:7"/>Similarly, {because of the sins that we commit,} you become angry with us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you terrify us and then you destroy us.
<verse eid="PSA 90:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 90:8"/>It is as though you place our sins in front of you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">spreading out even our secret sins where you can see them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 90:9"/>Because you are angry with us, you cause our lives to end;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the years that we live pass as quickly as a sigh passes.
<verse eid="PSA 90:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 90:10"/>People live for {only} seventy years;
</para>
  <para style="q2">if they are strong, {some of them live} for eighty years.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But throughout our time we have much pain and troubles;
</para>
  <para style="q2">our lives soon end, and we die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 90:11"/>No one has fully experienced the powerful things that you can do to people when you are angry with them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">No, people are not adequately afraid of how you can punish them because you are angry with them.
<verse eid="PSA 90:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 90:12"/>So teach us to realize that we live for only a short time
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that we may think wisely {about how we use our time}.
<verse eid="PSA 90:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 90:13"/>Yahweh, how long will you be angry with us?
</para>
  <para style="q1">Pity us who serve you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 90:14"/>Each morning, show us that it is enough for us if you love us faithfully as you have promised that you would do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Show us this} so that we may shout joyfully and be happy all during the years that we live.
<verse eid="PSA 90:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 90:15"/>Cause us now to be happy for as many years as you afflicted us and we experienced bad things.
<verse eid="PSA 90:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 90:16"/>Enable us who serve you to see the {great} things that you do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and enable our descendants to see your glorious power {also}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 90:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 90:17"/>Lord, our God, give us your blessings
</para>
  <para style="q2">and enable us to be successful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, cause us to be successful in everything that we do!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 90:17"/><verse eid="PSA 90:17"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 90"/>
  <chapter number="91" style="c" sid="PSA 91"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 91:1"/>Those people whom God Most High protects
</para>
  <para style="q2">will be able to rest safely because Shaddai cares for them.
<verse eid="PSA 91:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 91:2"/>I will declare to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“You protect me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are like a stronghold in which I am safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are my God, the one in whom I trust.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 91:3"/>He will rescue you from all hidden traps
</para>
  <para style="q2">and save you from deadly diseases.
<verse eid="PSA 91:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 91:4"/>He will protect you as a bird does who covers her young under her wings.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will be safe in his care.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As he faithfully does what he has promised, that is like a shield or strong wall that will protect you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 91:5"/>You will not be afraid of things that happen during the night that could terrorize you
</para>
  <para style="q2">or of arrows {that your enemies will shoot at you} during the day.
<verse eid="PSA 91:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 91:6"/>You will not be afraid of plagues that infect people in the night
</para>
  <para style="q2">or of other evil forces that kill people in the light of day.
<verse eid="PSA 91:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 91:7"/>Even if a thousand people fall dead alongside you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">even if ten thousand people are dying around you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the deadly thing will not harm you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 91:8"/>All you need to do is watch
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you will see that God is punishing evil people!
<verse eid="PSA 91:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 91:9"/>This is because you trust Yahweh, God Most High, who protects me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to also protect you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 91:10"/>Therefore, nothing evil will happen to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no plague will affect your family
<verse eid="PSA 91:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 91:11"/>because Yahweh will command his angels
</para>
  <para style="q2">to protect you in whatever you are doing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 91:12"/>They will even hold you up with their hands
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that you will not hurt your foot on a big stone.
<verse eid="PSA 91:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 91:13"/>Yahweh will not allow your enemies to harm you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">even if strong lions and poisonous snakes attack you, you will defeat them!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 91:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 91:14"/>Yahweh says, “I will rescue those who love me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will protect them because they know me.
<verse eid="PSA 91:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 91:15"/>When they call out to me, I will answer them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will help them when they are experiencing trouble;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will rescue them and honor them.
<verse eid="PSA 91:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 91:16"/>I will reward them by enabling them to live a long time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will save them.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 91:16"/><verse eid="PSA 91:16"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 91"/>
  <chapter number="92" style="c" sid="PSA 92"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm that is to be sung on Sabbath days.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 92:1"/>Yahweh, it is good for people to thank you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to sing as they praise you, the Most High God.
<verse eid="PSA 92:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 92:2"/>It is good to proclaim every morning that you faithfully love us
</para>
  <para style="q2">and to declare each night that everything that you say is true,
<verse eid="PSA 92:2"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 92:3"/>{singing} {to the music} of {instruments that have} ten {strings}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and of lyres
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and} with {musicians playing} melodies on a harp.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 92:4"/>I do this, Yahweh, because what you have done makes me happy;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I sing joyfully because of the things that you do.
<verse eid="PSA 92:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 92:5"/>Yahweh, the things that you do are great!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We cannot understand all that you think.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 92:6"/>These are things that foolish people do not know about,
</para>
  <para style="q2">things that dolts cannot understand:
<verse eid="PSA 92:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 92:7"/>{They do not understand that} when the number of wicked people increases as blades of grass increase,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {when it seems that} all those who do what is evil prosper,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh will destroy them forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 92:8"/>But Yahweh, you will rule forever.
<verse eid="PSA 92:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 92:9"/>Just look at your enemies, Yahweh! Your enemies will certainly die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will destroy everyone who does wicked things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 92:10"/>But you have caused me to be as strong as a wild ox;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you have caused me to be very joyful.
<verse eid="PSA 92:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 92:11"/>I have observed my enemies as they oppose me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I have heard those evil men.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 92:12"/>But righteous {people} will prosper like {flourishing} palm trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will grow like the {tall} cedar trees in Lebanon.
<verse eid="PSA 92:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 92:13"/>They belong to Yahweh as securely as if they were trees with roots deep in his temple grounds.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are as prosperous and healthy as if they were trees growing in our God’s courtyard.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 92:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 92:14"/>They are like trees that continue to bear fruit even when they are old.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They remain strong and full of energy, like trees that are full of sap and have abundant leaves.
<verse eid="PSA 92:14"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 92:15"/>That shows that Yahweh is just;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is like a huge rock behind which I am safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he never does anything that is unjust.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 92:15"/><verse eid="PSA 92:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 92"/>
  <chapter number="93" style="c" sid="PSA 93"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 93:1"/>Yahweh, you are the King!
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as though you are wearing royal robes that are majestic and powerful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You are the one who put the world firmly in place, and no one can move it {out of its place}.
<verse eid="PSA 93:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 93:2"/>You have been king since long ago;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have always existed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 93:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 93:3"/>Yahweh, the oceans rise up;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their waves {loudly} pound {against the shore};
</para>
  <para style="q2">{it is as though} they roar with a powerful voice.
<verse eid="PSA 93:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 93:4"/>But you are more powerful than the roar of those oceans;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are more powerful than the huge ocean waves!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are Yahweh, the one who is great and powerful!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 93:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 93:5"/>Yahweh, your laws are completely reliable;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your temple is a beautifully holy place.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{That will be true} forever.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 93:5"/><verse eid="PSA 93:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 93"/>
  <chapter number="94" style="c" sid="PSA 94"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 94:1"/>Yahweh, you are a God who punishes {your enemies}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So reveal {to them} who you are!
<verse eid="PSA 94:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 94:2"/>You are the one who judges all people on the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q1">so take action and give the arrogant people what they deserve.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 94:3"/>Yahweh, wicked people just continue to be glad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that is not right!
<verse eid="PSA 94:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 94:4"/>They abundantly speak arrogant things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all people who do evil things say that they are great people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 94:5"/>Yahweh, it is as though those wicked people were crushing us, your people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they distress the people who belong to you alone.
<verse eid="PSA 94:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 94:6"/>They murder widows, people from other countries,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and also young people who have no fathers.
<verse eid="PSA 94:6"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 94:7"/>Those wicked people think to themselves, “Yahweh does not see {any of this};
</para>
  <para style="q2">the God whom the Israelites worship does not notice {the evil things that we do}.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 94:8"/>You wicked people in Israel need to understand {what is right};
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have been stupid and foolish far too long!
<verse eid="PSA 94:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 94:9"/>Since Yahweh is the one who made ears,
</para>
  <para style="q2">of course he can hear {what you say}!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Not only that, he created eyes;
</para>
  <para style="q2">so of course he can see {the evil things that you do}!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 94:10"/>He corrects {the leaders of} other nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so he will punish {you}, as well.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He has taught people everything that they know,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so of course he knows everything {that you do}.
<verse eid="PSA 94:10"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 94:11"/>Yahweh knows everything that people are thinking;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he knows that what they think is evil and useless.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 94:12"/>Yahweh, how fortunate are those who allow you to discipline them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{how fortunate are} those whom you teach from your laws!
<verse eid="PSA 94:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 94:13"/>You relieve those people from bad things when they happen,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and someday you will punish the wicked people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and stop them from doing wicked things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 94:14"/>This will happen because Yahweh will not reject his people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will not desert those who belong to him.
<verse eid="PSA 94:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 94:15"/>Yes, someday judges will again decide matters fairly for people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all honest people will be pleased about that.
<verse eid="PSA 94:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 94:16"/>{But when evil people oppressed me,}
</para>
  <para style="q1">I could find no one to defend me
</para>
  <para style="q2">against the wicked things that evil people did to me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 94:17"/>If Yahweh had not helped me {at that time},
</para>
  <para style="q2">I would have gone quickly to the place where dead people say nothing.
<verse eid="PSA 94:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 94:18"/>Just when I thought, “I am about to die,”
</para>
  <para style="q2">then, Yahweh, you saved me by being faithful and loving to me.
<verse eid="PSA 94:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 94:19"/>Whenever I am very worried,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you comfort me and cause me to be happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 94:20"/>Corrupt rulers,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those who establish laws that allow people to do what is not right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">cannot be your friends.
<verse eid="PSA 94:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 94:21"/>They plot together how to destroy righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they declare that innocent people must die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 94:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 94:22"/>But Yahweh has become like a fortress for me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">my God is like a huge rock that protects me.
<verse eid="PSA 94:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 94:23"/>He will do to those wicked leaders the terrible things that they have done to others;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will get rid of them because they do wicked things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, Yahweh our God will get rid of them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 94:23"/><verse eid="PSA 94:23"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 94"/>
  <chapter number="95" style="c" sid="PSA 95"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 95:1"/>{Everyone,} come and let us sing to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let us shout joyfully to the one who protects us and saves us!
<verse eid="PSA 95:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 95:2"/>Let us thank him as we come before him
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sing joyful psalms as we praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 95:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 95:3"/>Because Yahweh is a great God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is a great king who rules over all other spirit beings.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 95:4"/>He controls the whole earth.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From the deepest places to the highest mountains, it belongs to him.
<verse eid="PSA 95:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 95:5"/>The seas are his because he is the one who made them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He also made the dry land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 95:6"/>{Everyone,} come, let us worship him and bow down {before him}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let us kneel before Yahweh, who is the one who made us.
<verse eid="PSA 95:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 95:7"/>{Do this} because he is our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we are the people whom he protects,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like sheep that a shepherd takes care of.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I desire that today you may hear what Yahweh is saying to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:7"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 95:8"/>He says, “Do not become stubborn as your ancestors did at Meribah,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and as they did long ago at Massah in the wilderness.
<verse eid="PSA 95:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 95:9"/>There your ancestors tested whether I would continue to be patient with them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They wanted to see if they could do evil things and not have me punish them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They did this even though they had seen me perform many miracles.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 95:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 95:10"/>For 40 years I was angry with those people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I said about them, ‘Those people are unreliable.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They completely refuse to obey my commands.’
<verse eid="PSA 95:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 95:11"/>So because I was very angry, I solemnly said about them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">‘They will never enter {the land of Canaan} where I would have allowed them to rest!’”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 95:11"/><verse eid="PSA 95:11"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 95"/>
  <chapter number="96" style="c" sid="PSA 96"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 96:1"/>Sing to Yahweh a new song!
</para>
  <para style="q1">All you people throughout the earth, sing to Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 96:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 96:2"/>Sing to Yahweh and praise him!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Every day proclaim to others that he has saved us.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 96:3"/>Tell about how glorious he is to all people groups;
</para>
  <para style="q2">tell all peoples everywhere the marvelous things that he has done.
<verse eid="PSA 96:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 96:4"/>Do this because Yahweh is great, and he deserves very much for people to praise him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">people should revere him more than all other gods.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 96:5"/>This is true because all of the gods that the other peoples worship are only idols,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but it is Yahweh who made the heavens!
<verse eid="PSA 96:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 96:6"/>Yahweh is magnificent and majestic.
</para>
  <para style="q2">His holy house shows how strong and beautiful he is.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 96:7"/>You peoples in nations all over the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q1">Proclaim that Yahweh is the one who is truly glorious and strong!
<verse eid="PSA 96:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 96:8"/>Praise Yahweh as he deserves for us to praise him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">bring an offering and come to his temple.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 96:9"/>Bow down before Yahweh because he is marvelously holy.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone on earth should tremble because of who he is.
<verse eid="PSA 96:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 96:10"/>Say to {all} the people groups, “Yahweh is the king!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">He put the world in its place, and nothing will ever be able to move it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He judges {all} the peoples fairly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 96:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 96:11"/>All the beings that are in the heavens should be glad, and all the people on the earth should rejoice.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The oceans and all the creatures that are in the oceans should roar {to praise Yahweh}.
<verse eid="PSA 96:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 96:12"/>Let it be as though the fields and everything that is in them are rejoicing.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then let it be as though all the trees in the forests are singing joyfully
<verse eid="PSA 96:12"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 96:13"/>in front of Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q1">They should do this because he is coming to judge everyone on the earth, and this is certain.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will judge all the people fairly according to what he knows is true.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 96:13"/><verse eid="PSA 96:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 96"/>
  <chapter number="97" style="c" sid="PSA 97"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 97:1"/>Yahweh is the king!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I want everyone on the earth to be glad
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I want all the people who live on the land in and around the oceans to {also} rejoice {about that}!
<verse eid="PSA 97:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 97:2"/>There are very dark clouds all around him;
</para>
  <para style="q1">he always rules righteously and justly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 97:3"/>He sends fire out in front of him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {that fire} burns all of his enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 97:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 97:4"/>All around the world he sends his bright lightning;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people on the earth see {it}, and it causes them {to be afraid and} to tremble.
<verse eid="PSA 97:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 97:5"/>The mountains melt like wax before Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is the Lord who rules over all of the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 97:6"/>Everything that people can see in the heavens makes it clear that he is righteous,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all the people groups see how glorious he is.
<verse eid="PSA 97:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 97:7"/>Everyone who worships carved images should be ashamed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all those who are proud of their useless false gods should be ashamed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">All those gods should bow down to worship Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 97:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 97:8"/>The people of Jerusalem heard {Yahweh’s just decrees} and they were happy {about them};
</para>
  <para style="q2">people in the other cities in Judah also {heard and} rejoiced
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you judge {people} justly, Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 97:9"/>Of course, Yahweh, you are the supreme king who rules over all the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are far more powerful than any other spirit beings.
<verse eid="PSA 97:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 97:10"/>All you who love Yahweh, you must hate every evil thing {that people do}!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh protects those who are faithful to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he rescues them when wicked people try to harm them.
<verse eid="PSA 97:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 97:11"/>He makes good things happen for righteous people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he causes those who are honest to rejoice.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 97:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 97:12"/>You righteous people, let Yahweh make you glad,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and thank him, the one we all know to be holy!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 97:12"/><verse eid="PSA 97:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 97"/>
  <chapter number="98" style="c" sid="PSA 98"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 98:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Sing to Yahweh a new song
</para>
  <para style="q1">because he has done wonderful things!
</para>
  <para style="q1">By being powerfully holy he has saved {his people}.
<verse eid="PSA 98:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 98:2"/>Yahweh has shown openly that he saves {his people};
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has revealed to people all over the world that he always does what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 98:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 98:3"/>He is always loyal to his covenant to be faithful to the Israelite people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even the people who live in the most remote places of the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">will see that our God saves {his people}.
<verse eid="PSA 98:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 98:4"/>All you people everywhere should shout joyfully to Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q1">praise him while you sing joyfully and make music!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 98:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 98:5"/>Play to Yahweh on a harp,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and sing along as you play.
<verse eid="PSA 98:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 98:6"/>{Some of you should} blow trumpets and ram’s horns
</para>
  <para style="q2">{while others} shout joyfully to Yahweh, our king!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 98:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 98:7"/>The oceans and all {the creatures} that are in the oceans should roar {to praise Yahweh}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The earth itself and everyone on it should do the same!
<verse eid="PSA 98:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 98:8"/>It should seem as though the rivers were clapping their hands {to praise Yahweh}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that the hills were singing together joyfully
<verse eid="PSA 98:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 98:9"/>before Yahweh because he will come to judge everyone on the earth!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will judge all the people in the world justly and fairly.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 98:9"/><verse eid="PSA 98:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 98"/>
  <chapter number="99" style="c" sid="PSA 99"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 99:1"/>Yahweh is the supreme king,
</para>
  <para style="q1">so all people should tremble {in front of him}!
</para>
  <para style="q1">He sits on his throne {in the temple} above the {statues of} the cherubim,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so the earth should quake!
<verse eid="PSA 99:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 99:2"/>Yahweh is a mighty king in Jerusalem;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is also the supreme ruler of all peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 99:2"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 99:3"/>They should praise you, Yahweh, because you are great and awesome!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They should say,} “He is holy!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 99:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 99:4"/>Yahweh is a mighty king {because} he loves what is just.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You, Yahweh, have established what is fair.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have acted justly and righteously for the people of Israel.
<verse eid="PSA 99:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 99:5"/>Praise Yahweh, the God whom we worship!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Bow down to him at {the temple, which is} his footstool.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is holy!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 99:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 99:6"/>Moses and Aaron were two of his priests;
</para>
  <para style="q1">Samuel also was someone who prayed to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those {three} cried out to Yahweh {to help them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he helped them.
<verse eid="PSA 99:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 99:7"/>He spoke to Moses and Aaron from the cloud that was {like} a {huge} pillar.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They obeyed {all} the laws and commandments that he gave to them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 99:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 99:8"/>Yahweh, our God, you helped Moses, Aaron, and Samuel
</para>
  <para style="q2">{when they cried out to you to help them};
</para>
  <para style="q1">you are the God who forgave them {for the sins that they had committed},
</para>
  <para style="q1">even though you punished them for the things that they did that were wrong.
<verse eid="PSA 99:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 99:9"/>Praise Yahweh, our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and worship him {at the temple} on his holy hill;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{it is right to do that} because Yahweh, our God, is holy!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 99:9"/><verse eid="PSA 99:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 99"/>
  <chapter number="100" style="c" sid="PSA 100"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 100:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of thanksgiving.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Everyone in the world should shout joyfully to Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 100:1"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 100:2"/>We should worship Yahweh gladly!
</para>
  <para style="q2">We should come before him singing joyfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 100:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 100:3"/>We should acknowledge that Yahweh is God.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is he who made us; we did not make ourselves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We are the people who belong to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we are like sheep that he cares for as a shepherd does.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 100:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 100:4"/>Enter the gates {of his temple} thanking him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">enter the courtyard {of his temple} singing songs to praise him!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Thank him and praise him
<verse eid="PSA 100:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 100:5"/>because Yahweh always does good things for us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will faithfully love us forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will always fulfill everything that he has promised.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 100:5"/><verse eid="PSA 100:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 100"/>
  <chapter number="101" style="c" sid="PSA 101"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 101:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">David wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I will praise you with singing!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing that you are just and that you faithfully love us.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 101:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 101:2"/>I will examine how to live in the right way.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, I need you to come and help me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">In everything that I do in my household, I will sincerely try to do what is right.
<verse eid="PSA 101:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 101:3"/>I will not tempt myself to do any bad thing.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I hate any kind of sinful action;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not allow myself to think about doing those things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 101:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 101:4"/>I will not be dishonest,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will not do anything evil.
<verse eid="PSA 101:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 101:5"/>I will get rid of anyone who secretly slanders someone else.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will not tolerate anyone who is proud or arrogant.
<verse eid="PSA 101:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 101:6"/>I look for people in this land who are loyal to God
</para>
  <para style="q1">to help me rule {this nation}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Only people who behave honestly may work for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 101:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 101:7"/>I will not allow anyone who deceives others {to work} in my palace,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and I will not allow anyone who tells lies to continue working for me.
<verse eid="PSA 101:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 101:8"/>I will start every day by working to get rid of all of the wicked people in this land.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will expel everyone who does what is evil from this city that belongs to Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 101:8"/><verse eid="PSA 101:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 101"/>
  <chapter number="102" style="c" sid="PSA 102"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">Someone wrote this prayer when he was feeling discouraged and pleads for Yahweh to help him.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 102:1"/>Yahweh, please listen to me when I pray to you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">yes, please be attentive as I cry out to you!
<verse eid="PSA 102:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 102:2"/>When distressing things happen to me, please do not ignore me!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Listen to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and answer me quickly as soon as I call out to you!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 102:3"/>Please hurry because my life is ending as quickly as smoke that disappears;
</para>
  <para style="q1">my body feels like a fire is burning it.
<verse eid="PSA 102:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 102:4"/>I feel as though I am withering away like grass that the sun has scorched.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You see, I do not even remember to eat any food.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 102:5"/>I groan aloud so much
</para>
  <para style="q2">that my bones protrude under my skin.
<verse eid="PSA 102:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 102:6"/>I am {lonely and despised} like an owl in the desert;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have become like a screech owl in the ruins {of a town}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 102:7"/>I lie awake {at night};
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am like a lonely bird sitting on a housetop.
<verse eid="PSA 102:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 102:8"/>During the whole of each day my enemies insult me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Those who make fun of me use my name when they curse people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">saying, “May you be like him.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9-10" style="v" sid="PSA 102:9-10"/>It feels as though you have picked me up and thrown me away!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Because you are so very angry with me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">my food tastes like ashes
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my tears fall into my drink.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:9-10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 102:11"/>My time to remain alive is {coming to an end}
</para>
  <para style="q2">like an evening shadow {that will soon be gone}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have withered as grass withers {in the hot sun}.
<verse eid="PSA 102:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 102:12"/>But Yahweh, you will rule forever on your royal throne;
</para>
  <para style="q1">people of all times will talk about you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 102:13"/>You yourself will now act and be merciful to the people of Jerusalem;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will do this because it is now the time that you have set
</para>
  <para style="q1">for you to be kind to them.
<verse eid="PSA 102:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 102:14"/>It is true that we who serve you love everything about Jerusalem.

<verse eid="PSA 102:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 102:15"/>Yahweh, someday the people of all nations will revere you,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and all the kings on the earth will recognize how very glorious you are.
<verse eid="PSA 102:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 102:16"/>You see, it is Yahweh who builds Jerusalem;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will appear {there} gloriously.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 102:17"/>Yahweh listens to the prayers of {his} people who are homeless.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He does not ignore them
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they pray for him to help them.
<verse eid="PSA 102:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 102:18"/>I will write these things down
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that people in future years will know {what he has done},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{in order that} people who are not born yet will praise Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 102:19"/>{They will describe} how Yahweh looked down from his holy place in heaven
</para>
  <para style="q1">and saw {what was happening on} the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 102:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 102:20"/>Yahweh looked down in order to help the groaning prisoners.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He looked down in order to set free the people whom their enemies were about to kill.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 102:21"/>As a result, people in Jerusalem will tell what Yahweh has done and praise him for it.
<verse eid="PSA 102:21"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 102:22"/>This will happen when many peoples, including those from other kingdoms, gather to worship Yahweh together.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 102:23"/>{But now} he has caused me to become weak while I am still young;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I think that} I will not remain alive very long.
<verse eid="PSA 102:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 102:24"/>I say {to you}, “My God, do not let me die when I am only half-way through my lifetime!
</para>
  <para style="q2">In contrast, you live forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 102:25"/>You created the world long ago,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you are the one who made the heavens.
<verse eid="PSA 102:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 102:26"/>As for the earth and the heavens, they will disappear, but as for you, you will remain.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of it will wear out as clothes wear out.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You will get rid of them as people get rid of old clothes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will no longer exist.
<verse eid="PSA 102:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 102:27"/>But you are Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will always be.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 102:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 102:28"/>The children of those who worship you will live safely {in Jerusalem},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and you will protect their descendants as they live in your presence.”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 102:28"/><verse eid="PSA 102:28"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 102"/>
  <chapter number="103" style="c" sid="PSA 103"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 103:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm of David
</para>
  <para style="q1">I tell myself, “Praise Yahweh!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">To everything that is within me, I say, “Praise him because he is holy!”
<verse eid="PSA 103:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 103:2"/>I tell myself, “Praise Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and think about all of the kind things that he has done for me.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 103:3"/>He forgives all of my sins,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he heals me from all of my sicknesses.
<verse eid="PSA 103:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 103:4"/>He rescues me from things that would kill me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he blesses me by faithfully loving me and acting mercifully to me.
<verse eid="PSA 103:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 103:5"/>He gives me plenty of good things {during my entire life}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He makes me feel young {and strong} {as though I could fly high} like an eagle.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 103:6"/>It is Yahweh who does all this! He does what is right and judges justly for all those whom people have been treating unfairly.
<verse eid="PSA 103:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 103:7"/>{Long ago} he revealed to Moses the way that he works;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he showed to {our ancestors,} the people of Israel, the {mighty} things that he can do.
<verse eid="PSA 103:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 103:8"/>Yahweh acts mercifully and kindly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not quickly get angry {when we sin};
</para>
  <para style="q1">he always faithfully loves us.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 103:9"/>He will not always rebuke us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will not remain angry forever.
<verse eid="PSA 103:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 103:10"/>He does not punish us for our sins nearly as much as we deserve.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 103:11"/>Indeed, as high as the sky is above the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is how much Yahweh faithfully loves everyone who reveres him.
<verse eid="PSA 103:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 103:12"/>He has taken away the guilt for our sins
</para>
  <para style="q2">and put it as far from us as the east is from the west.
<verse eid="PSA 103:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 103:13"/>Just as parents always love their children,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh always loves those who revere him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 103:14"/>Indeed, he certainly knows how weak we are;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he remembers that he created us from dust.
<verse eid="PSA 103:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 103:15"/>The lifetime of humans passes quickly, like that of grass.
</para>
  <para style="q1">We are like wild flowers that bloom for a short while,
<verse eid="PSA 103:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 103:16"/>but then the wind blows over them and they disappear,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no one knows they were ever there.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 103:17"/>But Yahweh will continue to faithfully love
</para>
  <para style="q2">all those who revere him, forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will do what is right for generations of their children,
<verse eid="PSA 103:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 103:18"/>that is, he will act that way to all those who obey the covenant that he made with them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, he will act that way to all those who obey what he has commanded us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 103:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 103:19"/>Yahweh rules as king in heaven.
</para>
  <para style="q1">From there, he rules over everything.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 103:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 103:20"/>Praise Yahweh, you angels who belong to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">You powerful warriors who do what he tells you to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you who obey what he commands!
<verse eid="PSA 103:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 103:21"/>Praise Yahweh, all you armies of his angels,
</para>
  <para style="q1">you who serve him and do what he desires!
<verse eid="PSA 103:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 103:22"/>All of the creatures that Yahweh has created should praise him!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They should praise him in every place where he rules, {which is everywhere}!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I say to myself, “Praise Yahweh!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 103:22"/><verse eid="PSA 103:22"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 103"/>
  <chapter number="104" style="c" sid="PSA 104"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 104:1"/>I tell myself, “Bless Yahweh!”
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, my God, you are magnificent!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are more majestic than a king appearing in his beautiful robes!
<verse eid="PSA 104:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 104:2"/>You use light {itself} as your robe;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you spread out {all of} heaven as your tent.
<verse eid="PSA 104:2"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 104:3"/>The rain clouds are like the upper rooms of your palace.
</para>
  <para style="q1">The clouds are like chariots for you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the wind is like a bird that takes you wherever you want to go.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 104:4"/>You send the winds like your messengers,
</para>
  <para style="q1">{and you control} fire as your servant.
<verse eid="PSA 104:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 104:5"/>You created the world to be secure,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that nothing can ever move it from its place.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 104:6"/>Later, you covered the earth with a flood, like covering someone with clothing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">water even covered the mountains.
<verse eid="PSA 104:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 104:7"/>Then you commanded the water, and it receded;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, you spoke loudly,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and the water rushed away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 104:8"/>Part of the water ascended {to its place} above the mountains,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and part of it descended the valleys {to its place in the earth}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of it went {back} to the place that you had determined for it.
<verse eid="PSA 104:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 104:9"/>Then you set a boundary for the water that it cannot cross over.
</para>
  <para style="q2">That boundary ensures that the water will never again cover the whole earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 104:10"/>You make the springs that pour water into the stream beds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their water flows between the mountains.
<verse eid="PSA 104:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 104:11"/>Those streams provide water for all of his wild animals to drink.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The wild donkeys {drink the water and} are no longer thirsty.
<verse eid="PSA 104:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 104:12"/>Birds make their nests beside the streams.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They sing among the branches {of the trees}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 104:13"/>From the heavens you send rain down on the mountains.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As a result of doing this, you satisfy all of the creatures on earth {with many good things}.
<verse eid="PSA 104:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 104:14"/>You make grass to grow for the cattle {to eat},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you make plants to grow for people to cultivate,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they can make bread from {those plants that grew in} the soil.
<verse eid="PSA 104:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 104:15"/>You give us {grapes that produce} wine that makes us cheerful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you give us {olives that produce} oil to make our faces shine,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you give us {grain to make} bread that makes us strong.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 104:16"/>Yahweh, you send plenty of rain to water
</para>
  <para style="q2">your cedar trees that you planted in Lebanon.
<verse eid="PSA 104:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 104:17"/>Birds make their nests in those trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and storks make their nests in the cypress trees.
<verse eid="PSA 104:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 104:18"/>High up in the mountains is where the wild goats live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and hyraxes live in the rocky cliffs.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 104:19"/>Yahweh, you made the moon to indicate the times for our festivals,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you made the sun to always go down at the right time.
<verse eid="PSA 104:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 104:20"/>You bring darkness, and it becomes night
</para>
  <para style="q2">when all of your forest animals prowl around.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 104:21"/>The young lions roar then as they seek their prey,
</para>
  <para style="q2">looking for the food that you have provided for them.
<verse eid="PSA 104:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 104:22"/>At dawn, they go back to their dens and lie down.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 104:23"/>{That is when} people go to their work;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they do their work until it is evening.
<verse eid="PSA 104:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 104:24"/>Yahweh, you have made so many different kinds of things!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You were very wise as you made them all.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The earth is full of the creatures that you made.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 104:25"/>We see the ocean, which is vastly wide between its shores!
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is full of many kinds of wriggling creatures,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so many that no one can count them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There are creatures ranging from small to big.
<verse eid="PSA 104:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 104:26"/>Ships sail on the sea.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Leviathan is also there, the creature that you made to splash around in it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 104:27"/>All of these creatures depend on you
</para>
  <para style="q2">to give them the food that they need at the right time.
<verse eid="PSA 104:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 104:28"/>When you give them the food that they need,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then they gather it.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You give it to them freely.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They eat until they are full of your good things.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 104:29"/>But when you refuse to give food to them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they panic.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When you cause them to stop breathing, they die;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their bodies decay and become part of the soil.
<verse eid="PSA 104:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 104:30"/>When you cause {newborn} creatures to begin to breathe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they begin to live.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You give new life to {all the living creatures on} the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 104:31"/>I want all of Yahweh’s creatures to glorify him forever!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I want Yahweh to rejoice about everything that he has created!
<verse eid="PSA 104:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 104:32"/>He makes the earth shake just by looking at it!
</para>
  <para style="q2">When he {merely} touches the mountains they start to burn!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 104:33"/>I will sing to Yahweh as long as I live.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise my God until the day that I die.
<verse eid="PSA 104:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 104:34"/>May Yahweh be pleased by all {these things} that I have thought about him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As for me, I will rejoice because I know him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 104:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 104:35"/>However, I want sinners to disappear from the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for there to be no more wicked people!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I tell myself, “Bless Yahweh!”
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 104:35"/><verse eid="PSA 104:35"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 104"/>
  <chapter number="105" style="c" sid="PSA 105"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 105:1"/>Give thanks to Yahweh; worship him and pray to him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Tell everyone in the world what he has done!
<verse eid="PSA 105:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 105:2"/>Sing to him; praise him with instruments;
</para>
  <para style="q2">tell others about all of his wonderful miracles!
<verse eid="PSA 105:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 105:3"/>Be proud of Yahweh, who is the holy one.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You people who worship Yahweh, rejoice!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 105:4"/>Ask Yahweh to help you and to make you strong;
</para>
  <para style="q2">always try to be with him!
<verse eid="PSA 105:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5-6" style="v" sid="PSA 105:5-6"/>You people who are descendants of Yahweh’s servant Abraham,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you descendants of Jacob, the people whom Yahweh has chosen,
</para>
  <para style="q2">think about all of the wonderful things that he has done;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he performed miracles, and he proclaimed {righteous} judgments.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:5-6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 105:7"/>He is Yahweh, the God whom we worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">He rules over people throughout the earth.
<verse eid="PSA 105:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 105:8"/>He never forgets the covenant that he made;
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is, he will maintain what he promised for countless generations.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 105:9"/>That is the covenant that he made with Abraham,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that he repeated with an oath to Isaac.
<verse eid="PSA 105:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 105:10"/>Then he repeated it as a reliable covenant with Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is, with Israel, and it was a covenant that would last forever.
<verse eid="PSA 105:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 105:11"/>What Yahweh said to them was, “I will give to you the region of Canaan;
</para>
  <para style="q2">that will be what you {and your descendants} inherit from me.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 105:12"/>Yahweh said that to the people of Israel when there were only a few of them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They were just a tiny group of people who were living in that land like strangers.
<verse eid="PSA 105:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 105:13"/>They continually wandered from one place to another,
</para>
  <para style="q2">living in various kingdoms and people groups.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 105:14"/>But Yahweh did not allow others to oppress the people of Israel.
</para>
  <para style="q2">On their behalf, he warned kings {by saying to them},
<verse eid="PSA 105:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 105:15"/>“Do not harm the people whom I have chosen!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do nothing bad to my prophets!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 105:16"/>Yahweh created a famine in the land of Canaan,
</para>
  <para style="q1">that is, all of the people there had no food to eat.

<verse eid="PSA 105:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 105:17"/>{So the people of Israel went to Egypt, but} before they went, Yahweh had already sent someone {there}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He sent} Joseph, whom his brothers had sold to be a slave.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 105:18"/>{Later, while Joseph was in prison in Egypt,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">the guards trapped his feet in shackles,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and they put an iron collar around his neck.
<verse eid="PSA 105:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 105:19"/>{Joseph was in prison} until the time
</para>
  <para style="q1">when the events that he had predicted happened.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh spoke to him {during this time} and taught Joseph to trust him more.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 105:20"/>The king of Egypt, the ruler of the people, commanded his servants
</para>
  <para style="q2">who went to the prison and set Joseph free.
<verse eid="PSA 105:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 105:21"/>Then the king chose Joseph as the one to decide about everything in the king’s household,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is, to be in charge of everything that the king possessed.
<verse eid="PSA 105:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 105:22"/>The king permitted Joseph to command the king’s officials
</para>
  <para style="q2">to do anything that Joseph wanted them to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Joseph taught the king’s advisors how to be wise.
<verse eid="PSA 105:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 105:23"/>{Later, Joseph’s father} Jacob, also called Israel, arrived in Egypt.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He lived like a foreigner in that land that belonged to the descendants of Ham.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 105:24"/>Over the years, Yahweh caused the descendants of Jacob to become very numerous.
</para>
  <para style="q2">As a result, the enemies of the people of Israel considered that the people of Israel were becoming too strong.
<verse eid="PSA 105:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 105:25"/>So Yahweh caused the rulers of Egypt to hate Yahweh’s people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they devised ways to oppress his people.
<verse eid="PSA 105:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 105:26"/>But then Yahweh sent his servant Moses
</para>
  <para style="q2">along with {Moses’ older brother} Aaron, whom Yahweh had also chosen {to serve him}.
<verse eid="PSA 105:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 105:27"/>Those two performed Yahweh’s amazing miracles among the people of Egypt
</para>
  <para style="q2">in that land where the descendants of Ham lived.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 105:28"/>Yahweh sent darkness so that the land of Egypt was dark,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Moses and Aaron obeyed what Yahweh told them to do.
<verse eid="PSA 105:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 105:29"/>Yahweh caused all of the water in Egypt to become blood,
</para>
  <para style="q2">which caused all of their fish to die.
<verse eid="PSA 105:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 105:30"/>Then he caused the land to become full of frogs;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the royal family even had frogs in their bedrooms!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 105:31"/>Then Yahweh commanded {that flies come}, and {swarms of} flies descended {on the people of Egypt}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Gnats also swarmed across the whole country.
<verse eid="PSA 105:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 105:32"/>Yahweh sent them hail instead of rain,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he started fires that burned throughout their land.
<verse eid="PSA 105:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 105:33"/>The hail ruined their grapevines, fig trees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and destroyed all the other trees in their country.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 105:34"/>Yahweh commanded locusts to come, and hordes of them came of different kinds;
</para>
  <para style="q2">so many came that no one could count them.
<verse eid="PSA 105:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 105:35"/>The locusts ate every green plant in their land,
</para>
  <para style="q2">including all of the crops.
<verse eid="PSA 105:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 105:36"/>Then Yahweh killed every firstborn son, the one who first demonstrated that the man was virile, {in every house} of the people of Egypt.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 105:37"/>Then Yahweh brought the Israelite people out {from Egypt}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They were carrying {many heavy things made of} silver and gold {that the people of Egypt had given to them},
</para>
  <para style="q1">and yet none of his people stumbled as they went.
<verse eid="PSA 105:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 105:38"/>The people of Egypt were glad when the Israelite people left
</para>
  <para style="q2">because the people of Egypt had become very afraid of the Israelites.
<verse eid="PSA 105:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 105:39"/>{Then} Yahweh spread a cloud to cover the Israelites;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and at night {it became} a {big} fire {in the sky} to give them light.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 105:40"/>{Then} the Israelites asked {for meat to eat},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh sent {flocks of} quail to them,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he gave them plenty of {manna} bread from the sky {each morning}.
<verse eid="PSA 105:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 105:41"/>{One day} Yahweh split open a rock, and water poured out {from the opening for the people to drink}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The water became a river flowing in the desert.
<verse eid="PSA 105:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 105:42"/>Yahweh did those things because he continually thought about the sacred promise that he had given to his servant, Abraham.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 105:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 105:43"/>So his people were joyful as Yahweh brought them out {from Egypt}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">These people whom he had chosen were shouting joyfully as they went.
<verse eid="PSA 105:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 105:44"/>Then Yahweh gave to the people of Israel the land that had belonged to the people groups {that lived there in Canaan}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So the Israelites took over the fields that those peoples had planted.
<verse eid="PSA 105:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 105:45"/>Yahweh did all these things
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that his people would do all the things that he had commanded them to do.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 105:45"/><verse eid="PSA 105:45"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 105"/>
  <chapter number="106" style="c" sid="PSA 106"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 106:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Thank Yahweh because he is good
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because he faithfully loves us forever!
<verse eid="PSA 106:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 106:2"/>Because Yahweh has done so many great things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">no one can tell all the great things that Yahweh has done,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no one can praise him enough.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 106:3"/>How happy are those who act fairly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">always doing what is right!
<verse eid="PSA 106:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 106:4"/>Yahweh, be kind to me when you help your people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Include me when you rescue them!
<verse eid="PSA 106:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 106:5"/>Allow me to see the people whom you have chosen become prosperous again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Allow me to be happy with the people of your nation when they become happy again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Allow me to praise you along with all those others who belong to you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 106:6"/>We have sinned just as our ancestors did;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we have done all kinds of evil.
<verse eid="PSA 106:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 106:7"/>Our ancestors did not appreciate the wonderful things that you did when they were in Egypt.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They forgot about the many times that you showed that you faithfully loved them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Instead, when they were at the Sea of Reeds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they rebelled against you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 106:8"/>Even so, he rescued them because of who he is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that he could show that he is very powerful.
<verse eid="PSA 106:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 106:9"/>He rebuked the Sea of Reeds and it became dry.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then he led our ancestors through it and even the deepest parts were as dry as a desert.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 106:10"/>In that way he rescued them from their hateful enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 106:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 106:11"/>Then their enemies drowned under the water {of the Sea of Reeds};
</para>
  <para style="q2">not one of them remained {alive}.
<verse eid="PSA 106:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 106:12"/>When that happened, our ancestors believed that Yahweh had truly done for them what he had promised to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they sang to praise him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 106:13"/>But they soon forgot what he had done for them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they did things without waiting to find out what Yahweh wanted them to do.
<verse eid="PSA 106:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 106:14"/>They intensely wanted certain foods in the wilderness.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They did evil things there that challenged God to punish them.
<verse eid="PSA 106:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 106:15"/>So he gave them what they requested,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but then he made many of them sick so that they died.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 106:16"/>Later when some of the men in the camp became resentful of Moses
</para>
  <para style="q1">and of {his older brother} Aaron, who was dedicated to serve Yahweh {by being a priest},
<verse eid="PSA 106:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 106:17"/>the ground opened up and Dathan fell into it
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it also buried Abiram and his people.
<verse eid="PSA 106:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 106:18"/>God made a fire start among their people
</para>
  <para style="q2">that burned up all the wicked people {who agreed with them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 106:19"/>Then the Israelite leaders made a metal statue of a calf at Mount Horeb
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they worshiped it.
<verse eid="PSA 106:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 106:20"/>So instead of worshiping their glorious God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they worshiped a statue of a bull that eats grass!
<verse eid="PSA 106:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 106:21"/>They ignored God, who had rescued them by the great miracles that he performed in Egypt.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 106:22"/>They stopped thinking about the wonderful things that he did for them in Egypt
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the amazing things that he did for them at the Sea of Reeds.
<verse eid="PSA 106:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 106:23"/>Because of that, God said that he would get rid of the Israelites;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Moses, whom God had chosen {to serve him},
</para>
  <para style="q2">confronted God to persuade him not to destroy {them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 106:24"/>Then our ancestors refused to enter the beautiful land {of Canaan}
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they did not believe that God would fulfill his promise {that he would enable them to take the land from the people who were living there}.
<verse eid="PSA 106:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 106:25"/>Instead, they stayed in their tents and complained.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They did not obey what Yahweh said that they should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 106:26"/>So Yahweh solemnly swore to them
</para>
  <para style="q2">that he would cause them to die there in the wilderness,
<verse eid="PSA 106:26"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 106:27"/>and that he would spread their descendants among the people of other nations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, that he would disperse them in those {foreign} lands.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 106:28"/>Later the Israelite people began worshiping the statue of Baal at Mount Peor,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they ate meat that had been sacrificed to dead {ancestors}.
<verse eid="PSA 106:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 106:29"/>When the people did these things, that made Yahweh angry,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so {again} he caused many of them to get a terrible disease.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 106:30"/>But Phinehas stood up and punished {the ones who had sinned},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and as a result the plague ended.
<verse eid="PSA 106:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 106:31"/>Because of what Phinehas did, people have considered him to be a righteous man,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and people in all future years will continue to remember him as righteous.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 106:32"/>Then at Meribah, where the water came out {of the rock}, our ancestors caused Yahweh to become angry {again},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Moses suffered because of what they did.
<verse eid="PSA 106:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 106:33"/>Moses suffered because they caused him to become very angry,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he said things that were foolish.
<verse eid="PSA 106:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 106:34"/>Our ancestors did not destroy the other people groups
</para>
  <para style="q2">as Yahweh had told them to do.
<verse eid="PSA 106:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 106:35"/>Instead, the men married women from those people groups,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they started doing the {evil} things that those people did.
<verse eid="PSA 106:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 106:36"/>Our ancestors worshiped the idols of those people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that is how they began to reject Yahweh and his ways.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 106:37"/>{Many of} the Israelites sacrificed their sons and daughters to the demons {that those idols represented}.
<verse eid="PSA 106:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 106:38"/>They killed their own sons and daughters, who had done nothing wrong,
</para>
  <para style="q1">by offering them as sacrifices to the idols of the Canaanites.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because of those murders, the land of Canaan became defiled.
<verse eid="PSA 106:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 106:39"/>Because of what they did they made it impossible for Yahweh to accept them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">By worshiping idols instead of faithfully worshiping only Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they became like prostitutes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 106:40"/>So Yahweh became very angry with his people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he was completely disgusted with them.
<verse eid="PSA 106:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 106:41"/>As a result, he allowed other people groups to conquer our ancestors,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that those who hated our ancestors were their rulers.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 106:42"/>Their enemies oppressed our ancestors
</para>
  <para style="q2">and completely controlled them.
<verse eid="PSA 106:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 106:43"/>Many times Yahweh saved his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they insisted on rebelling against him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they destroyed themselves by being more and more sinful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 106:44"/>However, Yahweh saw everything that was distressing to them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he listened to them when they cried out to him for help.
<verse eid="PSA 106:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 106:45"/>He thought about the covenant that he had made with them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because he was completely committed to faithfully loving them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he decided that he would stop {punishing them}.
<verse eid="PSA 106:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 106:46"/>He caused all those who had captured the Israelites to feel sorry for them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 106:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 106:47"/>Yahweh our God, rescue us
</para>
  <para style="q1">and bring us back to Israel from among those other people groups
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that we may thank you who are holy
</para>
  <para style="q2">and joyfully praise you!
<verse eid="PSA 106:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 106:48"/>Praise Yahweh, the God whom we Israelites worship!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise him now and forever!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Let all the people say, “We agree!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise Yahweh!”

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 106:48"/><verse eid="PSA 106:48"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 106"/>
  <chapter number="107" style="c" sid="PSA 107"/>
  <para style="ms1">Book Five

</para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 107:1"/>Thank Yahweh because he is good
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because he faithfully loves us forever!
<verse eid="PSA 107:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 107:2"/>Those whom Yahweh has saved should tell others
</para>
  <para style="q2">that he has rescued them from their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 107:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 107:3"/>He has gathered them together from {many foreign} lands;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has gathered them from the east and the west,
</para>
  <para style="q2">from the north and from the {southern} sea.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 107:4"/>Some of those who returned from those countries wandered in the trackless desert;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they could find no town to live in.
<verse eid="PSA 107:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 107:5"/>They were hungry and thirsty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they became weak and discouraged.
<verse eid="PSA 107:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 107:6"/>Then because they were distressed, they called out to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rescued them from what was distressing them.
<verse eid="PSA 107:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 107:7"/>He led them along a straight road where they walked {safely}
</para>
  <para style="q2">to cities where they could live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 107:8"/>They should praise Yahweh for how he has loved them faithfully
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the wonderful things that he does for all people!
<verse eid="PSA 107:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 107:9"/>They should thank him because he satisfies people who are thirsty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he gives hungry people plenty of good food to eat.
<verse eid="PSA 107:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 107:10"/>Some of them sat in deep darkness;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they were prisoners, suffering in iron {chains fastened to their hands and feet}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 107:11"/>They were suffering in prison because they had rebelled against God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they actually rejected the instructions that the Most High God gave to them.

<verse eid="PSA 107:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 107:12"/>God made them experience difficult things so that they would no longer be proud.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When bad things happened to them, there was no one who would help them.
<verse eid="PSA 107:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 107:13"/>Then because they were so distressed, they called out to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rescued them from what was distressing them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 107:14"/>He broke the chains that were on their hands and feet
</para>
  <para style="q2">and brought them out of those very dark prisons.
<verse eid="PSA 107:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15-16" style="v" sid="PSA 107:15-16"/>Yahweh broke down the bronze gates
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he cut through the iron bars of their prison.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Therefore they should praise Yahweh for how he has loved them faithfully
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the wonderful things that he does for all people!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:15-16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 107:17"/>Some of them foolishly rebelled {against God},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they suffered because of their sins.
<verse eid="PSA 107:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 107:18"/>They did not want to eat any food,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they almost died.
<verse eid="PSA 107:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 107:19"/>Then because they were so distressed, they called out to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rescued them from what was distressing them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 107:20"/>Then Yahweh healed them by speaking a message of healing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">in this way he saved them from dying.
<verse eid="PSA 107:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 107:21"/>They should praise Yahweh for how he has loved them faithfully
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the wonderful things that he does for all people!
<verse eid="PSA 107:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 107:22"/>They should give offerings to him to show that they are thankful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they should tell about the miracles that he has performed by singing joyfully!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 107:23"/>Some of them sailed in ships;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they bought and sold things far away across the sea.
<verse eid="PSA 107:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 107:24"/>These people saw the creatures that Yahweh created;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they saw the amazing things that he had made {as they traveled} across the very deep seas.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 107:25"/>Then he commanded the winds to become strong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They became a storm and stirred up very high waves.
<verse eid="PSA 107:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 107:26"/>The ships in which they were sailing went up on the high waves,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then they went down into the troughs between the waves.
</para>
  <para style="q2">This dangerous action terrified the sailors.
<verse eid="PSA 107:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 107:27"/>They stumbled about and staggered as drunken men do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and everything that they tried to do was useless.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 107:28"/>Then because they were distressed, they called out to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rescued them from what was distressing them.
<verse eid="PSA 107:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 107:29"/>He calmed the storm
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he stilled the waves.
<verse eid="PSA 107:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 107:30"/>Then they were very glad that the storm had become calm
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh brought them {safely} into the harbor where they had wanted to go.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 107:31"/>They should praise Yahweh for how he has loved them faithfully
</para>
  <para style="q2">and for the wonderful things that he does for all people!
<verse eid="PSA 107:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 107:32"/>They should praise him among the Israelite people when they have gathered together,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they should praise him in front of the leaders of the community.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:32"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 107:33"/>Yahweh causes rivers to become dry
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that the land becomes barren,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he makes springs of water to become dusty ground.
<verse eid="PSA 107:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 107:34"/>Yahweh causes land that normally produces a lot of crops to become salty wastelands.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He does that because the people who live there are very wicked.
<verse eid="PSA 107:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 107:35"/>But Yahweh also creates pools of water in deserts,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is, he causes springs to flow where the ground had been dry.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 107:36"/>Then he brings people who are hungry into that land,
</para>
  <para style="q2">to live there and to build cities there.
<verse eid="PSA 107:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 107:37"/>Then they sow {some of} the fields with seeds
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {in other fields} they plant grapevines
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it all produces {a large amount of} crops.
<verse eid="PSA 107:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 107:38"/>He blesses those people so that they have very many children,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so that their herds of cattle become very large.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 107:39"/>Then the people become fewer because the leaders oppress them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cause them to become distressed and to suffer.
<verse eid="PSA 107:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 107:40"/>Then Yahweh shows that he despises the leaders {who oppress them},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and makes those leaders wander in a wilderness where there are no roads.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 107:40"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 107:41"/>But he rescues poor people from those who oppress them
</para>
  <para style="q2">and causes {their} families to increase in number as flocks of sheep do.
<verse eid="PSA 107:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 107:42"/>People who live rightly see {Yahweh do these things}, and they rejoice;
</para>
  <para style="q2">wicked people {know about these things, too,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but they} have nothing to say in reply.
<verse eid="PSA 107:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 107:43"/>Those who are wise should think carefully about these things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they should thoughtfully consider all the things that Yahweh has done to show that he faithfully loves them.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 107:43"/><verse eid="PSA 107:43"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 107"/>
  <chapter number="108" style="c" sid="PSA 108"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">David wrote this psalm. It is a song.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 108:1"/>God, I am completely committed to {worshiping} you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will sing and I will play music {to praise you}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will do this with my whole being!
<verse eid="PSA 108:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 108:2"/>I will arise before the sun rises,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will praise you while I play my lyre and my harp.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 108:3"/>Yahweh, I will thank you as foreign people listen;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, I will play music to praise you before other people groups.
<verse eid="PSA 108:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 108:4"/>I will do that because the way that you faithfully love us is so great that it is like the distance between the heavens and the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the way that you faithfully keep your promises is so great that it is like the distance between the earth and the clouds.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 108:5"/>God, show {all creatures} that you are greater than anything in the heavens!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Show how wonderful you are {to people} all over the earth!
<verse eid="PSA 108:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 108:6"/>Please answer our prayers and rescue us from our enemies by your power
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that we, the people whom you love, may be safe.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 108:7"/>Because God is holy, he answered, “I will joyfully divide the area of Shechem {for you}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will distribute {among my people} the land in the Valley of Succoth.
<verse eid="PSA 108:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 108:8"/>{The region of} Gilead is mine;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{the area of the tribe of} Manasseh is mine;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{the tribe of} Ephraim is {like} my war helmet;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {the tribe of} Judah is {like} my royal scepter.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 108:9"/>The people of Moab serve me as those who wash my feet;
</para>
  <para style="q2">the people of Edom also belong to me as menial servants;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have defeated the people of Philistia.”
<verse eid="PSA 108:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 108:10"/>I wait for God to lead us to {fight against the people of} Edom;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I wait for God to lead my army to {attack} their {capital} city that has strong walls around it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 108:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 108:11"/>God, we hope that you have not abandoned us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{we are distressed that} you have not been going with us when our army marches out {to fight our enemies}.
<verse eid="PSA 108:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 108:12"/>Please help us when we fight against our enemies
</para>
  <para style="q2">because the help that humans can give {to us} is worthless.
<verse eid="PSA 108:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 108:13"/>{But} with you {helping us}, we will win;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are the one who will {enable us to} defeat our enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 108:13"/><verse eid="PSA 108:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 108"/>
  <chapter number="109" style="c" sid="PSA 109"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 109:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A note to the worship leader: David wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">God, you are the one whom I praise,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please answer my prayer
<verse eid="PSA 109:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 109:2"/>because evil and dishonest people slander me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and tell lies about me.
<verse eid="PSA 109:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 109:3"/>On all sides of me they say things that show that they hate me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they harm me for no reason.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 109:4"/>I show them that I love them
</para>
  <para style="q2">but instead of being kind to me, they say that I have done evil things.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So I pray to God {about it}.
<verse eid="PSA 109:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 109:5"/>I do good things for them and they respond by doing evil things to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I love them and they respond by hating me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 109:6"/>So appoint a wicked judge who will judge my enemy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and bring one {of his enemies} who will stand next to him and accuse him {of doing evil things}.
<verse eid="PSA 109:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 109:7"/>Let that judge declare that my enemy is guilty,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may you judge that even his prayer {to you} is a sin.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 109:8"/>Then cause him to die soon;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let people honor someone else rather than him.
<verse eid="PSA 109:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 109:9"/>Cause his children not to have a father anymore,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cause his wife to become a widow.
<verse eid="PSA 109:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 109:10"/>Cause his children to wander far from their ruined homes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">begging and looking for food.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 109:11"/>Let the people to whom he owed money seize all of his property;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let strangers take away everything that he worked to acquire.
<verse eid="PSA 109:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 109:12"/>Make sure that no one is faithfully loving to him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">make sure that no one pities his fatherless children.
<verse eid="PSA 109:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 109:13"/>Cause all his children to die,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that there will not be another generation to continue his name.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 109:14"/>Yahweh, consider all of the evil things that his ancestors did
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not forgive the sins that his mother committed.
<verse eid="PSA 109:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 109:15"/>Please think about their sins always,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but cause everyone on earth to completely forget who they were.
<verse eid="PSA 109:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 109:16"/>I pray these things because that man{, my enemy,} was never faithful toward anyone as your covenant says we must be;
</para>
  <para style="q2">instead, he persecuted poor, needy, and grieving people
</para>
  <para style="q2">until they were dead.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 109:17"/>He enjoyed cursing {other people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so now people are cursing him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He did not want to bless {other people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">so there will be no one who blesses him.
<verse eid="PSA 109:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 109:18"/>Cursing {other people} is as natural for him as wearing clothes.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Cursing {other people} is so much a part of who he is that it is like the water that he drinks;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is so much a part of who he is that it is like olive oil that has soaked into his bones.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 109:19"/>Cause those terrible curses to continually afflict him like clothes that cling to him
</para>
  <para style="q2">and like the belt that he wears every day.
<verse eid="PSA 109:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 109:20"/>Yahweh, let this {curse} be the way that you punish all of those who accuse me {of doing bad things}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all of those who say evil things about me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 109:21"/>But you, Yahweh, my God, please be kind to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of who you are!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me {from my enemies}
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you faithfully love me as you promised.
<verse eid="PSA 109:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 109:22"/>I ask you to do this because I am destitute
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am intensely sorrowful.
<verse eid="PSA 109:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 109:23"/>I think that my time to remain alive will end
</para>
  <para style="q2">as quickly as an evening shadow disappears.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will be gone as quickly as a man shakes off a locust.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 109:24"/>My knees are weak because I have fasted very often,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and my body has become very thin; any fat is gone.
<verse eid="PSA 109:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 109:25"/>The people who accuse me despise me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they see me, they insult me by shaking their heads at me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 109:26"/>Yahweh, the God whom I worship, please help me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Rescue me because you faithfully love me!
<verse eid="PSA 109:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 109:27"/>Then my enemies will know
</para>
  <para style="q2">that you, Yahweh, are the one who has done it!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 109:28"/>As for them, they will curse {me}, but you, in contrast, will bless {me}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When they persecute {me}, {the result will be that} you make them ashamed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but you cause {me,} your servant, to be glad!
<verse eid="PSA 109:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 109:29"/>Please let everyone see that those who accuse me are completely disgraceful!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, cause other people to see that they are shameful as easily as someone sees the clothes that they wear!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 109:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 109:30"/>I will thank Yahweh very much out loud;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise him when I am among the crowd of people who are worshiping him.
<verse eid="PSA 109:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 109:31"/>I will do that because he defends poor people {like me}
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to save {us} from those who would condemn us to die.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 109:31"/><verse eid="PSA 109:31"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 109"/>
  <chapter number="110" style="c" sid="PSA 110"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 110:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">David wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh said to my lord,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Sit {here,} close to me, in the place of highest honor
</para>
  <para style="q2">until I completely defeat your enemies
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make them {like} a stool for your feet!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 110:2"/>Yahweh will extend your powerful kingdom
</para>
  <para style="q2">from Zion {to other lands};
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are to rule over all your enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 110:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 110:3"/>When you lead your army into battle,
</para>
  <para style="q2">your people will offer themselves freely {to join your army}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The way that they are completely devoted to you will be beautiful.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You will be as strong as you were as a young man every day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as surely as the dew comes that waters the earth every morning.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 110:4"/>Yahweh has made a solemn promise
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will never change his mind {about it};
</para>
  <para style="q1">{he said to the king,} “You are an eternal priest
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the way that Melchizedek was a priest.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 110:5"/>The Lord fights for you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when he becomes angry, he defeats many kings.
<verse eid="PSA 110:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 110:6"/>He will punish the people of many nations;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will cause many {enemy soldiers} to fall dead, with crushed heads,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all over a broad land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 110:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 110:7"/>But the king will drink from the stream alongside the road;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of {all} this, he will be victorious.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 110:7"/><verse eid="PSA 110:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 110"/>
  <chapter number="111" style="c" sid="PSA 111"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 111:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">I will thank Yahweh with my entire inner being
</para>
  <para style="q2">every time that those who do what is right meet together.
<verse eid="PSA 111:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 111:2"/>The things that Yahweh does are wonderful!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All those who delight in those things study them carefully.
<verse eid="PSA 111:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 111:3"/>The things that he does show how wonderful and glorious he is,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that he is eternally righteous.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 111:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 111:4"/>He has done wonderful things that people will always remember;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh always acts kindly and mercifully.
<verse eid="PSA 111:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 111:5"/>He provides food for those who profoundly respect him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he never forgets the covenant that he made {with our ancestors}.
<verse eid="PSA 111:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 111:6"/>By enabling his people to capture the lands that had belonged to other people groups,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he showed to {us,} his people, that he is very powerful.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 111:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 111:7"/>He does everything fairly and in the right way,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we can trust that everything that he tells us to do is for our good.
<verse eid="PSA 111:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 111:8"/>We must obey his instructions forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he created them in order to do what is best for us, and they are completely right.
<verse eid="PSA 111:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 111:9"/>He rescued us, his people, {from being slaves in Egypt,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he made a covenant {with us} that will last forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is holy and awesome!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 111:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 111:10"/>Having a profound respect for Yahweh is the way to become wise.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All those who obey his instructions will come to understand why it is good to do them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">We should praise him forever!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 111:10"/><verse eid="PSA 111:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 111"/>
  <chapter number="112" style="c" sid="PSA 112"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 112:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">How fortunate are those who have a profound respect for Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">How fortunate are those who happily obey his commands!
<verse eid="PSA 112:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 112:2"/>Their descendants will prosper in their land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh will bless all who do what is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 112:3"/>Their families will be wealthy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and their righteous deeds will endure forever.
<verse eid="PSA 112:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 112:4"/>For those who honor God, it is as if a light were shining on them in the darkness,
</para>
  <para style="q2">on those who are kind, merciful, and righteous.
<verse eid="PSA 112:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 112:5"/>It is good to be kind to others and to generously lend money to them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">A person like that does everything honestly.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 112:6"/>Righteous people do this because they know that bad things will never overwhelm them;
</para>
  <para style="q2">other people will always {joyfully} remember them.
<verse eid="PSA 112:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 112:7"/>Righteous people are not afraid when they receive bad news;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they confidently trust in Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 112:8"/>They are confident and not afraid
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they know that they will see God defeat their enemies.
<verse eid="PSA 112:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 112:9"/>They give things generously to poor people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">their kind deeds will endure forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people will greatly honor them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 112:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 112:10"/>Wicked people will see {those things} and become angry;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will gnash their teeth {angrily},
</para>
  <para style="q2">then people will stop hearing from them and they will die.
</para>
  <para style="q2">The wicked things that they want to do will never happen.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 112:10"/><verse eid="PSA 112:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 112"/>
  <chapter number="113" style="c" sid="PSA 113"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 113:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You people who serve Yahweh, praise him!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh for who he is!
<verse eid="PSA 113:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 113:2"/>Everyone should praise Yahweh for who he is, both now and forevermore!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 113:3"/>From the people who live in the far east to the people who live in the far west,
</para>
  <para style="q2">everyone should praise Yahweh for who he is!
<verse eid="PSA 113:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 113:4"/>Yahweh rules over all the nations,
</para>
  <para style="q1">he is more glorious than anything under the heavens.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 113:5"/>There is no one who is like Yahweh, the God whom we worship,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who sits on his throne in the highest heaven
<verse eid="PSA 113:5"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 113:6"/>and who stoops down to look at the sky and at the earth.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 113:7"/>He rescues very poor people from the very poor way that they live
<verse eid="PSA 113:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 113:8"/>and causes people to honor them by making them
</para>
  <para style="q2">leaders among those who rule his people.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 113:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 113:9"/>He also enables women who have had no children to live in their houses
</para>
  <para style="q2">as happy mothers with children.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 113:9"/><verse eid="PSA 113:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 113"/>
  <chapter number="114" style="c" sid="PSA 114"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 114:1"/>When the Israelite people left Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, when the descendants of Jacob left those people who spoke a foreign language,
<verse eid="PSA 114:1"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 114:2"/>the land of Judah became the place where people worshiped God;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the land of Israel became the area that he ruled over.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 114:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 114:3"/>{When they came to} the Sea {of Reeds},
</para>
  <para style="q2">{it was as though the water} saw {them} and ran away!
</para>
  <para style="q2">{When they came to} the Jordan River,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{the water in the river} stopped flowing {so that the Israelites could cross it}.
<verse eid="PSA 114:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 114:4"/>{When Mount Sinai shook,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">{it was as though} the mountains skipped like rams
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the hills jumped like lambs.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 114:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 114:5"/>{If someone asks,} “What happened at the Sea {of Reeds} that made it seem to run away?
</para>
  <para style="q2">What happened that caused {the water in} the Jordan {River} to stop flowing?
<verse eid="PSA 114:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 114:6"/>{What happened at Mount Sinai that made the} mountains {seem to} skip like rams
</para>
  <para style="q2">and made the hills {seem to} jump like lambs?”
<verse eid="PSA 114:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 114:7"/>{I would reply,} “The earth trembles because the Lord is there!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone should tremble because of the presence of the God whom Jacob worshiped!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 114:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 114:8"/>He is the one who caused pools of water to flow from a rock {for the Israelite people to drink};
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed, he caused a spring to flow from a solid rock!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 114:8"/><verse eid="PSA 114:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 114"/>
  <chapter number="115" style="c" sid="PSA 115"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">A psalm written by David
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 115:1"/>Yahweh, {we ask} not so people will honor us, no, not that at all;
</para>
  <para style="q2">rather, we want people to honor you alone
</para>
  <para style="q2">because of seeing how you faithfully love us and by seeing you do what you have promised to do.
<verse eid="PSA 115:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 115:2"/>It is not right that other people groups should say {about us},
</para>
  <para style="q1">“We do not see their God doing anything {to help them}.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 115:3"/>Well, the God whom we worship lives in heaven;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does whatever he wants!
<verse eid="PSA 115:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 115:4"/>But the idols of those people groups are only silver and gold {statues};
</para>
  <para style="q2">humans made them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 115:5"/>Their idols have mouths, but they cannot say anything;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have eyes, but they cannot see anything.
<verse eid="PSA 115:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 115:6"/>They have ears, but they cannot hear anything;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have noses, but they cannot smell anything.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 115:7"/>They have hands, but they cannot feel anything;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have feet, but they cannot walk;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they cannot even make any sounds in their throats!
<verse eid="PSA 115:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 115:8"/>The people who make those idols are {as powerless} as those idols,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Everyone who trusts in those idols {to do anything} is also {powerless}!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 115:9"/>You, my fellow Israelite people, trust in Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who helps you and protects you like a shield.
<verse eid="PSA 115:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 115:10"/>You {priests, the} descendants of Aaron, trust in Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who helps you and protects you like a shield.
<verse eid="PSA 115:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 115:11"/>All you who deeply respect Yahweh, trust in Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who helps you and protects you like a shield.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 115:12"/>Yahweh has not forgotten us; he will bless {us}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">he will bless us Israelite people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will bless the priests!
<verse eid="PSA 115:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 115:13"/>Yahweh will bless all those who deeply respect him—
</para>
  <para style="q2">those who are less important as well as the important people, that is, each one!
<verse eid="PSA 115:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 115:14"/>I pray that Yahweh may give {many children}
</para>
  <para style="q2">{both} to you, {my fellow Israelite people,} and to your children {after you}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 115:15"/>I pray that Yahweh, the one who made heaven and the earth, may bless all of you!
<verse eid="PSA 115:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 115:16"/>The highest heavens belong to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he gave everything that is on the earth to humankind.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 115:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 115:17"/>People who are dead are not able to praise Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they go to the place where dead people are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">they become silent and cannot praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 115:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 115:18"/>But we who are alive will praise Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">both now and forevermore.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 115:18"/><verse eid="PSA 115:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 115"/>
  <chapter number="116" style="c" sid="PSA 116"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 116:1"/>I love Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he hears me when I cry out for him to help me.
<verse eid="PSA 116:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 116:2"/>I love him because he listens to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will call out to him all during my life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 116:3"/>Everything around me caused me to think that I was about to die;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it seemed to me that I was already dying.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I was distressed and very sad.
<verse eid="PSA 116:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 116:4"/>But then I called out to Yahweh.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I said, “Yahweh, I plead with you to save me!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 116:5"/>Yahweh is kind and does what is right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the God whom we worship, and he loves us.
<verse eid="PSA 116:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 116:6"/>Yahweh protects those who are helpless;
</para>
  <para style="q2">when I was experiencing bad things, he saved me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 116:7"/>I encourage myself to relax once again
</para>
  <para style="q2">because Yahweh has restored me.
<verse eid="PSA 116:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 116:8"/>Indeed, Yahweh has saved me from dying,
</para>
  <para style="q2">he has delivered me from being sorrowful,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and he has kept me from making bad mistakes.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 116:9"/>So while I am still alive,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will live as Yahweh directs me.
<verse eid="PSA 116:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 116:10"/>I continued to trust {in Yahweh},
</para>
  <para style="q2">even when I said, “As for me, I am greatly suffering.”
<verse eid="PSA 116:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 116:11"/>For my part, I was so distressed that I thought,
</para>
  <para style="q1">“I cannot trust anyone.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 116:12"/>I can never repay Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">for all the good things that he has done for me.
<verse eid="PSA 116:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 116:13"/>{But I can do this:} I will present a cup {of wine as a thank offering}
</para>
  <para style="q2">as I call out to thank him for saving me.
<verse eid="PSA 116:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 116:14"/>Also, as the people who belong to Yahweh watch,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will give to him the offerings that I solemnly promised to give to him.
<verse eid="PSA 116:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 116:15"/>Yahweh is very grieved when one of his people dies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 116:16"/>Certainly I am one of Yahweh’s people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am his servant; I have belonged to him since my mother bore me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">So he saved me from what was going to kill me.
<verse eid="PSA 116:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 116:17"/>So I will offer to him a sacrifice to thank him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will pray to Yahweh.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 116:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18-19" style="v" sid="PSA 116:18-19"/>As the people who belong to Yahweh watch,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the courtyard outside his temple,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the middle of Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will give to him the offerings that I solemnly promised to give to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 116:18-19"/><verse eid="PSA 116:18-19"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 116"/>
  <chapter number="117" style="c" sid="PSA 117"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 117:1"/>You people of all nations, praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">All you people groups, greatly praise him!
<verse eid="PSA 117:1"/></para>
  <para style="q2"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 117:2"/>Do this, because he is fully committed to love us faithfully, just as he promised to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we can trust that Yahweh will be faithful forever.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 117:2"/><verse eid="PSA 117:2"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 117"/>
  <chapter number="118" style="c" sid="PSA 118"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 118:1"/>Thank Yahweh because he is good
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because he faithfully loves us forever!
<verse eid="PSA 118:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 118:2"/>All Israelite people should repeatedly shout,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“because he faithfully loves us forever!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 118:3"/>You {priests} who are descendants of Aaron should repeatedly shout,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“because he faithfully loves us forever!”
<verse eid="PSA 118:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 118:4"/>All you who deeply revere Yahweh should repeatedly shout,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“because he faithfully loves us forever!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 118:5"/>When I was distressed, I called out to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Yahweh answered me and set me free.
<verse eid="PSA 118:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 118:6"/>Yahweh is on my side,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I will not be afraid of anything.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that humans cannot really harm me!
<verse eid="PSA 118:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 118:7"/>Yes, Yahweh is on my side. He helps me defeat my enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I know that I will look {triumphantly} on them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 118:8"/>It is better to rely on Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to depend on people.
<verse eid="PSA 118:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 118:9"/>It is better to rely on Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">than to trust that influential people will protect us.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 118:10"/>Armies of many nations surrounded me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh powerfully enabled me to make them retreat.
<verse eid="PSA 118:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 118:11"/>They completely surrounded me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh powerfully enabled me to make them retreat.
<verse eid="PSA 118:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 118:12"/>They swarmed around me like {angry} bees,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they diminished as quickly as a fire that is burning only thorns;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh powerfully enabled me to make them retreat.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 118:13"/>My enemies attacked me fiercely and thought that they would defeat me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but Yahweh helped me.
<verse eid="PSA 118:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 118:14"/>Yahweh is the one who makes me strong,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and who gives me a reason to sing;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he saves me from my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 118:15"/>Listen to the joyful songs of how Yahweh saves people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They come from the tents of the people who honor God!
</para>
  <para style="q2">They sing, “Yahweh has powerfully defeated our enemies;
<verse eid="PSA 118:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 118:16"/>Yahweh has shown himself to be victorious!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh has powerfully defeated our enemies!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 118:17"/>My enemies will not kill me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no, I will live to proclaim the great things that Yahweh has done.
<verse eid="PSA 118:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 118:18"/>Yahweh has punished me severely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he has not allowed me to die.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 118:19"/>{You gatekeepers,} open for me the gates through which those who obey Yahweh may enter,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may enter through them and thank Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 118:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 118:20"/>{The gatekeeper says,} “This is Yahweh’s gate;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all who obey him may enter through it.”
<verse eid="PSA 118:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 118:21"/>{Yahweh,} I thank you that you answered my prayer
</para>
  <para style="q2">and saved me {from my enemies}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 118:22"/>{People considered me worthless, like} a stone that builders rejected,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{but then Yahweh showed that he highly values me,
</para>
  <para style="q1">as if} that stone then became the most important stone in the building.
<verse eid="PSA 118:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 118:23"/>The people said, “Yahweh made that happen,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and for us, it is a wonderful thing.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 118:24"/>Yahweh made possible everything that we are celebrating today;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we should be extremely happy about all of it!
<verse eid="PSA 118:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 118:25"/>Yahweh, we plead with you to keep rescuing us {from our enemies}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, please continue to help us to succeed {against our enemies}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 118:26"/>Yahweh, bless the one who will come with your power.
</para>
  <para style="q2">From the temple we bless all of you.
<verse eid="PSA 118:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 118:27"/>Yahweh is God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he has made us victorious.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Bring an animal sacrifice {for him} and tie it to the horns of the altar.”
<verse eid="PSA 118:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 118:28"/>Yahweh, you are the God whom I worship, and I will praise you!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You are the only God whom I worship, and I will tell everyone that you are great!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 118:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 118:29"/>Thank Yahweh because he is good
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because he faithfully loves us forever!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 118:29"/><verse eid="PSA 118:29"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 118"/>
  <chapter number="119" style="c" sid="PSA 119"/>
  <para style="qa">ALEPH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 119:1"/>How fortunate are those about whom no one can say truthfully that they have done things that are wrong!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those are the people who always obey Yahweh’s instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 119:2"/>How fortunate are those who do what he tells them to do!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Those are the people who sincerely want to know him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 119:3"/>They certainly do not want to cheat other people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they live in a way that pleases Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 119:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 119:4"/>Yahweh, you have given us your instructions
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that we would carefully obey them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 119:5"/>I want very much to continually obey everything that you command!
<verse eid="PSA 119:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 119:6"/>If I did that, then I would not be ashamed
</para>
  <para style="q2">when I think about everything that you command.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 119:7"/>As I learn all of your just regulations,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I thank you sincerely.
<verse eid="PSA 119:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 119:8"/>I will obey your regulations;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not desert me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:8"/></para>
  <para style="qa">BETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 119:9"/>I know how a young person can live in the right way;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is by obeying your commands.
<verse eid="PSA 119:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 119:10"/>I eagerly want to please you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not allow me to disobey what you have commanded.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 119:11"/>I have memorized your commands
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to not sin against you.
<verse eid="PSA 119:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 119:12"/>Yahweh, I praise you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">teach me your rules.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 119:13"/>I have proclaimed to the people all of the things that you have commanded us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 119:14"/>I delight in obeying your instructions;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I enjoy that more than being very rich.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 119:15"/>I will carefully think about everything that you have commanded me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, I will pay attention to the way of living that you have taught me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 119:16"/>I am happy to obey your decrees;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not forget what you have said.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:16"/></para>
  <para style="qa">GIMEL
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 119:17"/>Do good things for me, the one who serves you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I may continue to live and obey you.
<verse eid="PSA 119:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 119:18"/>Help me to understand
</para>
  <para style="q2">how wonderful your instructions are.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 119:19"/>I am living here on the earth for only a short time;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please let me know your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 119:20"/>I am weak from constantly desiring to know your instructions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 119:21"/>You rebuke people who are proud;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you curse people who disobey your commands.
<verse eid="PSA 119:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 119:22"/>Do not allow them to continue to insult and scorn me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{I request this} because I have obeyed what you have required.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 119:23"/>Rulers gather together and plan ways to harm me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I, your servant, will meditate on what you have commanded me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 119:24"/>Yes, I am delighted with your requirements;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are like {good} advisors for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:24"/></para>
  <para style="qa">DALETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 119:25"/>{Sometimes} I feel like I will soon die;
</para>
  <para style="q2">allow me to live as you have told me that you would do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 119:26"/>When I told you about what was happening with me, you responded to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">teach me the things that you want me to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:26"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="27" style="v" sid="PSA 119:27"/>Help me to understand how you want me to behave,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then I can think about how amazing your instructions are.
<verse eid="PSA 119:27"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="28" style="v" sid="PSA 119:28"/>I am very sad, with the result that I am becoming weak;
</para>
  <para style="q2">enable me to be strong again through a message from you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:28"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="29" style="v" sid="PSA 119:29"/>Prevent me from telling lies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and be kind to me by teaching me your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:29"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="30" style="v" sid="PSA 119:30"/>I have decided that I will faithfully obey you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that what you say is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:30"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="31" style="v" sid="PSA 119:31"/>Yahweh, I try to carefully obey what you say;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please do not allow me to do anything shameful.
<verse eid="PSA 119:31"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="32" style="v" sid="PSA 119:32"/>I eagerly obey your instructions
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you help me increasingly to understand {how they benefit me}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:32"/></para>
  <para style="qa">HE
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="33" style="v" sid="PSA 119:33"/>Yahweh, teach me what your regulations mean,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and then I will always obey them.
<verse eid="PSA 119:33"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="34" style="v" sid="PSA 119:34"/>Help me to understand your instructions
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may eagerly obey them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:34"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="35" style="v" sid="PSA 119:35"/>I am happy to do the things that you command,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so teach me the best way to obey them.
<verse eid="PSA 119:35"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="36" style="v" sid="PSA 119:36"/>Cause me to want to do what you say
</para>
  <para style="q2">rather than to want to get things {that belong to other people}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:36"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="37" style="v" sid="PSA 119:37"/>Do not allow me to desire things that are not good for me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">make me able to live as you want me to live.
<verse eid="PSA 119:37"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="38" style="v" sid="PSA 119:38"/>Please do what you promised to do for me, your servant.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Your promises are what cause people to deeply revere you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:38"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="39" style="v" sid="PSA 119:39"/>I become afraid when my enemies insult me {for obeying you};
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please stop them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because it is good to do what you tell us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:39"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="40" style="v" sid="PSA 119:40"/>Indeed, I very much desire to obey what you have declared that we should do!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you are righteous, please make me joyful again in living {for you}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:40"/></para>
  <para style="qa">WAW
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="41" style="v" sid="PSA 119:41"/>Then I will know that you faithfully love me, Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that you will save me as you promised that you would do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:41"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="42" style="v" sid="PSA 119:42"/>After you do that, I will be able to reply to those who insult me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I trust what you have said.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:42"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="43" style="v" sid="PSA 119:43"/>Please do allow me to truthfully tell {them how you saved me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">you see, I am patiently waiting for you to act justly.
<verse eid="PSA 119:43"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="44" style="v" sid="PSA 119:44"/>I will consistently obey your instructions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">for as long as I live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:44"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="45" style="v" sid="PSA 119:45"/>I will live freely and safely
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I {always} try to obey your regulations.
<verse eid="PSA 119:45"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="46" style="v" sid="PSA 119:46"/>I will tell kings the things that you have said;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will not be ashamed {to do so}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:46"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="47" style="v" sid="PSA 119:47"/>I am very happy to obey the things that you command me to do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I love to do them.
<verse eid="PSA 119:47"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="48" style="v" sid="PSA 119:48"/>I eagerly ask to receive more of your commandments.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I love them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will think deeply about everything that you require us to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:48"/></para>
  <para style="qa">ZAYIN
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="49" style="v" sid="PSA 119:49"/>Please do what you said you would do for me, the one who serves you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because what you have said has caused me to confidently expect good things from you.
<verse eid="PSA 119:49"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="50" style="v" sid="PSA 119:50"/>When I am suffering, your promise to me comforts me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">knowing that you will do what you have said makes me joyful again in living {for you}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:50"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="51" style="v" sid="PSA 119:51"/>Proud people are always making fun of me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I do not stop obeying your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:51"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="52" style="v" sid="PSA 119:52"/>Yahweh, I think about your regulations that you gave to us long ago.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Doing that comforts me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:52"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="53" style="v" sid="PSA 119:53"/>When I see wicked people disregard your instructions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I become very angry.
<verse eid="PSA 119:53"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="54" style="v" sid="PSA 119:54"/>During this short time that I am living here on the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the regulations that you have given to us are like music to me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:54"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="55" style="v" sid="PSA 119:55"/>Yahweh, {even} during the night I think about you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I {always} obey your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:55"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="56" style="v" sid="PSA 119:56"/>This is what I do;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I obey your regulations.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:56"/></para>
  <para style="qa">HETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="57" style="v" sid="PSA 119:57"/>Yahweh, you have granted to me that I would belong to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I promise to obey what you tell me to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:57"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="58" style="v" sid="PSA 119:58"/>I earnestly plead with you {to be good to me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">act kindly to me as you promised that you would do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:58"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="59" style="v" sid="PSA 119:59"/>I think about my behavior,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {when it is wrong,} I once again obey what you tell me to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:59"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="60" style="v" sid="PSA 119:60"/>{When I understand} your instructions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I do them immediately.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:60"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="61" style="v" sid="PSA 119:61"/>Wicked people try to make me do bad things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I continue to obey your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:61"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="62" style="v" sid="PSA 119:62"/>In the middle of the night I get up,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to praise you
</para>
  <para style="q2">because everything that you say is completely right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:62"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="63" style="v" sid="PSA 119:63"/>I am a friend of all those who deeply revere you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, to all those who obey what you tell us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:63"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="64" style="v" sid="PSA 119:64"/>Yahweh, you faithfully love people all over the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please {continue to} teach me how you want people to live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:64"/></para>
  <para style="qa">TETH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="65" style="v" sid="PSA 119:65"/>Yahweh, you have done good things for me, your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as you promised that you would do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:65"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="66" style="v" sid="PSA 119:66"/>Teach me to understand {what is happening around me} and to think carefully {before I decide what to do},
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I believe that the best way to live is to obey what you tell us to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:66"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="67" style="v" sid="PSA 119:67"/>Before you afflicted me, I did things that were wrong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but now I obey what you say to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:67"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="68" style="v" sid="PSA 119:68"/>You are good, and what you do is good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">teach me the {good} things that you have told us to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:68"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="69" style="v" sid="PSA 119:69"/>Proud people tell many lies about me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but as for me, I enthusiastically obey what you have told us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:69"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="70" style="v" sid="PSA 119:70"/>Those people are stupid,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but as for me, I happily obey your instructions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:70"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="71" style="v" sid="PSA 119:71"/>It was good for me that you afflicted me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because the result was that I learned {how good} your regulations {are}.
<verse eid="PSA 119:71"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="72" style="v" sid="PSA 119:72"/>The instructions that you give {to us} are beneficial to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They are more beneficial than thousands of pieces of gold and silver.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:72"/></para>
  <para style="qa">YODH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="73" style="v" sid="PSA 119:73"/>You created me and made me who I am;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please help me to be wise so that I may learn {to obey} what you tell me to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:73"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="74" style="v" sid="PSA 119:74"/>I want everyone who deeply reveres you to see {what you have done for} me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Then they will be glad, because they will see {how good it is} that I have trusted you to do what you said.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:74"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="75" style="v" sid="PSA 119:75"/>Yahweh, I know that when you judge people, you are always right.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that you have made me suffer only because you faithfully love me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:75"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="76" style="v" sid="PSA 119:76"/>Please comfort me by showing that you faithfully love me
</para>
  <para style="q2">as you said to me, your servant, that you would do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:76"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="77" style="v" sid="PSA 119:77"/>I want you to act mercifully to me in order that I may continue to live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am delighted with your instruction.
<verse eid="PSA 119:77"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="78" style="v" sid="PSA 119:78"/>Cause the proud people who falsely accuse me to be ashamed;
</para>
  <para style="q2">but as for me, I will continue meditating on what you have commanded that I should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:78"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="79" style="v" sid="PSA 119:79"/>Cause those who deeply revere you to come to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that they may learn what you say to us.
<verse eid="PSA 119:79"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="80" style="v" sid="PSA 119:80"/>Enable me to want to perfectly obey your regulations
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I may not be ashamed {because of not doing that}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:80"/></para>
  <para style="qa">KAPH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="81" style="v" sid="PSA 119:81"/>I desperately long for you to save me {from my enemies},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I will wait, knowing that you will answer {my prayer}.
<verse eid="PSA 119:81"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="82" style="v" sid="PSA 119:82"/>My eyes are tired from watching for you to do what you promised that you would do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I ask, “When will you help me?”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:82"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="83" style="v" sid="PSA 119:83"/>Indeed, I feel as {weak and useless as} a wineskin that is {shriveled up from} hanging {a long time} in the smoke,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I have not forgotten your regulations.
<verse eid="PSA 119:83"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="84" style="v" sid="PSA 119:84"/>I, your servant, cannot wait any longer!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I want you to punish those who persecute me soon!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:84"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="85" style="v" sid="PSA 119:85"/>It is as though my proud enemies have dug deep pits for me {to fall into}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">These people disobey your instructions {to us}.

<verse eid="PSA 119:85"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="86" style="v" sid="PSA 119:86"/>Everything that you tell us to do is truly good {for us};
</para>
  <para style="q2">but people are persecuting me by telling lies {about me}, so please help me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:86"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="87" style="v" sid="PSA 119:87"/>Those people have come very close to killing me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but as for me, I have not stopped obeying what you have told us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:87"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="88" style="v" sid="PSA 119:88"/>Because you faithfully love {me}, allow me to {continue to} live
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may {continue to} obey what you have instructed {us to do}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:88"/></para>
  <para style="qa">LAMEDH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="89" style="v" sid="PSA 119:89"/>Yahweh, what you have proclaimed is eternal;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it exists forever in heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 119:89"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="90" style="v" sid="PSA 119:90"/>You will continue to act faithfully for people of every generation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have put the earth in its place, and it remains firmly {there}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:90"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="91" style="v" sid="PSA 119:91"/>To this day, all things on the earth remain because you decided that they should remain;
</para>
  <para style="q2">that is because everything on the earth serves you.
<verse eid="PSA 119:91"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="92" style="v" sid="PSA 119:92"/>If I had not been delighted to obey your instructions,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then I would have died because of what I was suffering.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:92"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="93" style="v" sid="PSA 119:93"/>I will always remember what you have declared that we should do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I obeyed those things, and as a result, you have enabled me to continue to live.
<verse eid="PSA 119:93"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="94" style="v" sid="PSA 119:94"/>I belong to you; please save me from my enemies
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I intentionally obey what you have declared that we should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:94"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="95" style="v" sid="PSA 119:95"/>Wicked men are waiting to ambush and kill me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I think about what you have instructed {us to do}.
<verse eid="PSA 119:95"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="96" style="v" sid="PSA 119:96"/>I have learned that there is a limit to {even} the best {that people can achieve},
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what you decree is limitless.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:96"/></para>
  <para style="qa">MEM
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="97" style="v" sid="PSA 119:97"/>I love your instructions very much!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I meditate on them throughout the day.
<verse eid="PSA 119:97"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="98" style="v" sid="PSA 119:98"/>Because I know what you have told us to do
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because I think about those things all the time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have become wiser than my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:98"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="99" style="v" sid="PSA 119:99"/>I understand more than any of my teachers do
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I continually think about everything that you tell {us}.
<verse eid="PSA 119:99"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="100" style="v" sid="PSA 119:100"/>I behave more intelligently than many old people do
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I obey what you have declared that we should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:100"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="101" style="v" sid="PSA 119:101"/>I have avoided all evil behavior
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I may obey what you have told us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:101"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="102" style="v" sid="PSA 119:102"/>I have not stopped obeying your regulations
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you are the one who taught {them} to me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:102"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="103" style="v" sid="PSA 119:103"/>When I read your words,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is like eating something sweet;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{yes,} it is even better than eating honey!
<verse eid="PSA 119:103"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="104" style="v" sid="PSA 119:104"/>Because I have learned what you have declared that we should do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am able to understand {many things};
</para>
  <para style="q2">therefore, I hate all evil activities.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:104"/></para>
  <para style="qa">NUN
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="105" style="v" sid="PSA 119:105"/>Your instruction is like a lamp that guides me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, it is like a light that shows me where to walk.
<verse eid="PSA 119:105"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="106" style="v" sid="PSA 119:106"/>I have solemnly promised, and I am solemnly promising it again,
</para>
  <para style="q2">that I will always obey your regulations;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they are always right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:106"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="107" style="v" sid="PSA 119:107"/>Yahweh, I am suffering very much;
</para>
  <para style="q2">cause me to be strong again as you have promised to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:107"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="108" style="v" sid="PSA 119:108"/>Yahweh, sometimes the sacrifices that I offer to you are just my prayers to thank and praise you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please accept them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me the things that you tell us to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:108"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="109" style="v" sid="PSA 119:109"/>My enemies are constantly trying to kill me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I do not forget your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:109"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="110" style="v" sid="PSA 119:110"/>Wicked people have tried to seize me {as a hunter tries to catch little animals} with a trap,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I have not disobeyed what you declared that we should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:110"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="111" style="v" sid="PSA 119:111"/>You have given me your instructions and they are mine forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Indeed, they are what make me joyful.
<verse eid="PSA 119:111"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="112" style="v" sid="PSA 119:112"/>I have determined that I will always obey your commands as long as I live, to the very end.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:112"/></para>
  <para style="qa">SAMEKH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="113" style="v" sid="PSA 119:113"/>I hate people who cannot decide what to commit to,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I love your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:113"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="114" style="v" sid="PSA 119:114"/>You are like a place where I can hide {from my enemies},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you are like a shield {behind which I am protected from them};
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will wait, knowing that you will answer {my prayer}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:114"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="115" style="v" sid="PSA 119:115"/>You people who do evil things, go away from me
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may obey what my God has commanded!
<verse eid="PSA 119:115"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="116" style="v" sid="PSA 119:116"/>Please enable me to be strong as you promised that you would do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I may {continue to} live.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I am confidently expecting {that you will restore me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">please do not disappoint me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:116"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="117" style="v" sid="PSA 119:117"/>Please take care of me so that I can be safe
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so that I can always pay attention to what you have decreed that we should do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:117"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="118" style="v" sid="PSA 119:118"/>You despise everyone who disregards what you have decreed that we should do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed, they deceive others by lying.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:118"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="119" style="v" sid="PSA 119:119"/>You get rid of all the wicked people on the earth as {people get rid of} trash;
</para>
  <para style="q2">therefore, I love what you say to us.
<verse eid="PSA 119:119"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="120" style="v" sid="PSA 119:120"/>I tremble because I am afraid of you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am afraid {because you punish those who do not obey} the rules that you have given to us.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:120"/></para>
  <para style="qa">AYIN
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="121" style="v" sid="PSA 119:121"/>But I have done what is right and fair;
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please do not allow people to oppress me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:121"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="122" style="v" sid="PSA 119:122"/>Please ensure that good things will happen for me, your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and do not allow proud people to oppress me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:122"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="123" style="v" sid="PSA 119:123"/>My eyes are tired from watching for you to save me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, from watching for you to do what is right, as you promised to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:123"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="124" style="v" sid="PSA 119:124"/>Please do {things} for me, your servant, to show that you faithfully love me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me how to do what you have decreed that we should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:124"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="125" style="v" sid="PSA 119:125"/>I am one who serves you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">please enable me to understand {what you want me to know}
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I may learn what you have instructed us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:125"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="126" style="v" sid="PSA 119:126"/>Yahweh, you should punish {people} now
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they have disobeyed your laws.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:126"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="127" style="v" sid="PSA 119:127"/>Because {I do not want to be like those people,} I love your instructions more than I love gold;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I love them more than I love very pure gold.
<verse eid="PSA 119:127"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="128" style="v" sid="PSA 119:128"/>So I am careful to obey everything that you have declared that we should do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I hate all of the evil things that people do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:128"/></para>
  <para style="qa">PE
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="129" style="v" sid="PSA 119:129"/>All the things that you have instructed us to do are wonderful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so I obey them enthusiastically.
<verse eid="PSA 119:129"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="130" style="v" sid="PSA 119:130"/>When someone explains what you have said {to us},
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is as though he is opening a door to a bright light {that allows people to see what they did not see before};
</para>
  <para style="q2">what he says causes {even} people who have not studied your instructions to be wise.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:130"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="131" style="v" sid="PSA 119:131"/>I eagerly desire to know what you have commanded {us},
</para>
  <para style="q2">as eagerly as though I were panting {for food and water}.
<verse eid="PSA 119:131"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="132" style="v" sid="PSA 119:132"/>Pay attention to me and act kindly to me
</para>
  <para style="q2">as is right {for you to do} for {all} those who love you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:132"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="133" style="v" sid="PSA 119:133"/>Please guide me by your instructions;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not allow me to desire to do sinful things more than to obey you.
<verse eid="PSA 119:133"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="134" style="v" sid="PSA 119:134"/>Rescue me from the people who oppress me
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may obey what you have declared that we should do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:134"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="135" style="v" sid="PSA 119:135"/>Please act kindly toward me, your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me what you have decreed that we should do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:135"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="136" style="v" sid="PSA 119:136"/>I cry very much
</para>
  <para style="q2">because many people do not obey your instructions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:136"/></para>
  <para style="qa">TSADHE
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="137" style="v" sid="PSA 119:137"/>Yahweh, you are righteous
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the rules that you have given to us are just.
<verse eid="PSA 119:137"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="138" style="v" sid="PSA 119:138"/>All of the things that you have instructed us to do are absolutely right
</para>
  <para style="q2">and exactly what we need.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:138"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="139" style="v" sid="PSA 119:139"/>I am furious
</para>
  <para style="q2">because my enemies disregard what you have told us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:139"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="140" style="v" sid="PSA 119:140"/>All of the things that you have said are perfectly dependable,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I, your servant, love them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:140"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="141" style="v" sid="PSA 119:141"/>I am not important, and people despise me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I do not forget what you have declared that we should do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:141"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="142" style="v" sid="PSA 119:142"/>You are righteous and you will be righteous forever,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and your instructions are completely reliable.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:142"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="143" style="v" sid="PSA 119:143"/>I am constantly stressed and anxious,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but what you have commanded {us} causes me to rejoice.
<verse eid="PSA 119:143"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="144" style="v" sid="PSA 119:144"/>All of the things that you have instructed us to do are always right;
</para>
  <para style="q2">help me to understand them in order that I may {continue to} live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:144"/></para>
  <para style="qa">QOPH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="145" style="v" sid="PSA 119:145"/>Yahweh, fervently I call out to you; please answer me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I fully intend to obey what you have decreed that we should do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:145"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="146" style="v" sid="PSA 119:146"/>I call out to you, “Save me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order that I may obey the things that you have instructed us to do.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:146"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="147" style="v" sid="PSA 119:147"/>{Each morning} I arise before dawn and call to you to help me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I confidently wait for you to do what you have promised to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:147"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="148" style="v" sid="PSA 119:148"/>All during the night I am awake,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I can think about what you have said {to us}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:148"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="149" style="v" sid="PSA 119:149"/>Yahweh, because you faithfully love me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please listen to me {while I pray};
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you do what is right, make me joyful again in living {for you}.
<verse eid="PSA 119:149"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="150" style="v" sid="PSA 119:150"/>People who intend to harm me are approaching me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they completely disregard your instructions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:150"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="151" style="v" sid="PSA 119:151"/>But Yahweh, you are near to me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and {I know that} what you command is completely right.
<verse eid="PSA 119:151"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="152" style="v" sid="PSA 119:152"/>Long ago, I learned from what you have said
</para>
  <para style="q2">that you established your commandments to last forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:152"/></para>
  <para style="qa">RESH
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="153" style="v" sid="PSA 119:153"/>Please acknowledge that I am suffering, and save me {from it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I continually obey your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:153"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="154" style="v" sid="PSA 119:154"/>Defend me {when others accuse me} and rescue me {from them};
</para>
  <para style="q2">allow me {to continue} to live as you promised that you would do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:154"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="155" style="v" sid="PSA 119:155"/>Wicked people do not obey what you have decreed that we should do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so you will certainly not save them.
<verse eid="PSA 119:155"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="156" style="v" sid="PSA 119:156"/>Yahweh, you are constantly being merciful {to me} in many ways;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you always do what is right, please allow me {to continue} to live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:156"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="157" style="v" sid="PSA 119:157"/>Many people cause me to suffer,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I continue to obey what you have instructed us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:157"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="158" style="v" sid="PSA 119:158"/>When I look at those who are not faithful to you, I feel disgust
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they do not obey what you have instructed us to do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:158"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="159" style="v" sid="PSA 119:159"/>Yahweh, please notice that I love what you have declared that we should do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you faithfully love me, please allow me {to continue} to live.
<verse eid="PSA 119:159"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="160" style="v" sid="PSA 119:160"/>Everything that you have said is true;
</para>
  <para style="q2">every statement that you have made is right and will endure forever.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:160"/></para>
  <para style="qa">SIN and SHIN
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="161" style="v" sid="PSA 119:161"/>Rulers persecute me for no reason,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I deeply respect your words.
<verse eid="PSA 119:161"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="162" style="v" sid="PSA 119:162"/>The things that you say make me very happy,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as happy as someone who has found a great treasure.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:162"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="163" style="v" sid="PSA 119:163"/>I thoroughly hate {all} lies
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I love your instructions.
<verse eid="PSA 119:163"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="164" style="v" sid="PSA 119:164"/>I praise you throughout the day
</para>
  <para style="q2">because everything that you tell us to do is completely right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:164"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="165" style="v" sid="PSA 119:165"/>Those who love your instructions live very peacefully;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will continually do the right thing.
<verse eid="PSA 119:165"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="166" style="v" sid="PSA 119:166"/>Yahweh, I confidently expect that you will rescue me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I obey what you have commanded {us}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:166"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="167" style="v" sid="PSA 119:167"/>I obey what you have told us to do;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I love all of it very much.
<verse eid="PSA 119:167"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="168" style="v" sid="PSA 119:168"/>I obey what you have instructed us to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you know everything that I do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:168"/></para>
  <para style="qa">TAW
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="169" style="v" sid="PSA 119:169"/>Yahweh, please listen as I call out to you {to help me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">help me to understand {your message}, as you said that you would do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:169"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="170" style="v" sid="PSA 119:170"/>Please pay attention to me while I pray to you to help me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and rescue me as you said that you would do.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:170"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="171" style="v" sid="PSA 119:171"/>I intend to continue praising {you} abundantly
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you teach me what you have told us to do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:171"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="172" style="v" sid="PSA 119:172"/>I intend to continue singing about your instructions
</para>
  <para style="q2">because everything that you command us to do is right.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:172"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="173" style="v" sid="PSA 119:173"/>Please be always ready to help me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I have chosen to obey what you have declared that we should do.
<verse eid="PSA 119:173"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="174" style="v" sid="PSA 119:174"/>Yahweh, I eagerly desire for you to rescue me {from my enemies},
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I greatly enjoy your instructions.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 119:174"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="175" style="v" sid="PSA 119:175"/>Please allow me to {continue to} live in order that I may {continue to} praise you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may the things that you tell us to do {continue to} help me.
<verse eid="PSA 119:175"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="176" style="v" sid="PSA 119:176"/>I am as vulnerable as a sheep that has left its flock;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please search for me, your servant, because I have not forgotten what you have commanded {us}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 119:176"/><verse eid="PSA 119:176"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 119"/>
  <chapter number="120" style="c" sid="PSA 120"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 120:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When I was distressed, I called out to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he answered me.

<verse eid="PSA 120:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 120:2"/>{I prayed,} “Yahweh, rescue me from people who tell lies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who say things to deceive me!”

<verse eid="PSA 120:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 120:3"/>You people who lie, God will certainly punish you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will do even more to you than that.

<verse eid="PSA 120:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 120:4"/>He will punish you severely as with a warrior’s sharp arrows,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and as with burning coals from broom tree wood.

<verse eid="PSA 120:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 120:5"/>It is terrible for me that I {have to} live among {people like those in} Meshech,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{that} I {have to} dwell with {people like those who live in} the tents of Kedar.

<verse eid="PSA 120:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 120:6"/>I have lived too long among people
</para>
  <para style="q2">who hate to live peacefully with others.

<verse eid="PSA 120:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 120:7"/>I want to live peacefully, but whenever I speak {about it},
</para>
  <para style="q2">they want to fight.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 120:7"/><verse eid="PSA 120:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 120"/>
  <chapter number="121" style="c" sid="PSA 121"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 121:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I look toward the hills
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and I ask myself,} “Where will anyone to help me come from?”
<verse eid="PSA 121:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 121:2"/>{I answer myself,} “Yahweh is the one who helps me.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the one who made everything that exists.
<verse eid="PSA 121:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 121:3"/>{You say,} “May Yahweh not let you stumble.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May Yahweh, who protects you, not become drowsy!”
<verse eid="PSA 121:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 121:4"/>{I reply,} “Listen to me, the one who protects the people of Israel
</para>
  <para style="q2">will never become drowsy; he never sleeps!”
<verse eid="PSA 121:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 121:5"/>Yahweh watches over you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He stays between you and what might harm you, like a shade {from the sun}.
<verse eid="PSA 121:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 121:6"/>The sun will not harm you during the day,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the moon will not harm you at night.
<verse eid="PSA 121:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 121:7"/>Yahweh will protect you from everything that could harm you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He will keep you safe.
<verse eid="PSA 121:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 121:8"/>Yahweh will protect you in everything that you do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He will do that} now, and {he will do that} forever.


<verse eid="PSA 121:8"/><verse eid="PSA 121:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 121"/>
  <chapter number="122" style="c" sid="PSA 122"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 122:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship. This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I was very happy when people said to me, “We should go to Yahweh’s temple {in Jerusalem}!”

<verse eid="PSA 122:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 122:2"/>Now we are standing inside the gates of Jerusalem.

<verse eid="PSA 122:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 122:3"/>This is Jerusalem, the city that people have built in a way that everything fits closely together.

<verse eid="PSA 122:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 122:4"/>The tribes of Israel who belong to Yahweh go there,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as Yahweh told them to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in order to thank him.

<verse eid="PSA 122:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 122:5"/>Indeed, the kings who belong to King David’s family
</para>
  <para style="q2">sit on their thrones there and judge {the people}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 122:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 122:6"/>Pray that people will live peacefully in Jerusalem!
</para>
  <para style="q2">May those who love Jerusalem be successful.

<verse eid="PSA 122:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 122:7"/>May everyone inside the city walls live well and prosper.

<verse eid="PSA 122:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 122:8"/>Because I love my fellow Israelites and my friends,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I want to say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“May the people in Jerusalem live well.”

<verse eid="PSA 122:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 122:9"/>Because Yahweh our God has his temple there,
</para>
  <para style="q2">I intend to always do what is best for Jerusalem.


<verse eid="PSA 122:9"/><verse eid="PSA 122:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 122"/>
  <chapter number="123" style="c" sid="PSA 123"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 123:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I look up toward you
</para>
  <para style="q2">who live in heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 123:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 123:2"/>You see, just as servants watch their master closely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">waiting for him to provide for them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and just as a female servant watches her mistress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the same way, we look to Yahweh our God,
</para>
  <para style="q2">waiting for him to be merciful to us.
<verse eid="PSA 123:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 123:3"/>Yahweh, please be very merciful to us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because people have despised us so much that we cannot endure any more.
<verse eid="PSA 123:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 123:4"/>We have endured far too much mocking
</para>
  <para style="q2">from people who are arrogant,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, from proud people who despise us.


<verse eid="PSA 123:4"/><verse eid="PSA 123:4"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 123"/>
  <chapter number="124" style="c" sid="PSA 124"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 124:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship; of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If Yahweh had not been helping us—
</para>
  <para style="q2">All Israelites should repeat this—
<verse eid="PSA 124:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 124:2"/>If Yahweh had not been helping us
</para>
  <para style="q2">when our enemies attacked us,
<verse eid="PSA 124:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 124:3"/>then they would have destroyed us completely,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they were so angry with us.
<verse eid="PSA 124:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 124:4"/>They would have overwhelmed us like a flood;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they would have swept over us like a raging river.
<verse eid="PSA 124:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 124:5"/>{They would have destroyed us as completely as} raging waters would have drowned us.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 124:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 124:6"/>We praise Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he did not let our enemies destroy us
</para>
  <para style="q2">as wild animals devour their prey.
<verse eid="PSA 124:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 124:7"/>We escaped from them like a bird that gets free from a hunter’s trap.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It was as though the trap broke, and, as for us, we went free!
<verse eid="PSA 124:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 124:8"/>Yahweh is the one who helps us;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he is the one who made everything that exists.


<verse eid="PSA 124:8"/><verse eid="PSA 124:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 124"/>
  <chapter number="125" style="c" sid="PSA 125"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 125:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">People who trust in Yahweh are as secure as Mount Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">which will stand firm forever.
<verse eid="PSA 125:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 125:2"/>Just as the hills surrounding Jerusalem protect the city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so Yahweh protects his people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will protect them forever.

<verse eid="PSA 125:2"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 125:3"/>Indeed, wicked people will not rule over the land that God gave to righteous people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that righteous people will not start doing what is wrong.

<verse eid="PSA 125:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 125:4"/>Yahweh, please do good things for people who do good things for others,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, for those who obey you sincerely.
<verse eid="PSA 125:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 125:5"/>But as for those people who choose to do evil things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh will send them away along with everyone else who does evil things.
</para>
  <para style="q1">May Yahweh bless the people of Israel!


<verse eid="PSA 125:5"/><verse eid="PSA 125:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 125"/>
  <chapter number="126" style="c" sid="PSA 126"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 126:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When Yahweh brought us back to Zion after our enemies had captured us {and taken us away},
</para>
  <para style="q2">we felt as if we were dreaming.
<verse eid="PSA 126:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 126:2"/>We laughed and shouted joyfully.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Then people from other people groups said about us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Yahweh has done great things for them!”
<verse eid="PSA 126:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 126:3"/>{Yes!} Yahweh {truly} has done great things for us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and we are very happy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 126:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 126:4"/>Yahweh, restore us as before our enemies captured us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as you restore the streams in the Negev {that flow again after being dry}.
<verse eid="PSA 126:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 126:5"/>Those who sow seeds while crying
</para>
  <para style="q2">will shout joyfully when they gather the harvest.
<verse eid="PSA 126:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 126:6"/>They may indeed walk {through the field} crying,
</para>
  <para style="q2">as they spread the seed from their bags.
</para>
  <para style="q1">But they will surely come back shouting joyfully,
</para>
  <para style="q2">carrying their bundles of grain.


<verse eid="PSA 126:6"/><verse eid="PSA 126:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 126"/>
  <chapter number="127" style="c" sid="PSA 127"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 127:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for people going up to the temple to worship. It is of Solomon.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If people are building a house, but Yahweh does not approve of it,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those who build it are doing nothing useful.
</para>
  <para style="q1">If Yahweh does not protect a city,
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is useless for the guards to stay awake watching it.
<verse eid="PSA 127:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 127:2"/>It is useless for you to get up very early and stay up very late,
</para>
  <para style="q2">working hard to get food,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because Yahweh wants to give sleep to those whom he loves.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 127:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 127:3"/>Children are a gift that Yahweh gives;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Offspring are a benefit {from him}.
<verse eid="PSA 127:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 127:4"/>When a man has sons while he is still young,
</para>
  <para style="q2">those sons become as useful as arrows are in the hand of a warrior.
<verse eid="PSA 127:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 127:5"/>A man who has many sons has such a good life!
</para>
  <para style="q2">When he argues with an opponent at the place where people settle disputes,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the opponent will not defeat him.


<verse eid="PSA 127:5"/><verse eid="PSA 127:5"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 127"/>
  <chapter number="128" style="c" sid="PSA 128"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 128:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for those going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">How good life is for all who deeply revere Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who do what he tells them to do!
<verse eid="PSA 128:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 128:2"/>You will enjoy eating the food that you have worked hard for,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and it will make you healthy.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 128:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 128:3"/>Your wife will bear many children in the innermost rooms of your house,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a grapevine that produces many grapes.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Your children will grow strong like young olive trees
</para>
  <para style="q2">as they fill the room around your table.
<verse eid="PSA 128:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 128:4"/>Yes, that is how Yahweh will bless every person
</para>
  <para style="q2">who deeply reveres him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 128:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 128:5"/>May Yahweh bless you from {where he lives} in Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that you may be able to experience how the people of Jerusalem prosper
</para>
  <para style="q2">during the whole time that you live,
<verse eid="PSA 128:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 128:6"/>and so that you may live long enough to see your grandchildren!
</para>
  <para style="q2">May the people of Israel live well!


<verse eid="PSA 128:6"/><verse eid="PSA 128:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 128"/>
  <chapter number="129" style="c" sid="PSA 129"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 129:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">A psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Ever since I was young, my enemies have oppressed me frequently.
</para>
  <para style="q2">All of the people of Israel should say this {with me}:
<verse eid="PSA 129:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 129:2"/>Ever since I was young, my enemies have oppressed me frequently,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but they have never defeated me!
<verse eid="PSA 129:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 129:3"/>{They oppressed me severely as though} they were plowing across my back,
</para>
  <para style="q2">making long wounds like furrows in a field.
<verse eid="PSA 129:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 129:4"/>Yahweh does what is right;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he no longer allows wicked people to control me.
<verse eid="PSA 129:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 129:5"/>May everyone who hates the people of Zion be ashamed and go away.
<verse eid="PSA 129:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 129:6"/>May they be {as insignificant} as the grass that grows on the rooftops
</para>
  <para style="q2">that dries up before anyone can pull it out,
<verse eid="PSA 129:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 129:7"/>that no harvester would {bother to} pick up
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that no one gathering bundles would {want to} wrap his arms around {to tie it up}.
<verse eid="PSA 129:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 129:8"/>They will never hear someone walking by {the reapers} say,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“May Yahweh bless you!”
</para>
  <para style="q2">{They will not hear the reapers reply,} “We bless you as representatives of Yahweh.”


<verse eid="PSA 129:8"/><verse eid="PSA 129:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 129"/>
  <chapter number="130" style="c" sid="PSA 130"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 130:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I am very distressed, so I call out to you.
<verse eid="PSA 130:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 130:2"/>Lord, please listen to me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please listen attentively as I call out to you to have mercy on me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 130:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 130:3"/>Yahweh, if you kept a record of {the} sins {that we have committed},
</para>
  <para style="q2">Lord, you would have to condemn and punish every one of us!
<verse eid="PSA 130:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 130:4"/>But you forgive us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">with the result that we deeply revere you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 130:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 130:5"/>Yahweh has said {that he would help me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">I trust what he said, and so I wait eagerly for him {to do that}.
<verse eid="PSA 130:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 130:6"/>I wait for the Lord {to help me}
</para>
  <para style="q2">more {eagerly} than watchmen wait for the morning {to come};
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, I wait more eagerly than watchmen wait for the morning!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 130:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 130:7"/>{My fellow} Israelites, confidently expect that Yahweh will help us.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{He will help us} because he faithfully loves us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he is very willing to save us.
<verse eid="PSA 130:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 130:8"/>It is he who will make it so he will not need to punish {us} Israelite people for all the sins that {we} have committed.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 130:8"/><verse eid="PSA 130:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 130"/>
  <chapter number="131" style="c" sid="PSA 131"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 131:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for people going up to the temple to worship. It is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I am not a proud, haughty person.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I do not concern myself with things that are too great or too amazing for me.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 131:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 131:2"/>Instead, I have calmed myself,
</para>
  <para style="q2">like a weaned child who rests {calmly} on {the breast of} his mother.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, my inner being is peaceful like that contented child.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 131:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 131:3"/>Israelites, confidently expect Yahweh {to do good things for you},
</para>
  <para style="q2">now and forever!


<verse eid="PSA 131:3"/><verse eid="PSA 131:3"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 131"/>
  <chapter number="132" style="c" sid="PSA 132"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 132:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, think about {King} David
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the many ways that he suffered.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 132:2"/>He made a solemn promise to Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Mighty God whom Jacob worshiped.
<verse eid="PSA 132:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 132:3"/>{He said,} “I will not go home
</para>
  <para style="q2">or lie down on my bed to rest.
<verse eid="PSA 132:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 132:4"/>I will not allow myself to sleep at all
<verse eid="PSA 132:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 132:5"/>until I build a home for Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the Mighty God whom Jacob worshiped.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 132:6"/>Listen, we heard about the sacred chest in Ephrathah;
</para>
  <para style="q2">we found it in the fields near Jaar (Kiriath-Jearim).
<verse eid="PSA 132:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 132:7"/>{We said}, “Let us go to the place where Yahweh lives;
</para>
  <para style="q2">let us worship {before the sacred chest} where he rests his feet.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 132:8"/>Yahweh, come to the place where you will stay,
</para>
  <para style="q2">together with the sacred chest that represents your powerful presence.
<verse eid="PSA 132:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 132:9"/>May your priests always do what is right,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may the people who are faithful to you shout joyfully.
<verse eid="PSA 132:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 132:10"/>Because of what you promised to David, who served you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not reject the king whom you chose.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 132:11"/>Yahweh swore a promise to David,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he will certainly not take it back: “I will place one of your own descendants
</para>
  <para style="q2">{to rule as king} on your throne.
<verse eid="PSA 132:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 132:12"/>If your sons obey my covenant
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the commands that I will teach them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">then their sons will also rule as kings on your throne forever.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 132:13"/>Indeed, Yahweh has chosen Zion
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he wanted it to be the place where he lives.
<verse eid="PSA 132:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 132:14"/>{He said,} “This is the place where I will stay forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will live here because I have chosen this place.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 132:15"/>I will certainly give the people of Zion everything that they need;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will give enough food to satisfy {even} the poor people who live there.
<verse eid="PSA 132:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 132:16"/>I will enable the priests of Zion to show others what a person looks like whom I have saved,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the people there who are faithful to me will shout very joyfully.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 132:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 132:17"/>In Zion I will cause a powerful king to come from David’s family;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I have arranged for the king whom I have chosen that a son of his will always rule.
<verse eid="PSA 132:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 132:18"/>I will cause his enemies to be very ashamed,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but his kingdom will prosper.”


<verse eid="PSA 132:18"/><verse eid="PSA 132:18"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 132"/>
  <chapter number="133" style="c" sid="PSA 133"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 133:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for people going up to the temple to worship. It is of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Think about how wonderful and delightful it is when God’s people live together {in a unified way}!
<verse eid="PSA 133:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 133:2"/>It is as delightful as {watching someone pour} fine olive oil on the head of Aaron, {the priest,}
</para>
  <para style="q2">oil that runs down onto his beard
</para>
  <para style="q2">and flows down to the collar of his robes.
<verse eid="PSA 133:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 133:3"/>It is as delightful as {feeling} the dew from Mount Hermon
</para>
  <para style="q2">coming down on the mountains of Zion.
</para>
  <para style="q1">That is where Yahweh blessed {his people},
</para>
  <para style="q2">giving them a way to live forever.


<verse eid="PSA 133:3"/><verse eid="PSA 133:3"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 133"/>
  <chapter number="134" style="c" sid="PSA 134"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 134:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm for people going up to the temple to worship.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Listen! Praise Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all you who serve Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you who stand in Yahweh’s temple during the night hours.
<verse eid="PSA 134:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 134:2"/>Raise your hands {to pray toward} the holy place
</para>
  <para style="q2">and praise Yahweh.
<verse eid="PSA 134:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 134:3"/>I pray that Yahweh will bless you from {his temple on} Mount Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">{for} he is the one who made everything that exists.


<verse eid="PSA 134:3"/><verse eid="PSA 134:3"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 134"/>
  <chapter number="135" style="c" sid="PSA 135"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 135:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise him because of who he is!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You who serve Yahweh, praise him,
<verse eid="PSA 135:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 135:2"/>you who stand {and serve} in Yahweh’s temple,
</para>
  <para style="q2">in the courtyards of the house of our God!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 135:3"/>Praise Yahweh, because he is good;
</para>
  <para style="q2">sing praises to him, because doing that is delightful.
<verse eid="PSA 135:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 135:4"/>Praise him because Yahweh chose {us,} the descendants of Jacob,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the people of Israel, to belong only to him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 135:5"/>Indeed, I know very well that Yahweh is great
</para>
  <para style="q2">and that our Lord is more powerful than all other spirit beings.
<verse eid="PSA 135:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 135:6"/>Yahweh does whatever he wants to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">everywhere, whether it is in heaven or on the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">or in the ocean, even deep down in the ocean.
<verse eid="PSA 135:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 135:7"/>He causes clouds to form in distant places on the earth;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he makes lightning flash along with the rain,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he sends out wind from the places where he stores it.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 135:8"/>He killed every firstborn in Egypt,
</para>
  <para style="q2">including those from both people and animals.
<verse eid="PSA 135:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 135:9"/>He did amazing miracles
</para>
  <para style="q2">among the people of Egypt
</para>
  <para style="q2">to punish Pharaoh and all of his officials.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 135:10"/>He defeated many nations
</para>
  <para style="q2">and killed their powerful kings.
<verse eid="PSA 135:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 135:11"/>He killed Sihon, king of the Amorites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and Og, king of Bashan,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all the kings of Canaan.
<verse eid="PSA 135:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 135:12"/>Then he gave the land that those kings had ruled over
</para>
  <para style="q2">to his own people, that is, to {us,} the people of Israel, to be our own land.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 135:13"/>Yahweh, people will always know how great you are;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, people in every generation will remember you,
<verse eid="PSA 135:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 135:14"/>because Yahweh defends his people
</para>
  <para style="q2">and is merciful to those who serve him.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 135:15"/>The idols that other people groups worship are only statues made of silver and gold;
</para>
  <para style="q2">people made them with their own hands.
<verse eid="PSA 135:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 135:16"/>Those idols have mouths, but they cannot say anything;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have eyes, but they cannot see anything.
<verse eid="PSA 135:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 135:17"/>They have ears, but they cannot hear anything;
</para>
  <para style="q2">In fact, they do not even breathe.
<verse eid="PSA 135:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 135:18"/>The people who make those idols will become as helpless as they are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and so will everyone who trusts in them.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 135:19"/>You Israelites, praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You descendants of Aaron, praise Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 135:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 135:20"/>You descendants of Levi, praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">All you who deeply revere Yahweh, praise him!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 135:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 135:21"/>Praise Yahweh from his temple on Mount Zion,
</para>
  <para style="q2">where he lives in Jerusalem!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!


<verse eid="PSA 135:21"/><verse eid="PSA 135:21"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 135"/>
  <chapter number="136" style="c" sid="PSA 136"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 136:1"/>Thank Yahweh because he is good {to us},
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 136:2"/>Thank God, the one who is greater than all other spirit beings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 136:3"/>Thank the Lord, the one who is greater than all other rulers;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 136:4"/>{Thank} him, the only one who does wonderful miracles,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 136:5"/>{Thank} him, the one who wisely created the heavens;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 136:6"/>{Thank} him, the one who formed the earth over the waters;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 136:7"/>{Thank} him, the one who created the great lights {in the sky};
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 136:8"/>{He made} the sun to light up the daytime,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 136:9"/>{He made} the moon and stars to light up the nighttime,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 136:10"/>{Thank} him, who killed the firstborn {sons} of the Egyptians;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 136:11"/>He brought the Israelite people out from among them,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 136:12"/>He did that by being very powerful,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 136:13"/>{Thank} him, the one who divided the Sea of Reeds into {two} parts;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 136:14"/>He enabled the Israelite people to walk through the middle of it {on dry land},
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 136:15"/>But he caused Pharaoh and his army to drown in the Sea of Reeds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 136:16"/>{Thank} him, the one who led his people {safely} through the desert,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 136:17"/>{Thank} him, the one who defeated powerful kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 136:18"/>He killed powerful kings,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 136:19"/>{He killed} Sihon, the king of the Amorites,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 136:20"/>{He killed} Og, the king of Bashan;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 136:21"/>He gave their land to the people of Israel to possess;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 136:22"/>{He gave it} to the people of Israel, who serve him, to be our own land,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 136:23"/>He did not forget about us when our enemies were oppressing us,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 136:24"/>He rescued us from our enemies,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!
<verse eid="PSA 136:24"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="25" style="v" sid="PSA 136:25"/>He gives food to every living creature;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 136:25"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="26" style="v" sid="PSA 136:26"/>Thank God, who rules from heaven;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he faithfully loves {us} forever!


<verse eid="PSA 136:26"/><verse eid="PSA 136:26"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 136"/>
  <chapter number="137" style="c" sid="PSA 137"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 137:1"/>{After soldiers had taken us to} Babylon, we sat down by the rivers there,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and we cried when we thought about {the temple on Mount} Zion {in Jerusalem}.
<verse eid="PSA 137:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 137:2"/>We hung our harps on the willow trees there
</para>
  <para style="q2">{and did not play them}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 137:3"/>We did that because those who had captured us {and taken us} there demanded that we sing for them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They tormented us and told us to sing a joyful song. {They said,} “Sing for us one of the songs about Zion!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 137:4"/>{We thought}, “We are not able to sing {joyful} songs about Yahweh
</para>
  <para style="q2">in this foreign land!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 137:5"/>If I ever forget about Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">may my right hand be unable {to play the harp}!
<verse eid="PSA 137:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 137:6"/>May my tongue and my mouth make me unable to sing
</para>
  <para style="q1">if I forget about Jerusalem,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or {even} if I do not consider that Jerusalem causes me to be more joyful
</para>
  <para style="q2">than anything else does.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 137:7"/>Yahweh, please punish the Edomites for what they did
</para>
  <para style="q2">when the enemy destroyed Jerusalem. They shouted,
</para>
  <para style="q2">“Completely tear it down to its foundations!”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 137:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 137:8"/>Concerning the people of Babylon, who devastate {other nations},
</para>
  <para style="q2">How good it will be for the person who completely pays them back
</para>
  <para style="q2">with what they did to us!
<verse eid="PSA 137:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 137:9"/>How good it will be for the one who seizes your babies
</para>
  <para style="q2">and smashes them against the rocks!


<verse eid="PSA 137:9"/><verse eid="PSA 137:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 137"/>
  <chapter number="138" style="c" sid="PSA 138"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 138:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I sincerely thank you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">In the presence of {idols of} other gods, I sing to praise you.
<verse eid="PSA 138:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 138:2"/>I bow down toward your sacred temple {to worship you}
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I thank you because you faithfully love us and because we can trust you to do all that you have promised.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You have given cause for people everywhere to honor you and what you have said more than anything else.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 138:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 138:3"/>When I called out to you, you helped me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you enabled me to be brave and strong.
<verse eid="PSA 138:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 138:4"/>Yahweh, {someday} all the kings of this earth should praise you
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they will have heard what you have said.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 138:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 138:5"/>They should sing about what you have done
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you are very glorious.
<verse eid="PSA 138:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 138:6"/>Yahweh, although you live in heaven,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you take care of humble people.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Proud people, however, you identify from far away.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 138:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 138:7"/>Even when dangerous things happen all around me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you keep me safe.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You rescue me from my enemies who are angry with me.
<verse eid="PSA 138:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 138:8"/>Yahweh, I know that you will continue to do what is good for me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, you faithfully love {us} forever.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please do not abandon {us,} the people that you have made!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 138:8"/><verse eid="PSA 138:8"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 138"/>
  <chapter number="139" style="c" sid="PSA 139"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 139:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a note for the worship leader: This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, you have thoroughly examined me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you know {me completely}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 139:2"/>You are the one who knows everything that I do, including when I sit and when I stand.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even from far away, you know what I am thinking.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 139:3"/>You have examined in detail all of my movements, from the time I go out until I lie down,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you know intimately all of my habits.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 139:4"/>Indeed, even before I say anything,
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, you already know everything that I am going to say!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 139:5"/>You guard me on every side,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you put your hand on me {to protect me}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 139:6"/>I am in awe that you know everything about me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am not able to comprehend that.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 139:7"/>There is nowhere I could go to get away from your Spirit!
</para>
  <para style="q2">There is nowhere I could run to escape from your presence!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 139:8"/>If I went up to heaven, you would be there.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even if I lay down in the place where dead people go, you would be there!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 139:9"/>If I rose up and flew to where the sun rises in the east,
</para>
  <para style="q2">or if I settled in the farthest place across the {western} sea,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 139:10"/>even there you would guide me
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you would keep me secure.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 139:11"/>Even if I said, “Let the darkness completely overwhelm me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the light around me turn to night,”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 139:12"/>even darkness is not dark to you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the night shines as bright as the daytime.
</para>
  <para style="q2">For you, darkness and light are the same.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 139:13"/>Indeed, you are the one who created my deepest inner parts;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you formed me inside my mother’s womb.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 139:14"/>I praise you because you made me in such an awesome and wonderful way.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Everything that you do is wonderful!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I know that very well.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 139:15"/>You saw my bones when you made me in that hidden place.
</para>
  <para style="q1">As you wove me together deep in the womb,

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 139:16"/>you saw me before I had any form.
</para>
  <para style="q1">You wrote in your book each day that you had planned for me to live,
</para>
  <para style="q2">before any of those days had even started.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 139:17"/>God, the things that you think are very valuable to me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">There are so many of them!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 139:18"/>If I tried to count them, {I would not be able to do that, because} they are more than the grains of sand {on the earth}.
</para>
  <para style="q2">{Every morning} I wake up, I am still with you, {and there are still more of them to count}.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 139:19"/>God, I wish that you would kill all wicked people!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I wish that all violent men would go away from me!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 139:20"/>They say wicked things about you and plan evil things;
</para>
  <para style="q2">your enemies misuse your name.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 139:21"/>Yahweh, I certainly hate those who hate you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I am disgusted with those who rise up against you.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:21"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="22" style="v" sid="PSA 139:22"/>I hate them completely;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I consider them to be my enemies.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:22"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="23" style="v" sid="PSA 139:23"/>God, I invite you to search me and to know what I am thinking;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please examine me and know what I worry about.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 139:23"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="24" style="v" sid="PSA 139:24"/>See if there is any harmful way in me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and teach me to live in the way that lasts forever.


<verse eid="PSA 139:24"/><verse eid="PSA 139:24"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 139"/>
  <chapter number="140" style="c" sid="PSA 140"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a note to the worship leader: David wrote this psalm.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 140:1"/>Yahweh, please save me from evil people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">protect me from people who want to attack me.
<verse eid="PSA 140:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 140:2"/>They are always planning how to do evil things,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and every day they provoke fights.
<verse eid="PSA 140:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 140:3"/>They say things {to people} that hurt {them};
</para>
  <para style="q2">what comes from their mouths is as deadly as the venom of a viper.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 140:3"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 140:4"/>Yahweh, protect me from wicked people who want to harm me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">keep me safe from violent people
</para>
  <para style="q1">who have planned to destroy me.
<verse eid="PSA 140:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 140:5"/>Proud people are trying to destroy me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{It is as though} they have hidden a snare for me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{It is as though} they have spread out a net along my path;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{It is as though} they have set traps to catch me.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 140:5"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 140:6"/>I say to you, “Yahweh, you are my God.”
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh, please listen to me as I plead with you to help me!
<verse eid="PSA 140:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 140:7"/>Yahweh, my Lord, you are the one who powerfully saves me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you have protected me during battles as though you had covered my head {with a helmet}.

<verse eid="PSA 140:7"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 140:8"/>Yahweh, do not give wicked people what they want;
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not let their plans succeed, or they will become proud.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<verse eid="PSA 140:8"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 140:9"/>As for the leaders of those who surround me,
</para>
  <para style="q2">let the harmful things that they have said {to others} happen to them.
<verse eid="PSA 140:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 140:10"/>Pour burning coals on them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Throw them into a fire!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Throw them into deep holes from which they will never get out!
<verse eid="PSA 140:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 140:11"/>Yahweh, please do not allow people who slander others to prosper in this land;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Cause evil things to continually happen to violent people and destroy them.

<verse eid="PSA 140:11"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <ms style="ts"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 140:12"/>Yahweh, I know that you do what is just
</para>
  <para style="q2">and right for poor people.
<verse eid="PSA 140:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 140:13"/>People who do what is right will surely thank you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will live with you.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 140:13"/><verse eid="PSA 140:13"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 140"/>
  <chapter number="141" style="c" sid="PSA 141"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 141:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, I call out to you; please help me quickly!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please listen to me when I am calling out to you.
<verse eid="PSA 141:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 141:2"/>Please accept my prayer {as though it were} an offering of incense to you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please accept me while I lift up my hands {to pray to you},
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as you accept the sacrifices that people offer to you each evening.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 141:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 141:3"/>Yahweh, do not allow me to say things that are bad or wrong.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Do not allow me to say those things as a sentry does not allow the wrong people to go through a doorway.
<verse eid="PSA 141:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 141:4"/>Prevent me from wanting to do anything that is wrong
</para>
  <para style="q2">and from joining with wicked men when they want to do evil deeds.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not even allow me to share in eating their delightful food!

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 141:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 141:5"/>It is all right if righteous people strike me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they are acting faithfully and kindly toward me to correct me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{If they do that, it will be as if they have honored me by} anointing my head with {olive} oil, and may I never refuse to accept it.
</para>
  <para style="q2">but I am always praying that you will punish the wicked because of the wicked deeds that they do.
<verse eid="PSA 141:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 141:6"/>When their rulers are thrown down from the top of rocky cliffs,
</para>
  <para style="q2">the wicked will hear what I am saying, and will know that what I am saying is right and good.
<verse eid="PSA 141:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 141:7"/>{They will say,} “Just as one scatters {clods of earth} when he breaks up the ground, {soon} our bodies will lie scattered on the way to the place where dead people are.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 141:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 141:8"/>But Lord Yahweh, I continue to rely on you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">I ask you to protect me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">please do not stop protecting my life!
<verse eid="PSA 141:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 141:9"/>People who do evil things are trying to trick me and destroy me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">It is as though they have laid out snares and set traps for me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Please keep me safe from what they are trying to do to me.
<verse eid="PSA 141:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 141:10"/>I desire that wicked people fall together into the traps that they have set {to catch me},
</para>
  <para style="q2">while, for my part, I escape {from them}.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 141:10"/><verse eid="PSA 141:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 141"/>
  <chapter number="142" style="c" sid="PSA 142"/>
  <para style="p"/>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm that David prayed when he was hiding in a cave.
</para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 142:1"/>Yahweh, I cry out to you;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I plead for you to help me.
<verse eid="PSA 142:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 142:2"/>I am complaining to you about {all of} my problems;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I am telling you {all of} my troubles.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 142:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 142:3"/>When I am very discouraged,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you are the one who knows what I must do.
</para>
  <para style="q1">As I go about my activities, {it is as though} my enemies have hidden traps along my path for me {to fall into}.
<verse eid="PSA 142:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 142:4"/>If you look to my right you will see
</para>
  <para style="q2">that there is no one who watches over me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">There is nowhere I can go to be safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and no one cares what happens to me.
<verse eid="PSA 142:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 142:5"/>So Yahweh, I called out to you {to help me};
</para>
  <para style="q2">I said, “You are the one who protects me;
</para>
  <para style="q1">you are all that I need while I am alive.”

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 142:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 142:6"/>Please listen to me while I call out to you {to help me}
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I am very distressed.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Save me from those who are making me suffer,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because they are stronger than I am.
<verse eid="PSA 142:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 142:7"/>Please free me from those who are distressing me
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that I may thank you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">When you do that, the other righteous people will gather with me {to praise you together}
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you will have fulfilled my request.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 142:7"/><verse eid="PSA 142:7"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 142"/>
  <chapter number="143" style="c" sid="PSA 143"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 143:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Yahweh, please listen to me as I pray to you, pleading for you to help me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Because you are righteous
</para>
  <para style="q2">and because you faithfully do what you have promised,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please do what I am asking you to do for me!
<verse eid="PSA 143:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 143:2"/>Please do not judge me, your servant,
</para>
  <para style="q1">because you know that there is no one alive who is completely innocent.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 143:3"/>Please help me because my enemies have pursued me;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they have completely defeated me.
</para>
  <para style="q1">{It is as though} they have already put me in a grave
</para>
  <para style="q1">like people who are dead for eternity.
<verse eid="PSA 143:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 143:4"/>So I am very discouraged;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I feel very dismayed.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 143:5"/>I remember what has happened previously;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I think about all the things that you have done;
</para>
  <para style="q1">I consider the {great} deeds that you have performed.
<verse eid="PSA 143:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 143:6"/>I lift up my hands to you {as I pray};
</para>
  <para style="q2">I need you, just as much as a very dry land needs water.
<char style="qs" closed="true">Selah
</char>

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 143:7"/>Yahweh, I am absolutely despairing,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so please answer me right now!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Do not keep away from me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because if you do that, I will {soon} be among those who descend to where the dead people are.
<verse eid="PSA 143:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 143:8"/>Every morning cause me to remember that you faithfully love me
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I trust in you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">show me the things that I should do
</para>
  <para style="q2">because I depend on you for my life.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 143:9"/>Yahweh, please save me from my enemies;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I rely on you to protect me.
<verse eid="PSA 143:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 143:10"/>You are the God to whom I belong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">so teach me to do what pleases you.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I want your good Spirit to show me the best way to live.

<ms style="ts"/>
<verse eid="PSA 143:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 143:11"/>Yahweh, please keep me alive because of who you are;
</para>
  <para style="q2">because you are righteous, please rescue me from {the people who are} oppressing me!
<verse eid="PSA 143:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 143:12"/>I am one who serves you;
</para>
  <para style="q1">so because you faithfully love me as you promised to do,
</para>
  <para style="q2">please kill all of my enemies who want to kill me.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 143:12"/><verse eid="PSA 143:12"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 143"/>
  <chapter number="144" style="c" sid="PSA 144"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 144:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">I praise Yahweh, who protects me!
</para>
  <para style="q2">He equips me to fight well in wars.
<verse eid="PSA 144:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 144:2"/>He is always faithful and kind to me.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He keeps me safe and helps me escape from danger,
</para>
  <para style="q1">as if he were my shield
</para>
  <para style="q2">or a place where I could go to be safe.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He enables me to rule other peoples.
<verse eid="PSA 144:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 144:3"/>Yahweh, people are so insignificant;
</para>
  <para style="q2">it is amazing that you pay any attention to them!
<verse eid="PSA 144:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 144:4"/>People live for only a very short time,
</para>
  <para style="q2">just as a mist or a shadow quickly disappears.
<verse eid="PSA 144:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 144:5"/>Yahweh, please come down from the sky
</para>
  <para style="q2">and split open the mountains so that smoke pours from them.
<verse eid="PSA 144:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 144:6"/>Please send lightning bolts like arrows
</para>
  <para style="q2">against my enemies to make them run away.
<verse eid="PSA 144:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 144:7"/>Reach down from heaven and rescue me from my enemies
</para>
  <para style="q2">who are surrounding me like a dangerous flood.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Save me from the power of these foreign people.
<verse eid="PSA 144:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 144:8"/>They say things that are not true
</para>
  <para style="q2">and raise their right hands to swear oaths that are false.
<verse eid="PSA 144:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 144:9"/>God, I will sing a new song to you
</para>
  <para style="q2">and play my ten-stringed harp to praise you,
<verse eid="PSA 144:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 144:10"/>because you are the one who saves kings
</para>
  <para style="q2">and who rescues me, your servant David, from danger in battle.
<verse eid="PSA 144:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 144:11"/>Save me from the power of these foreign people.
</para>
  <para style="q2">They say things that are not true
</para>
  <para style="q2">and raise their right hands to swear oaths that are false.
<verse eid="PSA 144:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 144:12"/>Then our sons will be like strong plants
</para>
  <para style="q2">that grow tall when they are young,
</para>
  <para style="q1">and our daughters will be as beautiful and stately
</para>
  <para style="q2">as pillars that craftsmen carve to decorate a palace.
<verse eid="PSA 144:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 144:13"/>May our barns overflow with many kinds of crops.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May our sheep give birth to great numbers of lambs,
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, very great numbers as they graze in our pastures.
<verse eid="PSA 144:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 144:14"/>May our oxen be strong to pull plows.
</para>
  <para style="q2">May no one break through our walls, may no one go into exile,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and may no one cry out {in distress} in our city squares.
<verse eid="PSA 144:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 144:15"/>What a good life people have when these things happen for them!
</para>
  <para style="q2">What a good life people have who worship Yahweh as their God!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 144:15"/><verse eid="PSA 144:15"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 144"/>
  <chapter number="145" style="c" sid="PSA 145"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 145:1"/>
  </para>
  <para style="d">This is a psalm of David.
</para>
  <para style="q1">My God and king, I will proclaim that you are very great;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise you now and always.
<verse eid="PSA 145:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 145:2"/>I will bless you every day;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise you forever.
<verse eid="PSA 145:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 145:3"/>Yahweh, you are great, and people should praise you very much;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no one can fully understand how great you are.
<verse eid="PSA 145:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 145:4"/>People of every generation will tell the next generation about what you have done;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they will tell about your mighty deeds.
<verse eid="PSA 145:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 145:5"/>I will think about how very glorious and majestic you are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will think about your wonderful deeds.
<verse eid="PSA 145:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 145:6"/>People will talk about how powerful your awesome deeds are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and I will proclaim how great you are.
<verse eid="PSA 145:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 145:7"/>People will celebrate how very good you are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and they will sing joyfully about how righteous you are.
<verse eid="PSA 145:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 145:8"/>Yahweh acts kindly and mercifully;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he does not quickly become angry, and he faithfully loves us very much.
<verse eid="PSA 145:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 145:9"/>Yahweh is good to everyone,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he acts mercifully toward everything that he has made.
<verse eid="PSA 145:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 145:10"/>Yahweh, all the creatures that you have made will praise you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and the people who are faithful to you will bless you.
<verse eid="PSA 145:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 145:11"/>They will tell others about how gloriously you rule as king
</para>
  <para style="q2">and about how powerful you are,
<verse eid="PSA 145:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 145:12"/>so that all people will know about your mighty deeds
</para>
  <para style="q2">and about how gloriously and majestically you rule.
<verse eid="PSA 145:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 145:13"/>You will never stop ruling as king;
</para>
  <para style="q2">you will rule throughout every generation.
<verse eid="PSA 145:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 145:14"/>Yahweh sustains people who are in difficult circumstances,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he helps those who are struggling.
<verse eid="PSA 145:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 145:15"/>All creatures look to you expectantly,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you give them food when they need it.
<verse eid="PSA 145:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 145:16"/>You give generously
</para>
  <para style="q2">and satisfy the desire of every living thing.
<verse eid="PSA 145:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 145:17"/>Yahweh does everything rightly;
</para>
  <para style="q2">indeed, he acts faithfully in all that he does.
<verse eid="PSA 145:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 145:18"/>Yahweh is ready to help everyone who asks him for help
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they do that sincerely.
<verse eid="PSA 145:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 145:19"/>He gives those who deeply respect him what they need.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He responds to them when they call for help,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he rescues them.
<verse eid="PSA 145:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 145:20"/>Yahweh protects all those who love him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he destroys wicked people.
<verse eid="PSA 145:20"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="21" style="v" sid="PSA 145:21"/>I will always say things to praise Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">I want all people always to praise him because he is so holy.

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 145:21"/><verse eid="PSA 145:21"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 145"/>
  <chapter number="146" style="c" sid="PSA 146"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 146:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">I will praise Yahweh with my whole being.
<verse eid="PSA 146:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 146:2"/>I will praise Yahweh for as long as I am alive;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, I will sing to praise my God for the rest of my life.
<verse eid="PSA 146:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 146:3"/>Since no human being can save you,
</para>
  <para style="q2">do not rely on your leaders.
<verse eid="PSA 146:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 146:4"/>When they die, their bodies decay and become soil again.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When that happens, they can no longer carry out their plans.
<verse eid="PSA 146:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 146:5"/>Some people confidently expect Yahweh their God to help them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is the God whom Jacob worshiped.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He does help them, and they have a very good life.
<verse eid="PSA 146:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 146:6"/>He is the one who created the sky and the land.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He also created the oceans and all the creatures that are in them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He always does what he has promised to do.
<verse eid="PSA 146:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 146:7"/>He defends people whom others oppress,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he provides food for people who are hungry.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh frees people who are in prison.
<verse eid="PSA 146:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 146:8"/>Yahweh enables people who are blind to see again;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh helps people who are struggling;
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yahweh loves people who do what is right.
<verse eid="PSA 146:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 146:9"/>Yahweh protects foreigners;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he preserves the property of orphans and widows,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he makes the plans of wicked people fail.
<verse eid="PSA 146:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 146:10"/>Yahweh will be the king forever;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, the God of the people of Jerusalem will always reign.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 146:10"/><verse eid="PSA 146:10"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 146"/>
  <chapter number="147" style="c" sid="PSA 147"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 147:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Singing praises to our God is a good thing to do.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He deserves it, and it makes us happy.
<verse eid="PSA 147:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 147:2"/>Yahweh is rebuilding Jerusalem
</para>
  <para style="q2">and bringing back the Israelites whom our enemies had scattered.
<verse eid="PSA 147:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 147:3"/>He comforts people who are very sad
</para>
  <para style="q2">and heals their pain.
<verse eid="PSA 147:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 147:4"/>He knows how many stars there are,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he has given each one its name.
<verse eid="PSA 147:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 147:5"/>Our Lord is great and very powerful;
</para>
  <para style="q2">no one can measure how much he understands.
<verse eid="PSA 147:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 147:6"/>Yahweh helps humble people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">but he makes wicked people fail in what they want to do.
<verse eid="PSA 147:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 147:7"/>Thank Yahweh, our God, for all he has done for us
</para>
  <para style="q2">as you play the harp and sing to him.
<verse eid="PSA 147:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 147:8"/>He makes the sky form rain clouds
</para>
  <para style="q2">so that they will rain on the earth
</para>
  <para style="q2">and make grass grow on the mountains.
<verse eid="PSA 147:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 147:9"/>He provides food for wild animals.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He even feeds young ravens when they cry out for food.
<verse eid="PSA 147:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 147:10"/>He does not value the strength of a horse
</para>
  <para style="q2">or the speed of a human runner.
<verse eid="PSA 147:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 147:11"/>Instead, Yahweh values people who deeply respect him.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He values people who confidently expect him
</para>
  <para style="q2">to be faithful to his covenant promises.
<verse eid="PSA 147:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 147:12"/>Praise Yahweh our God, you people of Jerusalem
</para>
  <para style="q2">who live on Mount Zion!
<verse eid="PSA 147:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 147:13"/>He has made the defenses of your city strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he has blessed the people who live among you.
<verse eid="PSA 147:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 147:14"/>He keeps your borders safe,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and gives you plenty of wheat to eat.
<verse eid="PSA 147:14"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="15" style="v" sid="PSA 147:15"/>He gives commands about what will happen on the earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and these things happen right away.
<verse eid="PSA 147:15"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="16" style="v" sid="PSA 147:16"/>He makes snow that covers the ground like a white wool blanket,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and he scatters frost on the ground like ashes.
<verse eid="PSA 147:16"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="17" style="v" sid="PSA 147:17"/>He hurls down hail like small stones.
</para>
  <para style="q2">When he makes it cold, no one can stand outside.
<verse eid="PSA 147:17"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="18" style="v" sid="PSA 147:18"/>But then he gives a command, and the snow and ice melt.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He sends a warm wind, and the water flows again.
<verse eid="PSA 147:18"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="19" style="v" sid="PSA 147:19"/>He told the descendants of Jacob how he wanted them to live.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Yes, he gave decrees and laws to the Israelites.
<verse eid="PSA 147:19"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="20" style="v" sid="PSA 147:20"/>He has not done this for any other nation;
</para>
  <para style="q2">they do not know his laws.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 147:20"/><verse eid="PSA 147:20"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 147"/>
  <chapter number="148" style="c" sid="PSA 148"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 148:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">You who are in heaven, praise Yahweh;
</para>
  <para style="q2">yes, you who are in the highest places, praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 148:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 148:2"/>All you angels, praise him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all you heavenly armies, praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 148:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 148:3"/>Sun and moon, praise him;
</para>
  <para style="q2">all you shining stars, praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 148:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 148:4"/>You highest heavens, praise him,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and you waters above the sky, praise him.
<verse eid="PSA 148:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 148:5"/>Let all of these praise Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he created them by his own command.
<verse eid="PSA 148:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 148:6"/>He set them in their places permanently;
</para>
  <para style="q2">{to do that,} he made a decree that will always be in effect.
<verse eid="PSA 148:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 148:7"/>You who are on the earth, praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">You great sea creatures and everything deep in the ocean,
<verse eid="PSA 148:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 148:8"/>lightning and hail, snow and clouds,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and strong winds that obey what he commands,
<verse eid="PSA 148:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 148:9"/>all you mountains and hills,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all you fruit trees and cedar trees,
<verse eid="PSA 148:9"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="10" style="v" sid="PSA 148:10"/>all you wild animals and livestock,
</para>
  <para style="q2">all you creatures that crawl on the ground
</para>
  <para style="q2">and all you birds that fly in the sky,
<verse eid="PSA 148:10"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="11" style="v" sid="PSA 148:11"/>you kings of the earth and all your peoples,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you rulers and all you judges,
<verse eid="PSA 148:11"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="12" style="v" sid="PSA 148:12"/>you young men and young women,
</para>
  <para style="q2">you old people and children,
<verse eid="PSA 148:12"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="13" style="v" sid="PSA 148:13"/>you should all praise Yahweh,
</para>
  <para style="q2">because he alone is truly great.
</para>
  <para style="q2">He is more glorious than everything on earth and in heaven.
<verse eid="PSA 148:13"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="14" style="v" sid="PSA 148:14"/>He has made his people strong,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and other nations respect them.
</para>
  <para style="q1">His people are the Israelite people,
</para>
  <para style="q2">who are close to him.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 148:14"/><verse eid="PSA 148:14"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 148"/>
  <chapter number="149" style="c" sid="PSA 149"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 149:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Sing a new song to Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Let his faithful people praise him when they gather together.
<verse eid="PSA 149:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 149:2"/>You Israelite people, God made you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Be happy because of what he has done for you.
</para>
  <para style="q2">You people of Jerusalem, rejoice because God is your king.
<verse eid="PSA 149:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 149:3"/>Praise Yahweh by dancing.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Play tambourines and harps to honor him.
<verse eid="PSA 149:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 149:4"/>Do that because Yahweh loves his people;
</para>
  <para style="q2">he honors poor people by rescuing them.
<verse eid="PSA 149:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 149:5"/>God’s faithful people should celebrate because he has honored them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">Even on their beds at night, they should praise him with joyful songs.
<verse eid="PSA 149:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 149:6"/>They should also shout loudly to praise God
</para>
  <para style="q2">when they go into battle holding swords that have two sharp edges.
<verse eid="PSA 149:6"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="7" style="v" sid="PSA 149:7"/>{They should be ready} to punish the people of other nations
</para>
  <para style="q2">for the sins they have committed against God.
<verse eid="PSA 149:7"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="8" style="v" sid="PSA 149:8"/>They should bind their kings with chains
</para>
  <para style="q2">and put iron shackles on their leaders.
<verse eid="PSA 149:8"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="9" style="v" sid="PSA 149:9"/>In that way, they will carry out the judgment that God has decreed against them.
</para>
  <para style="q2">God will give his faithful people the honor {of doing that for him}.
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!

<ms style="ts"/>

<verse eid="PSA 149:9"/><verse eid="PSA 149:9"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 149"/>
  <chapter number="150" style="c" sid="PSA 150"/>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="1" style="v" sid="PSA 150:1"/>Praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise God in his temple here on earth,
</para>
  <para style="q2">and praise him in the heavens that he created by his power!
<verse eid="PSA 150:1"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="2" style="v" sid="PSA 150:2"/>Praise him for the mighty things he has done!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise him because he is so very great!
<verse eid="PSA 150:2"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="3" style="v" sid="PSA 150:3"/>Praise him by blowing horns loudly!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise him by playing lyres and harps!
<verse eid="PSA 150:3"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="4" style="v" sid="PSA 150:4"/>Praise him by beating tambourines and by dancing!
</para>
  <para style="q2">Praise him by playing stringed instruments and flutes!
<verse eid="PSA 150:4"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="5" style="v" sid="PSA 150:5"/>Praise him by playing loud cymbals
</para>
  <para style="q2">and cymbals that make high notes!
<verse eid="PSA 150:5"/></para>
  <para style="q1"><verse number="6" style="v" sid="PSA 150:6"/>Let everything that breathes praise Yahweh!
</para>
  <para style="q1">Praise Yahweh!
<verse eid="PSA 150:6"/></para>
  <chapter eid="PSA 150"/>
</usx>
